ession-stream, @ui-agent-dispatch, @ui-session-history, @ui-inbox-enhanced, @ui-plans-view, @ui-validation-view, @ui-dashboard-overview\\n  Tasks: @implement-ui-design-system, @implement-app-shell-and-navigation, @implement-task-board-kanban, @implement-session-stream-view, @implement-agent-and-dispatch-view, @implement-session-history, @implement-enhanced-inbox-view, @implement-plans-view, @implement-validation-and-alignment-view, @implement-dashboard-overview\\n\\n─── Content ───\\n# UI/UX Revamp\\n\\n## Specs\\n\\n```yaml\\n- title: \\\"UI Design System\\\"\\n  slug: ui-design-system\\n  type: feature\\n  parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  description: |\\n    Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n    Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n    keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n    across all views.\\n  acceptance_criteria:\\n    - id: ac-1\\n      given: |\\n        The web UI app.css file\\n      when: |\\n        imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n      then: |\\n        All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\n        are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n    - id: ac-2\\n      given: |\\n        A component using design tokens\\n      when: |\\n        The dark theme tokens are applied\\n      then: |\\n        oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\n        pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\n        are visually distinct\\n    - id: ac-3\\n      given: |\\n        A view with loading states\\n      when: |\\n        Content is loading\\n      then: |\\n        Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n    - id: ac-4\\n      given: |\\n        An active agent task card\\n      when: |\\n        The agent is working\\n      then: |\\n        Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n- title: \\\"App Shell and Navigation\\\"\\n  slug: ui-app-shell\\n  type: feature\\n  parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  description: |\\n    Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\\n    with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\\n    Preserve existing functionality during migration.\\n  acceptance_criteria:\\n    - id: ac-1\\n      given: |\\n        The web UI loaded in daemon mode\\n      when: |\\n        The app shell renders\\n      then: |\\n        A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\\n        Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\\n        Config (Workflows, Settings)\\n    - id: ac-2\\n      given: |\\n        Sidebar navigation items\\n      when: |\\n        Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\\n      then: |\\n        Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\\n    - id: ac-3\\n      given: |\\n        The /items route\\n      when: |\\n        A user navigates to /items\\n      then: |\\n        They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\\n    - id: ac-4\\n      given: |\\n        The Observations nav item\\n      when: |\\n        There are zero unresolved observations\\n      then: |\\n        The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\\n\\n- title: \\\"Task Board (Kanban)\\\"\\n  slug: ui-task-board\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_014q6H8WZaokRfjNoD59v1Gf\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\"}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:38:{\"ts\":1772684311760,\"seq\":37,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_014q6H8WZaokRfjNoD59v1Gf\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"rawOutput\":\"ULID:     01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2\\nTitle:    UI/UX Revamp\\nStatus:   active\\nSlugs:    plan-ui-ux-revamp\\nCreated:  2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z (2 hours ago)\\n\\nDerived Work:\\n  Specs: @ui-design-system, @ui-app-shell, @ui-task-board, @ui-session-stream, @ui-agent-dispatch, @ui-session-history, @ui-inbox-enhanced, @ui-plans-view, @ui-validation-view, @ui-dashboard-overview\\n  Tasks: @implement-ui-design-system, @implement-app-shell-and-navigation, @implement-task-board-kanban, @implement-session-stream-view, @implement-agent-and-dispatch-view, @implement-session-history, @implement-enhanced-inbox-view, @implement-plans-view, @implement-validation-and-alignment-view, @implement-dashboard-overview\\n\\n─── Content ───\\n# UI/UX Revamp\\n\\n## Specs\\n\\n```yaml\\n- title: \\\"UI Design System\\\"\\n  slug: ui-design-system\\n  type: feature\\n  parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  description: |\\n    Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n    Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n    keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n    across all views.\\n  acceptance_criteria:\\n    - id: ac-1\\n      given: |\\n        The web UI app.css file\\n      when: |\\n        imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n      then: |\\n        All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\n        are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n    - id: ac-2\\n      given: |\\n        A component using design tokens\\n      when: |\\n        The dark theme tokens are applied\\n      then: |\\n        oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\n        pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\n        are visually distinct\\n    - id: ac-3\\n      given: |\\n        A view with loading states\\n      when: |\\n        Content is loading\\n      then: |\\n        Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n    - id: ac-4\\n      given: |\\n        An active agent task card\\n      when: |\\n        The agent is working\\n      then: |\\n        Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n- title: \\\"App Shell and Navigation\\\"\\n  slug: ui-app-shell\\n  type: feature\\n  parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  description: |\\n    Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\\n    with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\\n    Preserve existing functionality during migration.\\n  acceptance_criteria:\\n    - id: ac-1\\n      given: |\\n        The web UI loaded in daemon mode\\n      when: |\\n        The app shell renders\\n      then: |\\n        A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\\n        Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\\n        Config (Workflows, Settings)\\n    - id: ac-2\\n      given: |\\n        Sidebar navigation items\\n      when: |\\n        Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\\n      then: |\\n        Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\\n    - id: ac-3\\n      given: |\\n        The /items route\\n      when: |\\n        A user navigates to /items\\n      then: |\\n        They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\\n    - id: ac-4\\n      given: |\\n        The Observations nav item\\n      when: |\\n        There are zero unresolved observations\\n      then: |\\n        The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\\n\\n- title: \\\"Task Board (Kanban)\\\"\\n  slug: ui-task-board\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"```console\\nULID:     01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2\\nTitle:    UI/UX Revamp\\nStatus:   active\\nSlugs:    plan-ui-ux-revamp\\nCreated:  2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z (2 hours ago)\\n\\nDerived Work:\\n  Specs: @ui-design-system, @ui-app-shell, @ui-task-board, @ui-session-stream, @ui-agent-dispatch, @ui-session-history, @ui-inbox-enhanced, @ui-plans-view, @ui-validation-view, @ui-dashboard-overview\\n  Tasks: @implement-ui-design-system, @implement-app-shell-and-navigation, @implement-task-board-kanban, @implement-session-stream-view, @implement-agent-and-dispatch-view, @implement-session-history, @implement-enhanced-inbox-view, @implement-plans-view, @implement-validation-and-alignment-view, @implement-dashboard-overview\\n\\n─── Content ───\\n# UI/UX Revamp\\n\\n## Specs\\n\\n```yaml\\n- title: \\\"UI Design System\\\"\\n  slug: ui-design-system\\n  type: feature\\n  parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  description: |\\n    Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n    Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n    keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n    across all views.\\n  acceptance_criteria:\\n    - id: ac-1\\n      given: |\\n        The web UI app.css file\\n      when: |\\n        imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n      then: |\\n        All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\n        are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n    - id: ac-2\\n      given: |\\n        A component using design tokens\\n      when: |\\n        The dark theme tokens are applied\\n      then: |\\n        oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\n        pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\n        are visually distinct\\n    - id: ac-3\\n      given: |\\n        A view with loading states\\n      when: |\\n        Content is loading\\n      then: |\\n        Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n    - id: ac-4\\n      given: |\\n        An active agent task card\\n      when: |\\n        The agent is working\\n      then: |\\n        Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n- title: \\\"App Shell and Navigation\\\"\\n  slug: ui-app-shell\\n  type: feature\\n  parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  description: |\\n    Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\\n    with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\\n    Preserve existing functionality during migration.\\n  acceptance_criteria:\\n    - id: ac-1\\n      given: |\\n        The web UI loaded in daemon mode\\n      when: |\\n        The app shell renders\\n      then: |\\n        A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\\n        Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\\n        Config (Workflows, Settings)\\n    - id: ac-2\\n      given: |\\n        Sidebar navigation items\\n      when: |\\n        Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\\n      then: |\\n        Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\\n    - id: ac-3\\n      given: |\\n        The /items route\\n      when: |\\n        A user navigates to /items\\n      then: |\\n        They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\\n    - id: ac-4\\n      given: |\\n        The Observations nav item\\n      when: |\\n        There are zero unresolved observations\\n      then: |\\n        The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\\n\\n- title: \\\"Task Board (Kanban)\\\"\\n  slug: ui-task-board\\n```\"}}]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:109:{\"ts\":1772684326582,\"seq\":108,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Task\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01ThiD6dTsa1F73oouG6F7np\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"rawInput\":{\"subagent_type\":\"Explore\",\"description\":\"Read UI revamp plan\",\"prompt\":\"Read the file .kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-plan.md completely. I need the full architectural context and wireframes for the UI revamp plan, especially any details about the design system, token architecture, and component structure.\"},\"title\":\"Read UI revamp plan\",\"kind\":\"think\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read the file .kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-plan.md completely. I need the full architectural context and wireframes for the UI revamp plan, especially any details about the design system, token architecture, and component structure.\"}}]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:200:{\"ts\":1772684336855,\"seq\":199,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolResponse\":{\"mode\":\"content\",\"numFiles\":0,\"filenames\":[],\"content\":\"7613:      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\\n8069:    source_path: /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-import.md\",\"numLines\":2},\"toolName\":\"Grep\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_019g3pjHBNS1tQxvqaKtgStB\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\"}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:201:{\"ts\":1772684336855,\"seq\":200,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Grep\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_019g3pjHBNS1tQxvqaKtgStB\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"rawOutput\":\"7613:      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\\n8069:    source_path: /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-import.md\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"7613:      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\\n8069:    source_path: /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-import.md\"}}]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:207:{\"ts\":1772684338103,\"seq\":206,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01NJVDyrz6B8SgqxpHvx8aMj\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call\",\"rawInput\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"plan-ui-ux-revamp\\\\|plan_ui_ux_revamp\\\" /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml | head -5\"},\"status\":\"pending\",\"title\":\"grep -n \\\"plan-ui-ux-revamp\\\\|plan_ui_ux_revamp\\\" /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml | head -5\",\"kind\":\"execute\",\"content\":[]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:208:{\"ts\":1772684338280,\"seq\":207,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolResponse\":{\"stdout\":\"7613:      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01NJVDyrz6B8SgqxpHvx8aMj\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\"}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:209:{\"ts\":1772684338282,\"seq\":208,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01NJVDyrz6B8SgqxpHvx8aMj\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"rawOutput\":\"7613:      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"```console\\n7613:      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\\n```\"}}]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:220:{\"ts\":1772684339375,\"seq\":219,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolResponse\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml\",\"content\":\"    created_at: 2026-03-04T21:54:25.649Z\\n    approved_at: null\\n    completed_at: null\\n    notes:\\n      - _ulid: 01KJXDJAQZ6BF9RK02TYSEARZ0\\n        created_at: 2026-03-04T21:55:20.447Z\\n        author: \\\"@claude\\\"\\n        content: \\\"Plan details: Add review_url field to task schema + dispatch prompt orientation context\\n          (task title, trigger meaning, fix-cycle notes, review URL, template interpolation). Spec\\n          ACs added to @task-submit (ac-submit-1 through ac-submit-3) and @agent-dispatch-engine\\n          (ac-13 through ac-16). Full plan at ~/.claude/plans/resilient-wiggling-token.md\\\"\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2\\n    slugs:\\n      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\\n    title: UI/UX Revamp\\n    content: >\\n      # UI/UX Revamp\\n\\n\\n      ## Specs\\n\\n\\n      ```yaml\\n\\n      - title: \\\"UI Design System\\\"\\n        slug: ui-design-system\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n          Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n          keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n          across all views.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              The web UI app.css file\\n            when: |\\n              imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n            then: |\\n              All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\n              are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              A component using design tokens\\n            when: |\\n              The dark theme tokens are applied\\n            then: |\\n              oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\n              pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\n              are visually distinct\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: |\\n              A view with loading states\\n            when: |\\n              Content is loading\\n            then: |\\n              Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n          - id: ac-4\\n            given: |\\n              An active agent task card\\n            when: |\\n              The agent is working\\n            then: |\\n              Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n      - title: \\\"App Shell and Navigation\\\"\\n        slug: ui-app-shell\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\\n          with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\\n          Preserve existing functionality during migration.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              The web UI loaded in daemon mode\\n            when: |\\n              The app shell renders\\n            then: |\\n              A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\\n              Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\\n              Config (Workflows, Settings)\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              Sidebar navigation items\\n            when: |\\n              Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\\n            then: |\\n              Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: |\\n              The /items route\\n            when: |\\n              A user navigates to /items\\n            then: |\\n              They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\\n          - id: ac-4\\n            given: |\\n              The Observations nav item\\n            when: |\\n              There are zero unresolved observations\\n            then: |\\n              The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Task Board (Kanban)\\\"\\n        slug: ui-task-board\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          Kanban-style task board with columns mapping to kspec task states.\\n          Active Fleet row shows currently running agent work with live output.\\n          Task cards show key metadata, clicking opens detail modal.\\n          Not drag-and-drop — tasks transition via agents/CLI.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              Tasks in various states\\n            when: |\\n              The task board renders\\n            then: |\\n              Tasks are distributed into columns: Backlog (pending, manual_only/unassessed),\\n              Ready (pending, eligible), In Progress (in_progress, needs_work),\\n              Review (pending_review), Done (completed recent), with blocked and cancelled\\n              handled as sections/indicators\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              A task card on the board\\n            when: |\\n              The card renders\\n            then: |\\n              It shows priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (mono), spec ref link,\\n              and metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: |\\n              A task card\\n            when: |\\n              The user clicks it\\n            then: |\\n              A detail modal opens showing full task info: title, description, status,\\n              priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos,\\n              automation status, VCS info (branch, PR link), plan ref, session link\\n          - id: ac-4\\n            given: |\\n              Agents actively working on tasks (dispatch running)\\n            when: |\\n              The task board renders\\n            then: |\\n              An Active Fleet row appears at the top showing cards with task title,\\n              agent name, elapsed time with pulse indicator, and last few lines of output\\n          - id: ac-5\\n            given: |\\n              The task board with WebSocket connected\\n            when: |\\n              A task state changes\\n            then: |\\n              The board updates in real-time without page refresh\\n          - id: ac-6\\n            given: |\\n              The task detail modal in daemon mode\\n            when: |\\n              The user clicks action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note)\\n            then: |\\n              The corresponding task transition or mutation is executed via API\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Session Stream View\\\"\\n        slug: ui-session-stream\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          View for watching agent work — both historical and live. Renders structured\\n          session events (messages, tool calls, thinking blocks) from events.jsonl.\\n          Live sessions show streaming text with periodic structured refresh.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              A completed session with events.jsonl\\n            when: |\\n              The user navigates to /sessions/:id\\n            then: |\\n              The session events render as structured blocks: agent messages (markdown),\\n              tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), and thinking blocks\\n              (collapsed by default, expandable)\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              An active session with streaming output\\n            when: |\\n              The user views the session\\n            then: |\\n              Live text streams in real-time via agent_text_chunk WebSocket events,\\n              with periodic structured refresh from events.jsonl\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: |\\n              The session stream view\\n            when: |\\n              New content arrives while auto-scrolling\\n            then: |\\n              The view auto-scrolls to follow new content, pauses when user scrolls up\\n              (>100px from bottom), and resumes when scrolled back. A \\\"jump to bottom\\\"\\n              button appears when paused.\\n          - id: ac-4\\n            given: |\\n              The session stream view\\n            when: |\\n              A session context panel is shown on the left\\n            then: |\\n              It displays session metadata, spec context with AC checklist,\\n              files changed during session, and budget info\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Agent and Dispatch View\\\"\\n        slug: ui-agent-dispatch\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          View showing agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped),\\n          and active invocations with links to session streams.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              The /agents route\\n            when: |\\n              Agent definitions exist in meta\\n            then: |\\n              Each agent shows name, triggers, active invocation count, and completed count\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              The dispatch engine is running\\n            when: |\\n              The agents page renders\\n            then: |\\n              Dispatch status shows as running with a stop button, and active invocations\\n              show task ref, elapsed time, and link to session stream\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: |\\n              The dispatch engine is stopped\\n            when: |\\n              The agents page renders\\n            then: |\\n              Dispatch status shows as stopped with no active invocations\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Session History\\\"\\n        slug: ui-session-history\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          List view of past agent sessions with filtering and navigation to session detail.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              Sessions exist on disk\\n            when: |\\n              The user navigates to /sessions\\n            then: |\\n              A list of sessions shows ID, agent type, task ref, status,\\n              duration, and age, sorted by most recent first\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              The session list\\n            when: |\\n              The user clicks a session\\n            then: |\\n              They navigate to /sessions/:id showing the session stream view\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Enhanced Inbox View\\\"\\n        slug: ui-inbox-enhanced\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          Enhanced inbox with triage status inline, quick actions, filtering, and bulk selection.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              Inbox items with varying triage states\\n            when: |\\n              The inbox view renders\\n            then: |\\n              Each item shows triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n              with quick triage action links\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              The inbox view\\n            when: |\\n              The user applies filters (status, tags, age)\\n            then: |\\n              The list filters accordingly\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Plans View\\\"\\n        slug: ui-plans-view\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          View for browsing plan records with progress tracking via linked specs and tasks.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              Plan records exist\\n            when: |\\n              The user navigates to /plans\\n            then: |\\n              Each plan shows title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts,\\n              and progress based on task completion status\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Validation and Alignment View\\\"\\n        slug: ui-validation-view\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          View showing validation results, alignment statistics, and issues.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              The user navigates to /validate\\n            when: |\\n              Validation data loads\\n            then: |\\n              Summary shows error count, warning count, valid item count.\\n              Alignment section shows spec coverage %, AC coverage %,\\n              orphaned tasks/specs counts. Issues list grouped by severity.\\n\\n      - title: \\\"Dashboard Overview\\\"\\n        slug: ui-dashboard-overview\\n        type: feature\\n        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n        description: |\\n          Home view answering \\\"what's happening right now?\\\" with active work,\\n          status summary, recent activity, and needs-attention aggregation.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              The user navigates to /\\n            when: |\\n              The dashboard renders\\n            then: |\\n              Active work section shows currently running agent tasks (if any),\\n              status summary shows clickable count cards per status,\\n              needs-attention section aggregates untriaged inbox, unresolved observations,\\n              validation warnings, and blocked tasks\\n      ```\\n\\n\\n      ## Tasks\\n\\n\\n      derive_from_specs: true\\n\\n\\n      ### Implementation Notes\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-design-system\\n\\n      Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\\n\\n      Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\\n\\n      dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\\n\\n      tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\\n\\n      skeleton and error boundary patterns.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-app-shell\\n\\n      Restructure +layout.svelte with new sidebar component. Migrate existing\\n\\n      Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation. Add /items -> /specs redirect.\\n\\n      Fix Observations nav visibility bug. Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4\\n\\n      to Svelte 5 runes. Consolidate three existing task detail implementations.\\n\\n      Ensure all existing routes still work.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-task-board\\n\\n      Prerequisite: daemon must return type and automation in task list API response\\n\\n      (quick fix to packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts). Add needs_work to status\\n\\n      color/label maps. Build KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal,\\n\\n      ActiveFleetRow components. Wire to tasks:updates WebSocket topic. Build task\\n\\n      mutation endpoints in daemon (submit, complete, block) for detail modal actions.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-session-stream\\n\\n      Prerequisite: build GET /api/sessions and GET /api/sessions/:id/events daemon\\n\\n      endpoints. Two-tier rendering: structured events from events.jsonl for history,\\n\\n      agent_text_chunk WS for live text. Build SessionStream, ChatMessage,\\n\\n      ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock components. Implement auto-scroll with pause/resume.\\n\\n      Port patterns from kynetic-internal's ChatPanel.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-agent-dispatch\\n\\n      Uses existing GET /api/agent/dispatch/status and GET /api/agent/status endpoints.\\n\\n      Subscribe to agents WS topic for real-time updates. Build AgentList,\\n\\n      DispatchStatus, InvocationCard components.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-session-history\\n\\n      Depends on GET /api/sessions endpoint from ui-session-stream work.\\n\\n      Build SessionList with filtering. Link to session stream view.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-inbox-enhanced\\n\\n      Enhance existing inbox view. Add triage status from existing triage API.\\n\\n      Add filter controls. Keep existing add/delete functionality.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-plans-view\\n\\n      Prerequisite: build GET /api/plans daemon endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans).\\n\\n      Build PlanList with progress calculation from linked task statuses.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-validation-view\\n\\n      Uses existing GET /api/validate and GET /api/alignment endpoints.\\n\\n      Build ValidationSummary, AlignmentStats, IssueList components.\\n\\n\\n      #### ui-dashboard-overview\\n\\n      Build last. Uses data from tasks, inbox, observations, validation APIs.\\n\\n      Active work section reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board.\\n\\n      No aggregated activity API needed — merge recent data client-side.\\n    status: active\\n    derived_tasks:\\n      - \\\"@implement-ui-design-system\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-app-shell-and-navigation\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-task-board-kanban\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-session-stream-view\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-agent-and-dispatch-view\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-session-history\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-enhanced-inbox-view\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-plans-view\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-validation-and-alignment-view\\\"\\n      - \\\"@implement-dashboard-overview\\\"\\n    derived_specs:\\n      - \\\"@ui-design-system\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-app-shell\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-task-board\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-session-stream\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-agent-dispatch\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-session-history\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-inbox-enhanced\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-plans-view\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-validation-view\\\"\\n      - \\\"@ui-dashboard-overview\\\"\\n    source_path: /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-import.md\\n    created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\\n    approved_at: null\\n    completed_at: null\\n    notes:\\n      - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YDSBAM76XMSQHBCFX\\n        created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\\n        author: \\\"@claude\\\"\\n        content: |-\\n          Implementation notes:\\n\\n          #### ui-design-system\\n          Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\\n          Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\\n          dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\\n          tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\\n          skeleton and error boundary patterns.\\n\\n          #### ui-app-shell\\n          Restructure +layout.svelte with new sidebar component. Migrate existing\\n          Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation. Add /items -> /specs redirect.\\n          Fix Observations nav visibility bug. Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4\\n          to Svelte 5 runes. Consolidate three existing task detail implementations.\\n          Ensure all existing routes still work.\\n\\n          #### ui-task-board\\n          Prerequisite: daemon must return type and automation in task list API response\\n          (quick fix to packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts). Add needs_work to status\\n          color/label maps. Build KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal,\\n          ActiveFleetRow components. Wire to tasks:updates WebSocket topic. Build task\\n          mutation endpoints in daemon (submit, complete, block) for detail modal actions.\",\"numLines\":500,\"startLine\":7600,\"totalLines\":8133}},\"toolName\":\"Read\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01XtKFDrNvwd7srEJhTGmvDu\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\"}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:221:{\"ts\":1772684339384,\"seq\":220,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Read\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01XtKFDrNvwd7srEJhTGmvDu\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"rawOutput\":\"  7600→    created_at: 2026-03-04T21:54:25.649Z\\n  7601→    approved_at: null\\n  7602→    completed_at: null\\n  7603→    notes:\\n  7604→      - _ulid: 01KJXDJAQZ6BF9RK02TYSEARZ0\\n  7605→        created_at: 2026-03-04T21:55:20.447Z\\n  7606→        author: \\\"@claude\\\"\\n  7607→        content: \\\"Plan details: Add review_url field to task schema + dispatch prompt orientation context\\n  7608→          (task title, trigger meaning, fix-cycle notes, review URL, template interpolation). Spec\\n  7609→          ACs added to @task-submit (ac-submit-1 through ac-submit-3) and @agent-dispatch-engine\\n  7610→          (ac-13 through ac-16). Full plan at ~/.claude/plans/resilient-wiggling-token.md\\\"\\n  7611→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2\\n  7612→    slugs:\\n  7613→      - plan-ui-ux-revamp\\n  7614→    title: UI/UX Revamp\\n  7615→    content: >\\n  7616→      # UI/UX Revamp\\n  7617→\\n  7618→\\n  7619→      ## Specs\\n  7620→\\n  7621→\\n  7622→      ```yaml\\n  7623→\\n  7624→      - title: \\\"UI Design System\\\"\\n  7625→        slug: ui-design-system\\n  7626→        type: feature\\n  7627→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7628→        description: |\\n  7629→          Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n  7630→          Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n  7631→          keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n  7632→          across all views.\\n  7633→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7634→          - id: ac-1\\n  7635→            given: |\\n  7636→              The web UI app.css file\\n  7637→            when: |\\n  7638→              imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n  7639→            then: |\\n  7640→              All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\n  7641→              are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n  7642→          - id: ac-2\\n  7643→            given: |\\n  7644→              A component using design tokens\\n  7645→            when: |\\n  7646→              The dark theme tokens are applied\\n  7647→            then: |\\n  7648→              oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\n  7649→              pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\n  7650→              are visually distinct\\n  7651→          - id: ac-3\\n  7652→            given: |\\n  7653→              A view with loading states\\n  7654→            when: |\\n  7655→              Content is loading\\n  7656→            then: |\\n  7657→              Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n  7658→          - id: ac-4\\n  7659→            given: |\\n  7660→              An active agent task card\\n  7661→            when: |\\n  7662→              The agent is working\\n  7663→            then: |\\n  7664→              Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n  7665→\\n  7666→      - title: \\\"App Shell and Navigation\\\"\\n  7667→        slug: ui-app-shell\\n  7668→        type: feature\\n  7669→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7670→        description: |\\n  7671→          Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\\n  7672→          with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\\n  7673→          Preserve existing functionality during migration.\\n  7674→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7675→          - id: ac-1\\n  7676→            given: |\\n  7677→              The web UI loaded in daemon mode\\n  7678→            when: |\\n  7679→              The app shell renders\\n  7680→            then: |\\n  7681→              A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\\n  7682→              Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\\n  7683→              Config (Workflows, Settings)\\n  7684→          - id: ac-2\\n  7685→            given: |\\n  7686→              Sidebar navigation items\\n  7687→            when: |\\n  7688→              Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\\n  7689→            then: |\\n  7690→              Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\\n  7691→          - id: ac-3\\n  7692→            given: |\\n  7693→              The /items route\\n  7694→            when: |\\n  7695→              A user navigates to /items\\n  7696→            then: |\\n  7697→              They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\\n  7698→          - id: ac-4\\n  7699→            given: |\\n  7700→              The Observations nav item\\n  7701→            when: |\\n  7702→              There are zero unresolved observations\\n  7703→            then: |\\n  7704→              The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\\n  7705→\\n  7706→      - title: \\\"Task Board (Kanban)\\\"\\n  7707→        slug: ui-task-board\\n  7708→        type: feature\\n  7709→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7710→        description: |\\n  7711→          Kanban-style task board with columns mapping to kspec task states.\\n  7712→          Active Fleet row shows currently running agent work with live output.\\n  7713→          Task cards show key metadata, clicking opens detail modal.\\n  7714→          Not drag-and-drop — tasks transition via agents/CLI.\\n  7715→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7716→          - id: ac-1\\n  7717→            given: |\\n  7718→              Tasks in various states\\n  7719→            when: |\\n  7720→              The task board renders\\n  7721→            then: |\\n  7722→              Tasks are distributed into columns: Backlog (pending, manual_only/unassessed),\\n  7723→              Ready (pending, eligible), In Progress (in_progress, needs_work),\\n  7724→              Review (pending_review), Done (completed recent), with blocked and cancelled\\n  7725→              handled as sections/indicators\\n  7726→          - id: ac-2\\n  7727→            given: |\\n  7728→              A task card on the board\\n  7729→            when: |\\n  7730→              The card renders\\n  7731→            then: |\\n  7732→              It shows priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (mono), spec ref link,\\n  7733→              and metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n  7734→          - id: ac-3\\n  7735→            given: |\\n  7736→              A task card\\n  7737→            when: |\\n  7738→              The user clicks it\\n  7739→            then: |\\n  7740→              A detail modal opens showing full task info: title, description, status,\\n  7741→              priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos,\\n  7742→              automation status, VCS info (branch, PR link), plan ref, session link\\n  7743→          - id: ac-4\\n  7744→            given: |\\n  7745→              Agents actively working on tasks (dispatch running)\\n  7746→            when: |\\n  7747→              The task board renders\\n  7748→            then: |\\n  7749→              An Active Fleet row appears at the top showing cards with task title,\\n  7750→              agent name, elapsed time with pulse indicator, and last few lines of output\\n  7751→          - id: ac-5\\n  7752→            given: |\\n  7753→              The task board with WebSocket connected\\n  7754→            when: |\\n  7755→              A task state changes\\n  7756→            then: |\\n  7757→              The board updates in real-time without page refresh\\n  7758→          - id: ac-6\\n  7759→            given: |\\n  7760→              The task detail modal in daemon mode\\n  7761→            when: |\\n  7762→              The user clicks action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note)\\n  7763→            then: |\\n  7764→              The corresponding task transition or mutation is executed via API\\n  7765→\\n  7766→      - title: \\\"Session Stream View\\\"\\n  7767→        slug: ui-session-stream\\n  7768→        type: feature\\n  7769→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7770→        description: |\\n  7771→          View for watching agent work — both historical and live. Renders structured\\n  7772→          session events (messages, tool calls, thinking blocks) from events.jsonl.\\n  7773→          Live sessions show streaming text with periodic structured refresh.\\n  7774→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7775→          - id: ac-1\\n  7776→            given: |\\n  7777→              A completed session with events.jsonl\\n  7778→            when: |\\n  7779→              The user navigates to /sessions/:id\\n  7780→            then: |\\n  7781→              The session events render as structured blocks: agent messages (markdown),\\n  7782→              tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), and thinking blocks\\n  7783→              (collapsed by default, expandable)\\n  7784→          - id: ac-2\\n  7785→            given: |\\n  7786→              An active session with streaming output\\n  7787→            when: |\\n  7788→              The user views the session\\n  7789→            then: |\\n  7790→              Live text streams in real-time via agent_text_chunk WebSocket events,\\n  7791→              with periodic structured refresh from events.jsonl\\n  7792→          - id: ac-3\\n  7793→            given: |\\n  7794→              The session stream view\\n  7795→            when: |\\n  7796→              New content arrives while auto-scrolling\\n  7797→            then: |\\n  7798→              The view auto-scrolls to follow new content, pauses when user scrolls up\\n  7799→              (>100px from bottom), and resumes when scrolled back. A \\\"jump to bottom\\\"\\n  7800→              button appears when paused.\\n  7801→          - id: ac-4\\n  7802→            given: |\\n  7803→              The session stream view\\n  7804→            when: |\\n  7805→              A session context panel is shown on the left\\n  7806→            then: |\\n  7807→              It displays session metadata, spec context with AC checklist,\\n  7808→              files changed during session, and budget info\\n  7809→\\n  7810→      - title: \\\"Agent and Dispatch View\\\"\\n  7811→        slug: ui-agent-dispatch\\n  7812→        type: feature\\n  7813→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7814→        description: |\\n  7815→          View showing agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped),\\n  7816→          and active invocations with links to session streams.\\n  7817→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7818→          - id: ac-1\\n  7819→            given: |\\n  7820→              The /agents route\\n  7821→            when: |\\n  7822→              Agent definitions exist in meta\\n  7823→            then: |\\n  7824→              Each agent shows name, triggers, active invocation count, and completed count\\n  7825→          - id: ac-2\\n  7826→            given: |\\n  7827→              The dispatch engine is running\\n  7828→            when: |\\n  7829→              The agents page renders\\n  7830→            then: |\\n  7831→              Dispatch status shows as running with a stop button, and active invocations\\n  7832→              show task ref, elapsed time, and link to session stream\\n  7833→          - id: ac-3\\n  7834→            given: |\\n  7835→              The dispatch engine is stopped\\n  7836→            when: |\\n  7837→              The agents page renders\\n  7838→            then: |\\n  7839→              Dispatch status shows as stopped with no active invocations\\n  7840→\\n  7841→      - title: \\\"Session History\\\"\\n  7842→        slug: ui-session-history\\n  7843→        type: feature\\n  7844→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7845→        description: |\\n  7846→          List view of past agent sessions with filtering and navigation to session detail.\\n  7847→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7848→          - id: ac-1\\n  7849→            given: |\\n  7850→              Sessions exist on disk\\n  7851→            when: |\\n  7852→              The user navigates to /sessions\\n  7853→            then: |\\n  7854→              A list of sessions shows ID, agent type, task ref, status,\\n  7855→              duration, and age, sorted by most recent first\\n  7856→          - id: ac-2\\n  7857→            given: |\\n  7858→              The session list\\n  7859→            when: |\\n  7860→              The user clicks a session\\n  7861→            then: |\\n  7862→              They navigate to /sessions/:id showing the session stream view\\n  7863→\\n  7864→      - title: \\\"Enhanced Inbox View\\\"\\n  7865→        slug: ui-inbox-enhanced\\n  7866→        type: feature\\n  7867→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7868→        description: |\\n  7869→          Enhanced inbox with triage status inline, quick actions, filtering, and bulk selection.\\n  7870→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7871→          - id: ac-1\\n  7872→            given: |\\n  7873→              Inbox items with varying triage states\\n  7874→            when: |\\n  7875→              The inbox view renders\\n  7876→            then: |\\n  7877→              Each item shows triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n  7878→              with quick triage action links\\n  7879→          - id: ac-2\\n  7880→            given: |\\n  7881→              The inbox view\\n  7882→            when: |\\n  7883→              The user applies filters (status, tags, age)\\n  7884→            then: |\\n  7885→              The list filters accordingly\\n  7886→\\n  7887→      - title: \\\"Plans View\\\"\\n  7888→        slug: ui-plans-view\\n  7889→        type: feature\\n  7890→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7891→        description: |\\n  7892→          View for browsing plan records with progress tracking via linked specs and tasks.\\n  7893→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7894→          - id: ac-1\\n  7895→            given: |\\n  7896→              Plan records exist\\n  7897→            when: |\\n  7898→              The user navigates to /plans\\n  7899→            then: |\\n  7900→              Each plan shows title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts,\\n  7901→              and progress based on task completion status\\n  7902→\\n  7903→      - title: \\\"Validation and Alignment View\\\"\\n  7904→        slug: ui-validation-view\\n  7905→        type: feature\\n  7906→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7907→        description: |\\n  7908→          View showing validation results, alignment statistics, and issues.\\n  7909→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7910→          - id: ac-1\\n  7911→            given: |\\n  7912→              The user navigates to /validate\\n  7913→            when: |\\n  7914→              Validation data loads\\n  7915→            then: |\\n  7916→              Summary shows error count, warning count, valid item count.\\n  7917→              Alignment section shows spec coverage %, AC coverage %,\\n  7918→              orphaned tasks/specs counts. Issues list grouped by severity.\\n  7919→\\n  7920→      - title: \\\"Dashboard Overview\\\"\\n  7921→        slug: ui-dashboard-overview\\n  7922→        type: feature\\n  7923→        parent: \\\"@web-ui\\\"\\n  7924→        description: |\\n  7925→          Home view answering \\\"what's happening right now?\\\" with active work,\\n  7926→          status summary, recent activity, and needs-attention aggregation.\\n  7927→        acceptance_criteria:\\n  7928→          - id: ac-1\\n  7929→            given: |\\n  7930→              The user navigates to /\\n  7931→            when: |\\n  7932→              The dashboard renders\\n  7933→            then: |\\n  7934→              Active work section shows currently running agent tasks (if any),\\n  7935→              status summary shows clickable count cards per status,\\n  7936→              needs-attention section aggregates untriaged inbox, unresolved observations,\\n  7937→              validation warnings, and blocked tasks\\n  7938→      ```\\n  7939→\\n  7940→\\n  7941→      ## Tasks\\n  7942→\\n  7943→\\n  7944→      derive_from_specs: true\\n  7945→\\n  7946→\\n  7947→      ### Implementation Notes\\n  7948→\\n  7949→\\n  7950→      #### ui-design-system\\n  7951→\\n  7952→      Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\\n  7953→\\n  7954→      Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\\n  7955→\\n  7956→      dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\\n  7957→\\n  7958→      tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\\n  7959→\\n  7960→      skeleton and error boundary patterns.\\n  7961→\\n  7962→\\n  7963→      #### ui-app-shell\\n  7964→\\n  7965→      Restructure +layout.svelte with new sidebar component. Migrate existing\\n  7966→\\n  7967→      Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation. Add /items -> /specs redirect.\\n  7968→\\n  7969→      Fix Observations nav visibility bug. Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4\\n  7970→\\n  7971→      to Svelte 5 runes. Consolidate three existing task detail implementations.\\n  7972→\\n  7973→      Ensure all existing routes still work.\\n  7974→\\n  7975→\\n  7976→      #### ui-task-board\\n  7977→\\n  7978→      Prerequisite: daemon must return type and automation in task list API response\\n  7979→\\n  7980→      (quick fix to packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts). Add needs_work to status\\n  7981→\\n  7982→      color/label maps. Build KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal,\\n  7983→\\n  7984→      ActiveFleetRow components. Wire to tasks:updates WebSocket topic. Build task\\n  7985→\\n  7986→      mutation endpoints in daemon (submit, complete, block) for detail modal actions.\\n  7987→\\n  7988→\\n  7989→      #### ui-session-stream\\n  7990→\\n  7991→      Prerequisite: build GET /api/sessions and GET /api/sessions/:id/events daemon\\n  7992→\\n  7993→      endpoints. Two-tier rendering: structured events from events.jsonl for history,\\n  7994→\\n  7995→      agent_text_chunk WS for live text. Build SessionStream, ChatMessage,\\n  7996→\\n  7997→      ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock components. Implement auto-scroll with pause/resume.\\n  7998→\\n  7999→      Port patterns from kynetic-internal's ChatPanel.\\n  8000→\\n  8001→\\n  8002→      #### ui-agent-dispatch\\n  8003→\\n  8004→      Uses existing GET /api/agent/dispatch/status and GET /api/agent/status endpoints.\\n  8005→\\n  8006→      Subscribe to agents WS topic for real-time updates. Build AgentList,\\n  8007→\\n  8008→      DispatchStatus, InvocationCard components.\\n  8009→\\n  8010→\\n  8011→      #### ui-session-history\\n  8012→\\n  8013→      Depends on GET /api/sessions endpoint from ui-session-stream work.\\n  8014→\\n  8015→      Build SessionList with filtering. Link to session stream view.\\n  8016→\\n  8017→\\n  8018→      #### ui-inbox-enhanced\\n  8019→\\n  8020→      Enhance existing inbox view. Add triage status from existing triage API.\\n  8021→\\n  8022→      Add filter controls. Keep existing add/delete functionality.\\n  8023→\\n  8024→\\n  8025→      #### ui-plans-view\\n  8026→\\n  8027→      Prerequisite: build GET /api/plans daemon endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans).\\n  8028→\\n  8029→      Build PlanList with progress calculation from linked task statuses.\\n  8030→\\n  8031→\\n  8032→      #### ui-validation-view\\n  8033→\\n  8034→      Uses existing GET /api/validate and GET /api/alignment endpoints.\\n  8035→\\n  8036→      Build ValidationSummary, AlignmentStats, IssueList components.\\n  8037→\\n  8038→\\n  8039→      #### ui-dashboard-overview\\n  8040→\\n  8041→      Build last. Uses data from tasks, inbox, observations, validation APIs.\\n  8042→\\n  8043→      Active work section reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board.\\n  8044→\\n  8045→      No aggregated activity API needed — merge recent data client-side.\\n  8046→    status: active\\n  8047→    derived_tasks:\\n  8048→      - \\\"@implement-ui-design-system\\\"\\n  8049→      - \\\"@implement-app-shell-and-navigation\\\"\\n  8050→      - \\\"@implement-task-board-kanban\\\"\\n  8051→      - \\\"@implement-session-stream-view\\\"\\n  8052→      - \\\"@implement-agent-and-dispatch-view\\\"\\n  8053→      - \\\"@implement-session-history\\\"\\n  8054→      - \\\"@implement-enhanced-inbox-view\\\"\\n  8055→      - \\\"@implement-plans-view\\\"\\n  8056→      - \\\"@implement-validation-and-alignment-view\\\"\\n  8057→      - \\\"@implement-dashboard-overview\\\"\\n  8058→    derived_specs:\\n  8059→      - \\\"@ui-design-system\\\"\\n  8060→      - \\\"@ui-app-shell\\\"\\n  8061→      - \\\"@ui-task-board\\\"\\n  8062→      - \\\"@ui-session-stream\\\"\\n  8063→      - \\\"@ui-agent-dispatch\\\"\\n  8064→      - \\\"@ui-session-history\\\"\\n  8065→      - \\\"@ui-inbox-enhanced\\\"\\n  8066→      - \\\"@ui-plans-view\\\"\\n  8067→      - \\\"@ui-validation-view\\\"\\n  8068→      - \\\"@ui-dashboard-overview\\\"\\n  8069→    source_path: /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-import.md\\n  8070→    created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\\n  8071→    approved_at: null\\n  8072→    completed_at: null\\n  8073→    notes:\\n  8074→      - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2YDSBAM76XMSQHBCFX\\n  8075→        created_at: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.718Z\\n  8076→        author: \\\"@claude\\\"\\n  8077→        content: |-\\n  8078→          Implementation notes:\\n  8079→\\n  8080→          #### ui-design-system\\n  8081→          Set up the isolated clone first. Port imgen's full token-contract.css into\\n  8082→          Tailwind @theme inline in app.css. Start with the token bridge pilot on the\\n  8083→          dashboard page to validate the approach before touching other views. Create\\n  8084→          tokens.css, animations.css, typography.css in lib/ds/. Establish loading\\n  8085→          skeleton and error boundary patterns.\\n  8086→\\n  8087→          #### ui-app-shell\\n  8088→          Restructure +layout.svelte with new sidebar component. Migrate existing\\n  8089→          Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation. Add /items -> /specs redirect.\\n  8090→          Fix Observations nav visibility bug. Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4\\n  8091→          to Svelte 5 runes. Consolidate three existing task detail implementations.\\n  8092→          Ensure all existing routes still work.\\n  8093→\\n  8094→          #### ui-task-board\\n  8095→          Prerequisite: daemon must return type and automation in task list API response\\n  8096→          (quick fix to packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts). Add needs_work to status\\n  8097→          color/label maps. Build KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal,\\n  8098→          ActiveFleetRow components. Wire to tasks:updates WebSocket topic. Build task\\n  8099→          mutation endpoints in daemon (submit, complete, block) for detail modal actions.\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":{\"path\":\"blobs/000220-content-0-content-text-49ec9946-4d9c-49a6-af82-3ad862b22462.blob\",\"bytes\":23056,\"sha256\":\"1e2adf3ad723957ac9dc0b3d7489c8cfd5158bede16a846f5fb9bbde65a0e795\",\"truncated\":true,\"preview\":\"```\\n  7600→    created_at: 2026-03-04T21:54:25.649Z\\n  7601→    approved_at: null\\n  7602→    completed_at: null\\n  7603→    notes:\\n  7604→      - _ulid: 01KJXDJAQZ6BF9RK02TYSEARZ0\\n  7605→        created_at: 2026-03-04T21:55:20.447Z\\n  7606→        author: \\\"@claude\\\"\\n  7607→        content: \\\"Plan details: Add review_url field to task schema + dispatch prompt orientation context\\n  7608→          (task title, trigger meaning, fix-cycle notes, review URL, template interpolation). Spec\\n  7609→   ...\"}}}]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:253:{\"ts\":1772684343200,\"seq\":252,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolResponse\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/modules/web-ui.yaml\",\"content\":\"_ulid: 01KFHMF5ZS4RD70JBQNGBQJVFY\\nslugs:\\n  - web-ui\\ntitle: Web UI System\\ntype: module\\nstatus:\\n  maturity: draft\\n  implementation: implemented\\ndescription: >\\n  Web-based interface for viewing, editing, and managing kspec state. Includes three deployment\\n  modes:\\n\\n  1. Local daemon mode - Elysia.js server on Bun with WebSocket for real-time updates\\n\\n  2. Web dashboard - SvelteKit + shadcn-svelte for full CRUD operations\\n\\n  3. GitHub Pages export - Static JSON snapshot with read-only SPA for public sharing\\n\\n\\n  Tech stack: Elysia.js, Bun runtime, WebSocket (not SSE), SvelteKit, shadcn-svelte.\\n\\n  Distribution via bun build --compile for portable executables.\\ntags:\\n  - web\\n  - ui\\n  - daemon\\n  - elysia\\n  - bun\\ndepends_on: []\\nimplements: []\\nrelates_to: []\\ntests: []\\ntraits: []\\nnotes: []\\nfeatures:\\n  - _ulid: 01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\\n    slugs:\\n      - daemon-server\\n    title: Daemon Server Mode\\n    type: feature\\n    tags:\\n      - server\\n      - websocket\\n      - elysia\\n    description: >\\n      Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and\\n      WebSocket\\n\\n      for real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and\\n      background\\n\\n      modes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits:\\n      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-error-guidance\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-shadow-commit\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-localhost-security\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:09.314Z\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: kspec is installed\\n        when: user runs 'kspec serve'\\n        then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: daemon is starting\\n        when: server binds to network interface\\n        then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\\n        when: request received\\n        then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\\n        then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\\n      - id: ac-5\\n        given: file watching is active\\n        when: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\\n        then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\\n      - id: ac-6\\n        given: watched file has YAML parse error\\n        when: change detected\\n        then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\\n      - id: ac-7\\n        given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\\n        when: watcher encounters error\\n        then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\\n      - id: ac-8\\n        given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\\n        when: reliability issue detected\\n        then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\\n      - id: ac-9\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\\n        then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\\n      - id: ac-10\\n        given: daemon is running in background\\n        when: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\\n        then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\\n      - id: ac-11\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/health is called\\n        then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\\n      - id: ac-12\\n        given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\\n        when: shutdown signal received\\n        then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\\n      - id: ac-13\\n        given: WebSocket connection established\\n        when: 30 seconds pass without activity\\n        then: server sends ping frame\\n      - id: ac-14\\n        given: ping was sent\\n        when: no pong received within 90 seconds\\n        then: connection closed with code 1001\\n      - id: ac-15\\n        given: Elysia server is configured\\n        when: routes are registered\\n        then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\\n      - id: ac-16\\n        given: daemon code is ready\\n        when: bun build --compile runs\\n        then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\\n      - id: ac-17\\n        given: daemon is running with web UI built\\n        when: browser opens http://localhost:<port>/\\n        then: serves the built web UI assets (SvelteKit static build) as the root route\\n    status:\\n      maturity: draft\\n      implementation: in_progress\\n    features:\\n      - _ulid: 01KJP2768T96S8870BH36ZE76K\\n        slugs:\\n          - daemon-agent-dispatch\\n        title: Daemon Agent Dispatch Integration\\n        type: feature\\n        tags: []\\n        description: |\\n          Agent dispatch API routes in the daemon, enhanced file watcher with\\n          task state diffing for change detection, CLI event emission endpoint,\\n          and WebSocket broadcasts for agent invocation status.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: |\\n              The daemon is running with dispatch enabled\\n            when: |\\n              The file watcher detects a change in project.tasks.yaml\\n            then: |\\n              The watcher parses the new task states, diffs against the\\n              previously cached states, and emits state change events to\\n              the dispatch engine for each detected transition\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: |\\n              A CLI command changes task state (e.g. kspec task start)\\n            when: |\\n              The daemon is running\\n            then: |\\n              The CLI posts a JSON event to POST /api/agent/events containing\\n              task_id, previous_status, new_status, and timestamp\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: |\\n              The daemon receives a state change event matching dispatch rules\\n            when: |\\n              The dispatch engine processes it\\n            then: |\\n              The agent is dispatched and a status event is broadcast on the\\n              agents WebSocket topic\\n          - id: ac-4\\n            given: |\\n              A WebSocket client subscribes to agent status updates\\n            when: |\\n              An agent invocation starts, completes, or fails\\n            then: |\\n              A broadcast event is sent containing session_id, agent_id,\\n              task_id, status, and timestamp\\n          - id: ac-5\\n            given: |\\n              GET /api/agent/status is called\\n            when: |\\n              The dispatch engine is running\\n            then: |\\n              Returns JSON with active invocations array, queue depth number,\\n              dispatch_enabled boolean, and agent_definitions array\\n          - id: ac-6\\n            given: |\\n              POST /api/agent/dispatch is called with action start or stop\\n            when: |\\n              The request is from localhost\\n            then: |\\n              The dispatch engine starts or stops and returns JSON with the\\n              new dispatch_enabled state\\n          - id: ac-7\\n            given: |\\n              The daemon is not running\\n            when: |\\n              A CLI command changes task state\\n            then: |\\n              The event emission POST fails silently with no error to the\\n              user — dispatch requires a running daemon\\n          - id: ac-8\\n            given: The dispatch engine runs an agent invocation\\n            when: The agent produces text output (agent_message_chunk events)\\n            then: The daemon broadcasts each text chunk on the agents WebSocket topic with type\\n              agent_text_chunk, session_id, agent_id, task_id, text, and timestamp\\n        depends_on: []\\n        implements: []\\n        relates_to: []\\n        tests: []\\n        traits:\\n          - \\\"@trait-api-endpoint\\\"\\n          - \\\"@trait-localhost-security\\\"\\n          - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n        notes: []\\n        created: 2026-03-02T01:22:20.058Z\\n        status:\\n          maturity: draft\\n          implementation: implemented\\n    requirements:\\n      - _ulid: 01KJRZWDCC8W2WT0Q3A9CZAAGY\\n        slugs:\\n          - daemon-web-ui-bundle\\n        title: Web UI assets bundled in npm package\\n        type: requirement\\n        tags: []\\n        depends_on: []\\n        implements: []\\n        relates_to: []\\n        tests: []\\n        traits: []\\n        notes: []\\n        created: 2026-03-03T04:39:13.036Z\\n        description: The kspec npm package bundles the pre-built web UI static assets so the daemon can\\n          serve the web UI when installed in any project, without requiring a local web UI build.\\n          The build pipeline copies packages/web-ui/build to dist/web-ui/, and resolveWebUiPath\\n          falls back to that location relative to the daemon module.\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: npm run build is executed\\n            when: build completes\\n            then: packages/web-ui/build output is copied to dist/web-ui/ in the package\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: kspec is installed in a project with no local web UI build\\n            when: daemon starts and resolves web UI path\\n            then: resolveWebUiPath returns the bundled dist/web-ui/ path relative to the daemon module location\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: kspec is installed as an npm package in a non-monorepo project\\n            when: browser opens http://localhost:3456/\\n            then: daemon serves the bundled web UI and returns HTTP 200 with HTML content\\n          - id: ac-4\\n            given: an explicit webUiDir option or WEB_UI_DIR env var or local packages/web-ui/build is present\\n            when: daemon starts\\n            then: the explicit or local path takes precedence over the bundled dist/web-ui/ fallback\\n        status:\\n          maturity: draft\\n          implementation: implemented\\n      - _ulid: 01KJTVMGPNP3HN9B9SRF6MEER7\\n        slugs:\\n          - ws-disconnect-lifecycle-cleanup\\n        title: WebSocket Disconnect Lifecycle Cleanup\\n        type: requirement\\n        tags:\\n          - daemon\\n          - websocket\\n          - reliability\\n        description: Ensure daemon WebSocket disconnect handling is accurate for abnormal closes. Disconnect\\n          events must reliably identify the same session created on connect, remove that session\\n          from in-memory registries, and prevent stale heartbeat/client counts after client\\n          disconnect or process termination.\\n        depends_on: []\\n        implements: []\\n        relates_to: []\\n        tests: []\\n        traits: []\\n        notes: []\\n        created: 2026-03-03T22:03:28.854Z\\n        acceptance_criteria:\\n          - id: ac-1\\n            given: multiple clients are connected and one disconnects\\n            when: GET /api/health is requested\\n            then: the connections field reflects only currently active sessions\\n          - id: ac-3\\n            given: a disconnected session was previously in heartbeat monitoring\\n            when: the next heartbeat interval executes\\n            then: the daemon does not attempt to ping that session and emits no stale heartbeat ping log for it\\n          - id: ac-2\\n            given: a WebSocket client disconnects unexpectedly with close code 1006\\n            when: the daemon close handler runs\\n            then: the session is removed from pubsub connection tracking and the disconnect log includes that\\n              session id rather than undefined\\n        status:\\n          maturity: draft\\n          implementation: implemented\\n  - _ulid: 01KFMM8F5V7H46QYW9MVFYRTHW\\n    slugs:\\n      - api-contract\\n    title: REST and WebSocket API Contract\\n    type: feature\\n    tags:\\n      - api\\n      - rest\\n      - websocket\\n    description: |\\n      REST API contract for HTTP endpoints and WebSocket protocol for real-time communication.\\n      All REST endpoints return JSON with consistent patterns. WebSocket uses topic-based pub/sub\\n      with request_id correlation for command acknowledgment.\\n    depends_on:\\n      - \\\"@daemon-server\\\"\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits:\\n      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-filterable-list\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-error-guidance\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-api-endpoint\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-01-22T07:00:00.000Z\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: request from allowed CORS origin received\\n        then: CORS headers allow the request (origins configured for dev and production)\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/tasks is called\\n        then: returns JSON array of all tasks with status, priority, spec_ref, notes count\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/tasks with status filter (e.g., ?status=pending&status=in_progress)\\n        then: returns only tasks matching filter (supports multi-value)\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/tasks with pagination (?limit=10&offset=20)\\n        then: returns paginated results with {items, total, offset, limit} wrapper\\n      - id: ac-5\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/tasks/:ref is called\\n        then: resolves ref via ReferenceIndex, returns full task with notes, todos, dependencies\\n      - id: ac-6\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: POST /api/tasks/:ref/start is called\\n        then: task transitions to in_progress, WebSocket broadcasts update, returns updated task\\n      - id: ac-7\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: POST /api/tasks/:ref/note with {content} body\\n        then: note appended to task, shadow commit occurs, WebSocket broadcasts update\\n      - id: ac-8\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/items is called\\n        then: returns JSON array of all spec items (modules, features, requirements)\\n      - id: ac-9\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/items with type filter (?type=feature&type=requirement)\\n        then: returns only items matching type filter\\n      - id: ac-10\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/items/:ref is called\\n        then: resolves ref, returns full item with acceptance_criteria, traits, relationships\\n      - id: ac-11\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/items/:ref/tasks is called\\n        then: returns tasks linked to this spec via AlignmentIndex\\n      - id: ac-12\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/inbox is called\\n        then: returns all inbox items ordered by created_at desc\\n      - id: ac-13\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: POST /api/inbox with {text} body\\n        then: creates inbox item, returns with generated ULID\\n      - id: ac-14\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: DELETE /api/inbox/:ref is called\\n        then: removes inbox item, returns success confirmation\\n      - id: ac-15\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/meta/session is called\\n        then: returns current session context (focus, threads, questions)\\n      - id: ac-16\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/meta/agents is called\\n        then: returns all defined agents\\n      - id: ac-17\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/meta/workflows is called\\n        then: returns all defined workflows\\n      - id: ac-18\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/meta/observations with filter (?resolved=false)\\n        then: returns observations matching filter\\n      - id: ac-19\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/search?q=login is called\\n        then: searches across all items using grep/title matching\\n      - id: ac-20\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/validate is called\\n        then: runs full validation, returns ValidationResult\\n      - id: ac-21\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: GET /api/alignment is called\\n        then: returns AlignmentIndex stats and warnings\\n      - id: ac-22\\n        given: API request has invalid ref\\n        when: any endpoint with :ref parameter\\n        then: returns {error, message, suggestion} with 404 status, suggests similar refs if available\\n      - id: ac-23\\n        given: API request has validation error\\n        when: POST/PUT with invalid body\\n        then: returns {error, details:[{field, message}]} with 400 status\\n      - id: ac-24\\n        given: API request causes state transition error\\n        when: POST action violates state machine\\n        then: returns {error, current, valid_transitions} with 409 status\\n      - id: ac-25\\n        given: client connects to /ws\\n        when: WebSocket connection established\\n        then: receives connected event with {session_id}\\n      - id: ac-26\\n        given: WebSocket connection active\\n        when: client sends command\\n        then: command format is {action, request_id?, payload}\\n      - id: ac-27\\n        given: command received\\n        when: processed\\n        then: \\\"server sends {ack: true, request_id, success, error?}\\\"\\n      - id: ac-28\\n        given: WebSocket connection\\n        when: \\\"client sends {action: 'subscribe', topics: ['files:updates']}\\\"\\n        then: server tracks subscription and sends events for that topic\\n      - id: ac-29\\n        given: file changes in .kspec/\\n        when: WebSocket client subscribed to files:updates\\n        then: \\\"receives event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data: {ref, action}}\\\"\\n      - id: ac-30\\n        given: malformed command received\\n        when: parsed\\n        then: \\\"return {ack: false, error: 'validation_error', details: ...}\\\"\\n      - id: ac-31\\n        given: connection closing\\n        when: close initiated\\n        then: use code 1000 for clean, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\\n      - id: ac-32\\n        given: server sends to slow client\\n        when: backpressure limit reached\\n        then: pause non-critical broadcasts until drain event\\n      - id: ac-33\\n        given: daemon is shutting down\\n        when: WebSocket connection active\\n        then: receives shutdown event with {reason}, connection closes gracefully\\n    status:\\n      maturity: draft\\n      implementation: in_progress\\n  - _ulid: 01KFHMFJD571JQEE33AKKMEQSJ\\n    slugs:\\n      - web-dashboard\\n    title: Web Dashboard\\n    type: feature\\n    tags:\\n      - svelte\\n      - ui\\n      - dashboard\\n    description: |\\n      SvelteKit-based web interface for viewing and editing specs, tasks, inbox, and session state.\\n      Uses shadcn-svelte components for accessible UI. Connects to daemon via REST API and WebSocket\\n      for real-time updates. Includes WebSocketManager for connection resilience with exponential\\n      backoff reconnection and sequence deduplication.\\n    depends_on:\\n      - \\\"@api-contract\\\"\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits:\\n      - \\\"@trait-filterable-list\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:11.366Z\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: daemon is running on configured port (default 3456)\\n        when: browser opens the daemon URL\\n        then: dashboard shows task overview with ready, in_progress, pending_review, blocked, completed\\n          counts\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: dashboard is displayed\\n        when: task counts update on server\\n        then: counts animate to new values without page refresh (WebSocket-driven)\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: dashboard is displayed\\n        when: user clicks a task count badge\\n        then: navigates to task list filtered by that status\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: user is viewing task list\\n        when: list loads\\n        then: shows task title, status badge, priority indicator, spec_ref link, notes count\\n      - id: ac-5\\n        given: user is viewing task list\\n        when: clicking a task row\\n        then: task detail panel opens showing description, notes (chronological), todos, dependencies\\n      - id: ac-6\\n        given: user is viewing task detail\\n        when: task has spec_ref\\n        then: spec reference is clickable link to spec item detail\\n      - id: ac-7\\n        given: user is viewing task detail\\n        when: user clicks Start Task button\\n        then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/start, task status updates, UI reflects change\\n      - id: ac-8\\n        given: user is viewing task detail\\n        when: user types in note textarea and clicks Add Note\\n        then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/note, note appears in list\\n      - id: ac-9\\n        given: user is viewing task list\\n        when: filter controls are visible\\n        then: can filter by status, type, tag, assignee, automation status\\n      - id: ac-10\\n        given: user applies filter\\n        when: filter selection changes\\n        then: URL updates with query params, list updates without full reload\\n      - id: ac-11\\n        given: user navigates to /items\\n        when: spec tree displays\\n        then: shows hierarchical tree with modules > features > requirements, expand/collapse\\n      - id: ac-12\\n        given: user clicks spec item in tree\\n        when: item detail panel opens\\n        then: shows title, description, acceptance criteria (GWT format), traits, implementation status\\n      - id: ac-13\\n        given: spec item has linked tasks\\n        when: viewing item detail\\n        then: Implementation section shows linked tasks with their status\\n      - id: ac-14\\n        given: spec item has traits\\n        when: viewing item detail\\n        then: Traits section shows trait titles as chips, clickable to trait detail\\n      - id: ac-15\\n        given: user clicks acceptance criterion\\n        when: AC row expands\\n        then: shows full Given/When/Then text with test coverage indicator if available\\n      - id: ac-16\\n        given: user navigates to /inbox\\n        when: inbox list displays\\n        then: shows items ordered by created_at desc with text preview, tags, added_by\\n      - id: ac-17\\n        given: user clicks Add button\\n        when: input field appears\\n        then: user can type text, press Enter to submit\\n      - id: ac-18\\n        given: new inbox item submitted\\n        when: POST succeeds\\n        then: item appears at top of list with animation\\n      - id: ac-19\\n        given: user clicks delete button on item\\n        when: confirmation appears\\n        then: on confirm, item removed from list\\n      - id: ac-20\\n        given: dashboard header area\\n        when: session has focus set\\n        then: displays current focus text prominently\\n      - id: ac-21\\n        given: dashboard sidebar\\n        when: observations exist\\n        then: shows unresolved observations count badge\\n      - id: ac-22\\n        given: user clicks observations badge\\n        when: observations panel opens\\n        then: lists unresolved observations with type icons (friction/success/question/idea)\\n      - id: ac-23\\n        given: user presses Cmd+K (or Ctrl+K)\\n        when: command palette opens\\n        then: shows search input with placeholder\\n      - id: ac-24\\n        given: user types in search box\\n        when: debounced search fires (300ms)\\n        then: results show tasks, items, inbox matching query grouped by type\\n      - id: ac-25\\n        given: search results display\\n        when: user clicks a result\\n        then: navigates to detail view for that item\\n      - id: ac-26\\n        given: browser width < 768px\\n        when: viewing any page\\n        then: layout adapts to single column, sidebar becomes bottom nav\\n      - id: ac-27\\n        given: browser width >= 1024px\\n        when: viewing detail panels\\n        then: detail panel opens as slide-over without navigating away from list\\n      - id: ac-28\\n        given: WebSocket connection drops\\n        when: reconnect logic triggers\\n        then: automatic reconnect with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s)\\n      - id: ac-29\\n        given: WebSocket disconnected for >10s\\n        when: viewing dashboard\\n        then: Connection lost indicator shown\\n      - id: ac-30\\n        given: events received via WebSocket\\n        when: seq <= lastSeqProcessed\\n        then: skip duplicate events (sequence deduplication)\\n      - id: ac-31\\n        given: WebSocket reconnects\\n        when: connection established\\n        then: client resets lastSeqProcessed = -1 (server generates new sequence)\\n      - id: ac-32\\n        given: WebSocket reconnects\\n        when: connection established\\n        then: client re-subscribes to all previous topics\\n      - id: ac-33\\n        given: another client modifies task\\n        when: WebSocket update received\\n        then: task list/detail updates without refresh, subtle highlight animation on changed item\\n    status:\\n      maturity: draft\\n      implementation: implemented\\n  - _ulid: 01KFHMFMN8PNQ78K7X7GATNQ2P\\n    slugs:\\n      - gh-pages-export\\n    title: GitHub Pages Export\\n    type: feature\\n    tags:\\n      - static\\n      - export\\n      - github\\n    description: >\\n      Static site generation from kspec state for hosting read-only views on GitHub Pages.\\n\\n      CI workflow builds JSON snapshot from shadow branch on push, SPA reads this JSON for\\n      rendering.\\n\\n      Enables deep linking to tasks/specs from PRs and issues with data freshness indicator.\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits:\\n      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-dry-run\\\"\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:13.672Z\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: kspec is installed\\n        when: user runs 'kspec export --format json'\\n        then: writes kspec-snapshot.json containing all tasks, items, inbox, meta to stdout or --output path\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: export runs\\n        when: output is generated\\n        then: JSON includes exported_at timestamp, version (kspec version), project metadata\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: export runs\\n        when: tasks are included\\n        then: each task includes resolved spec_ref title (not just ref string) for display without\\n          resolution\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: export runs\\n        when: items are included\\n        then: hierarchical structure preserved, acceptance_criteria expanded, traits resolved to include\\n          inherited ACs\\n      - id: ac-5\\n        given: export runs with --include-validation\\n        when: validation is run\\n        then: JSON includes validation block with error/warning counts and details\\n      - id: ac-6\\n        given: kspec is installed\\n        when: user runs 'kspec export --format html'\\n        then: generates self-contained HTML file with embedded JSON and SPA code\\n      - id: ac-7\\n        given: kspec is installed\\n        when: user runs 'kspec export --dry-run'\\n        then: shows what would be exported without writing files\\n      - id: ac-8\\n        given: push to kspec-meta branch\\n        when: CI workflow triggers\\n        then: runs kspec export, commits to gh-pages branch\\n      - id: ac-9\\n        given: CI workflow runs\\n        when: SPA assets don't exist\\n        then: copies SPA static assets (HTML, JS, CSS) to docs/ alongside JSON\\n      - id: ac-10\\n        given: rapid commits to kspec-meta\\n        when: multiple pushes within 30 seconds\\n        then: CI debounces and runs once with latest state\\n      - id: ac-11\\n        given: user opens gh-pages URL\\n        when: SPA loads\\n        then: fetches kspec-snapshot.json from same origin, renders dashboard\\n      - id: ac-12\\n        given: user navigates to /tasks/@task-slug\\n        when: deep link resolves\\n        then: SPA parses path (history API), shows task detail for that ref\\n      - id: ac-13\\n        given: user navigates to /items/@spec-slug\\n        when: deep link resolves\\n        then: SPA shows spec item detail for that ref\\n      - id: ac-14\\n        given: SPA renders\\n        when: validation data present in snapshot\\n        then: shows validation summary badge (green check or red X with count)\\n      - id: ac-15\\n        given: static export page\\n        when: displayed to user\\n        then: \\\"shows 'Data as of: [timestamp]' indicator prominently\\\"\\n      - id: ac-16\\n        given: viewing task in SPA mode\\n        when: user sees Start Task button area\\n        then: button is disabled with tooltip explaining read-only mode\\n      - id: ac-17\\n        given: viewing inbox in SPA mode\\n        when: Add button area visible\\n        then: button is disabled/hidden\\n      - id: ac-18\\n        given: SPA mode\\n        when: any write action attempted\\n        then: graceful no-op with informative message\\n      - id: ac-19\\n        given: app is built with VITE_STATIC_MODE=true\\n        when: app initializes on page load\\n        then: mode is set to static without attempting daemon health check\\n      - id: ac-20\\n        given: app is in static mode\\n        when: fetching kspec-snapshot.json\\n        then: URL is prefixed with SvelteKit configured base path from $app/paths\\n    status:\\n      maturity: draft\\n      implementation: implemented\\n  - _ulid: 01KFMM8F5WG89H244FXVSRZ35E\\n    slugs:\\n      - cli-serve-commands\\n    title: CLI Serve Commands\\n    type: feature\\n    tags:\\n      - cli\\n      - serve\\n    description: |\\n      CLI commands for managing the daemon server lifecycle. Provides human and script-friendly\\n      interfaces to start, stop, and monitor the daemon.\\n    depends_on:\\n      - \\\"@daemon-server\\\"\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits:\\n      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-semantic-exit-codes\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-error-guidance\\\"\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-01-22T07:00:00.000Z\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: daemon not running\\n        when: kspec serve executed\\n        then: starts server in foreground, logs to stdout, Ctrl+C stops\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: daemon not running\\n        when: kspec serve --daemon executed\\n        then: starts in background, writes PID file, returns immediately with status message\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: daemon not running\\n        when: kspec serve --port 8080 executed\\n        then: starts on specified port\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: daemon running\\n        when: kspec serve stop executed\\n        then: sends SIGTERM to daemon PID, waits for clean shutdown, removes PID file\\n      - id: ac-5\\n        given: daemon not running\\n        when: kspec serve stop executed\\n        then: outputs 'Daemon not running' with exit code 0 (idempotent)\\n      - id: ac-6\\n        given: any state\\n        when: kspec serve status executed\\n        then: outputs JSON with {running, pid, port, uptime, connections}\\n      - id: ac-7\\n        given: daemon running\\n        when: kspec serve restart executed\\n        then: stops existing daemon, starts new one, preserves port setting\\n      - id: ac-8\\n        given: any state\\n        when: kspec serve logs executed\\n        then: tails daemon log file (.kspec/.daemon.log)\\n      - id: ac-9\\n        given: daemon running\\n        when: kspec serve logs --follow executed\\n        then: streams log output continuously until Ctrl+C\\n      - id: ac-10\\n        given: port already in use\\n        when: kspec serve attempts to start\\n        then: fails with clear error message suggesting --port flag\\n    status:\\n      maturity: draft\\n      implementation: implemented\\n  - _ulid: 01KFQ84FVYMN3Z0HXWZ5AK7CQD\\n    slugs:\\n      - multi-directory-daemon\\n    title: Multi-Directory Daemon Architecture\\n    type: feature\\n    tags:\\n      - daemon\\n      - architecture\\n      - multi-project\\n    description: |\\n      Extends the daemon server to support multiple kspec projects simultaneously from a single\\n      daemon process. Projects are identified via X-Kspec-Dir HTTP header. Enables E2E testing\\n      with isolated fixtures and multi-project development workflows.\\n\\n      Key architectural changes:\\n      - Global daemon with PID/port files at ~/.config/kspec/\\n      - Project context caching with on-demand registration\\n      - Per-project file watchers\\n      - WebSocket connections bound to specific projects\\n\\n      BREAKING CHANGE: PID/port files move from .kspec/.daemon.pid to ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid\\n    depends_on:\\n      - \\\"@daemon-server\\\"\\n      - \\\"@api-contract\\\"\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to:\\n      - \\\"@cli-serve-commands\\\"\\n    tests: []\\n    traits:\\n      - \\\"@trait-localhost-security\\\"\\n      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n    notes:\\n      - _ulid: 01KFQ84FVZB2CWH7Y4GPQR8M9N\\n        created_at: 2026-01-24T06:00:00.000Z\\n        author: \\\"@claude\\\"\\n        content: |\\n          Design decisions:\\n          - X-Kspec-Dir header for project selection (clean URLs, easy for clients)\\n          - Single bundled web UI (consistent version across projects)\\n          - On-demand project registration (auto-register on first request)\\n          - No memory limit on cached projects (keep until restart)\\n          - Global PID at ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid\\n          - Per-project file watchers\\n          - Backwards compatible (no header = startup cwd project if valid)\\n    created: 2026-01-24T06:00:00.000Z\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: daemon is running\\n        when: request includes X-Kspec-Dir header with valid absolute path\\n        then: daemon uses that project's context for the request\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: daemon started from directory with .kspec/\\n        when: request has no X-Kspec-Dir header\\n        then: daemon uses startup directory's project as default\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: daemon started from directory without .kspec/\\n        when: request without X-Kspec-Dir arrives\\n        then: return 400 with error \\\"No default project configured. Specify X-Kspec-Dir header.\\\"\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: request specifies unknown project path\\n        when: path is valid kspec project\\n        then: daemon auto-registers and caches project context\\n      - id: ac-5\\n        given: request specifies invalid path (no .kspec/)\\n        when: request processed\\n        then: return 400 with error \\\"Invalid kspec project - .kspec/ not found at <path>\\\"\\n      - id: ac-6\\n        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value\\n        when: path is relative\\n        then: reject with 400 and error \\\"Path must be absolute\\\"\\n      - id: ac-7\\n        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value\\n        when: path contains \\\"..\\\" segments\\n        then: reject with 400 and error \\\"Path must not contain parent traversal\\\"\\n      - id: ac-8\\n        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value\\n        when: normalized path differs from provided path\\n        then: use normalized path for registration (resolve \\\".\\\" segments, remove trailing slashes, do NOT\\n          resolve symlinks)\\n      - id: ac-8b\\n        given: X-Kspec-Dir points to path with insufficient read permissions\\n        when: request processed\\n        then: return 403 with error \\\"Permission denied - cannot read <path>\\\"\\n      - id: ac-9\\n        given: no daemon running\\n        when: kspec serve start runs from any directory\\n        then: daemon starts and writes PID to ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid and port to\\n          ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port\\n      - id: ac-9b\\n        given: ~/.config/kspec/ does not exist\\n        when: daemon starts\\n        then: create directory with mode 0755 before writing PID/port files\\n      - id: ac-9c\\n        given: ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port exists but contains invalid content\\n        when: CLI reads port\\n        then: return error \\\"Invalid daemon port file\\\" and suggest \\\"kspec serve stop && kspec serve start\\\"\\n      - id: ac-10\\n        given: daemon running on port 3456\\n        when: kspec serve start runs from different directory\\n        then: command exits with success and outputs \\\"Daemon already running on port 3456\\\" (no second\\n          instance started)\\n      - id: ac-10b\\n        given: two kspec serve start commands run concurrently (neither has written PID yet)\\n        when: both check for running daemon\\n        then: only one daemon starts (use file lock on PID file)\\n      - id: ac-11\\n        given: daemon running\\n        when: kspec serve stop runs from any directory\\n        then: daemon stops and removes global PID and port files\\n      - id: ac-12\\n        given: daemon running\\n        when: kspec serve status runs\\n        then: shows daemon status with port, uptime, and list of registered projects with their paths\\n      - id: ac-13\\n        given: CLI needs to connect to daemon\\n        when: daemon is running\\n        then: CLI reads port from ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port\\n      - id: ac-14\\n        given: daemon restarts\\n        when: first request for a project arrives\\n        then: project is re-registered automatically (same as initial registration)\\n      - id: ac-15\\n        given: daemon running with registered projects\\n        when: daemon restarts\\n        then: registered project list is empty (no persistence across restarts)\\n      - id: ac-16\\n        given: two concurrent requests for unregistered project with same path\\n        when: processed\\n        then: both succeed and share the same registered project context (no duplicate watchers)\\n      - id: ac-17\\n        given: project is registered\\n        when: files change in project's .kspec/\\n        then: file watcher triggers events scoped to that project\\n      - id: ac-18\\n        given: multiple projects registered\\n        when: Project A changes\\n        then: only Project A's WebSocket subscribers receive updates\\n      - id: ac-19\\n        given: project watcher creation fails due to OS limits (ulimit)\\n        when: error occurs\\n        then: project registration fails with 503 and error \\\"Unable to watch project - resource limit\\n          reached\\\"\\n      - id: ac-20\\n        given: registered project's .kspec/ directory is deleted\\n        when: next request arrives for that project\\n        then: return 404 and unregister project automatically\\n      - id: ac-21\\n        given: WebSocket client connects with X-Kspec-Dir header during handshake\\n        when: connection established\\n        then: connection is bound to that project for its lifetime and only receives events from that\\n          project\\n      - id: ac-21b\\n        given: WebSocket connection is established and bound to project\\n        when: client attempts to change project\\n        then: project binding is immutable - client must disconnect and reconnect with new header\\n      - id: ac-22\\n        given: WebSocket client connects without X-Kspec-Dir header\\n        when: default project exists\\n        then: connection is bound to default project\\n      - id: ac-23\\n        given: WebSocket client connects without X-Kspec-Dir header\\n        when: no default project\\n        then: connection is rejected with close code 4000 and reason \\\"No project specified\\\"\\n      - id: ac-24\\n        given: multi-project mode\\n        when: any API endpoint is called\\n        then: response data is scoped to the request's project (no cross-project data leakage)\\n      - id: ac-25\\n        given: web UI loads\\n        when: more than one project registered\\n        then: project selector is shown listing all registered projects\\n      - id: ac-26\\n        given: user selects project in UI\\n        when: selection changes\\n        then: all subsequent API requests include that project's path in X-Kspec-Dir header\\n      - id: ac-27\\n        given: UI is showing project data\\n        when: different project selected\\n        then: UI reloads data from newly selected project\\n      - id: ac-28\\n        given: GET /api/projects\\n        when: called\\n        then: returns list of registered projects with paths, registration time, and watcher status\\n      - id: ac-29\\n        given: POST /api/projects\\n        when: called with {path string} body\\n        then: manually registers a project (for explicit registration use cases)\\n      - id: ac-30\\n        given: DELETE /api/projects/:encodedPath\\n        when: called\\n        then: unregisters project and stops its file watcher\\n      - id: ac-8c\\n        given: X-Kspec-Dir header contains symlinked path\\n        when: path resolves to same directory as another registered project via symlink\\n        then: paths are treated as separate projects (symlinks are NOT resolved during normalization)\\n      - id: ac-20b\\n        given: daemon started from directory with .kspec/ which is later deleted\\n        when: request without X-Kspec-Dir arrives after default project .kspec/ deleted\\n        then: return 400 with error 'Default project no longer valid. Specify X-Kspec-Dir header.'\\n      - id: ac-11b\\n        given: daemon is shutting down\\n        when: shutdown signal received\\n        then: all project watchers are stopped and all WebSocket connections are closed before process exits\\n    status:\\n      maturity: draft\\n      implementation: implemented\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2ZKQRVKRZYZVGP10EN\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-design-system\\n    title: UI Design System\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n      Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n      keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n      across all views.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          The web UI app.css file\\n        when: |\\n          imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n        then: |\\n          All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\n          are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: |\\n          A component using design tokens\\n        when: |\\n          The dark theme tokens are applied\\n        then: |\\n          oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\n          pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\n          are visually distinct\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: |\\n          A view with loading states\\n        when: |\\n          Content is loading\\n        then: |\\n          Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: |\\n          An active agent task card\\n        when: |\\n          The agent is working\\n        then: |\\n          Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.719Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF3J5HTWWDRHWM3C42DJ\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-app-shell\\n    title: App Shell and Navigation\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\\n      with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\\n      Preserve existing functionality during migration.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          The web UI loaded in daemon mode\\n        when: |\\n          The app shell renders\\n        then: |\\n          A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\\n          Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\\n          Config (Workflows, Settings)\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: |\\n          Sidebar navigation items\\n        when: |\\n          Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\\n        then: |\\n          Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: |\\n          The /items route\\n        when: |\\n          A user navigates to /items\\n        then: |\\n          They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: |\\n          The Observations nav item\\n        when: |\\n          There are zero unresolved observations\\n        then: |\\n          The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.738Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF40T8KCJHMT0JVYMVV7\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-task-board\\n    title: Task Board (Kanban)\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      Kanban-style task board with columns mapping to kspec task states.\\n      Active Fleet row shows currently running agent work with live output.\\n      Task cards show key metadata, clicking opens detail modal.\\n      Not drag-and-drop — tasks transition via agents/CLI.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          Tasks in various states\\n        when: |\\n          The task board renders\\n        then: |\\n          Tasks are distributed into columns: Backlog (pending, manual_only/unassessed),\\n          Ready (pending, eligible), In Progress (in_progress, needs_work),\\n          Review (pending_review), Done (completed recent), with blocked and cancelled\\n          handled as sections/indicators\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: |\\n          A task card on the board\\n        when: |\\n          The card renders\\n        then: |\\n          It shows priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (mono), spec ref link,\\n          and metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: |\\n          A task card\\n        when: |\\n          The user clicks it\\n        then: |\\n          A detail modal opens showing full task info: title, description, status,\\n          priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos,\\n          automation status, VCS info (branch, PR link), plan ref, session link\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: |\\n          Agents actively working on tasks (dispatch running)\\n        when: |\\n          The task board renders\\n        then: |\\n          An Active Fleet row appears at the top showing cards with task title,\\n          agent name, elapsed time with pulse indicator, and last few lines of output\\n      - id: ac-5\\n        given: |\\n          The task board with WebSocket connected\\n        when: |\\n          A task state changes\\n        then: |\\n          The board updates in real-time without page refresh\\n      - id: ac-6\\n        given: |\\n          The task detail modal in daemon mode\\n        when: |\\n          The user clicks action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note)\\n        then: |\\n          The corresponding task transition or mutation is executed via API\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.752Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF4FP4GY593BCW3XZHQM\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-session-stream\\n    title: Session Stream View\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      View for watching agent work — both historical and live. Renders structured\\n      session events (messages, tool calls, thinking blocks) from events.jsonl.\\n      Live sessions show streaming text with periodic structured refresh.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          A completed session with events.jsonl\\n        when: |\\n          The user navigates to /sessions/:id\\n        then: |\\n          The session events render as structured blocks: agent messages (markdown),\\n          tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), and thinking blocks\\n          (collapsed by default, expandable)\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: |\\n          An active session with streaming output\\n        when: |\\n          The user views the session\\n        then: |\\n          Live text streams in real-time via agent_text_chunk WebSocket events,\\n          with periodic structured refresh from events.jsonl\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: |\\n          The session stream view\\n        when: |\\n          New content arrives while auto-scrolling\\n        then: |\\n          The view auto-scrolls to follow new content, pauses when user scrolls up\\n          (>100px from bottom), and resumes when scrolled back. A \\\"jump to bottom\\\"\\n          button appears when paused.\\n      - id: ac-4\\n        given: |\\n          The session stream view\\n        when: |\\n          A session context panel is shown on the left\\n        then: |\\n          It displays session metadata, spec context with AC checklist,\\n          files changed during session, and budget info\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.767Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF4YR57EJQTNSHFQKZHE\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-agent-dispatch\\n    title: Agent and Dispatch View\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      View showing agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped),\\n      and active invocations with links to session streams.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          The /agents route\\n        when: |\\n          Agent definitions exist in meta\\n        then: |\\n          Each agent shows name, triggers, active invocation count, and completed count\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: |\\n          The dispatch engine is running\\n        when: |\\n          The agents page renders\\n        then: |\\n          Dispatch status shows as running with a stop button, and active invocations\\n          show task ref, elapsed time, and link to session stream\\n      - id: ac-3\\n        given: |\\n          The dispatch engine is stopped\\n        when: |\\n          The agents page renders\\n        then: |\\n          Dispatch status shows as stopped with no active invocations\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.782Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF5CPD38NH05CPXG4NFY\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-session-history\\n    title: Session History\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      List view of past agent sessions with filtering and navigation to session detail.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          Sessions exist on disk\\n        when: |\\n          The user navigates to /sessions\\n        then: |\\n          A list of sessions shows ID, agent type, task ref, status,\\n          duration, and age, sorted by most recent first\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: |\\n          The session list\\n        when: |\\n          The user clicks a session\\n        then: |\\n          They navigate to /sessions/:id showing the session stream view\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.796Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF5VWDHKVSJ51JSZDSPN\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-inbox-enhanced\\n    title: Enhanced Inbox View\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      Enhanced inbox with triage status inline, quick actions, filtering, and bulk selection.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          Inbox items with varying triage states\\n        when: |\\n          The inbox view renders\\n        then: |\\n          Each item shows triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n          with quick triage action links\\n      - id: ac-2\\n        given: |\\n          The inbox view\\n        when: |\\n          The user applies filters (status, tags, age)\\n        then: |\\n          The list filters accordingly\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.811Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF6C8W98RNSGH5V0EM4G\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-plans-view\\n    title: Plans View\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      View for browsing plan records with progress tracking via linked specs and tasks.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          Plan records exist\\n        when: |\\n          The user navigates to /plans\\n        then: |\\n          Each plan shows title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts,\\n          and progress based on task completion status\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.828Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF6TWXS4Z07QE6R2JEG8\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-validation-view\\n    title: Validation and Alignment View\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      View showing validation results, alignment statistics, and issues.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          The user navigates to /validate\\n        when: |\\n          Validation data loads\\n        then: |\\n          Summary shows error count, warning count, valid item count.\\n          Alignment section shows spec coverage %, AC coverage %,\\n          orphaned tasks/specs counts. Issues list grouped by severity.\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.842Z\\n  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF7944GT0W021545WRPK\\n    slugs:\\n      - ui-dashboard-overview\\n    title: Dashboard Overview\\n    type: feature\\n    tags: []\\n    description: |\\n      Home view answering \\\"what's happening right now?\\\" with active work,\\n      status summary, recent activity, and needs-attention aggregation.\\n    acceptance_criteria:\\n      - id: ac-1\\n        given: |\\n          The user navigates to /\\n        when: |\\n          The dashboard renders\\n        then: |\\n          Active work section shows currently running agent tasks (if any),\\n          status summary shows clickable count cards per status,\\n          needs-attention section aggregates untriaged inbox, unresolved observations,\\n          validation warnings, and blocked tasks\\n    depends_on: []\\n    implements: []\\n    relates_to: []\\n    tests: []\\n    traits: []\\n    notes: []\\n    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.857Z\\n\",\"numLines\":1400,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":1400}},\"toolName\":\"Read\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01PQwQbKfz7yaGA8TXycV9E1\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\"}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:254:{\"ts\":1772684343205,\"seq\":253,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Read\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01PQwQbKfz7yaGA8TXycV9E1\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"rawOutput\":\"     1→_ulid: 01KFHMF5ZS4RD70JBQNGBQJVFY\\n     2→slugs:\\n     3→  - web-ui\\n     4→title: Web UI System\\n     5→type: module\\n     6→status:\\n     7→  maturity: draft\\n     8→  implementation: implemented\\n     9→description: >\\n    10→  Web-based interface for viewing, editing, and managing kspec state. Includes three deployment\\n    11→  modes:\\n    12→\\n    13→  1. Local daemon mode - Elysia.js server on Bun with WebSocket for real-time updates\\n    14→\\n    15→  2. Web dashboard - SvelteKit + shadcn-svelte for full CRUD operations\\n    16→\\n    17→  3. GitHub Pages export - Static JSON snapshot with read-only SPA for public sharing\\n    18→\\n    19→\\n    20→  Tech stack: Elysia.js, Bun runtime, WebSocket (not SSE), SvelteKit, shadcn-svelte.\\n    21→\\n    22→  Distribution via bun build --compile for portable executables.\\n    23→tags:\\n    24→  - web\\n    25→  - ui\\n    26→  - daemon\\n    27→  - elysia\\n    28→  - bun\\n    29→depends_on: []\\n    30→implements: []\\n    31→relates_to: []\\n    32→tests: []\\n    33→traits: []\\n    34→notes: []\\n    35→features:\\n    36→  - _ulid: 01KFHMFGD2563NGHJWPPXGN9CB\\n    37→    slugs:\\n    38→      - daemon-server\\n    39→    title: Daemon Server Mode\\n    40→    type: feature\\n    41→    tags:\\n    42→      - server\\n    43→      - websocket\\n    44→      - elysia\\n    45→    description: >\\n    46→      Long-running Elysia.js server on Bun runtime that exposes kspec state via HTTP API and\\n    47→      WebSocket\\n    48→\\n    49→      for real-time updates. Binds to localhost only for security. Supports foreground and\\n    50→      background\\n    51→\\n    52→      modes with PID file management. Includes heartbeat ping/pong for connection health monitoring.\\n    53→    depends_on: []\\n    54→    implements: []\\n    55→    relates_to: []\\n    56→    tests: []\\n    57→    traits:\\n    58→      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n    59→      - \\\"@trait-error-guidance\\\"\\n    60→      - \\\"@trait-shadow-commit\\\"\\n    61→      - \\\"@trait-localhost-security\\\"\\n    62→      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n    63→    notes: []\\n    64→    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:09.314Z\\n    65→    acceptance_criteria:\\n    66→      - id: ac-1\\n    67→        given: kspec is installed\\n    68→        when: user runs 'kspec serve'\\n    69→        then: Elysia HTTP server starts on configurable port (default 3456) binding to localhost only\\n    70→      - id: ac-2\\n    71→        given: daemon is starting\\n    72→        when: server binds to network interface\\n    73→        then: only accepts connections from 127.0.0.1 and ::1 (IPv6 localhost)\\n    74→      - id: ac-3\\n    75→        given: connection attempt from non-localhost IP\\n    76→        when: request received\\n    77→        then: connection rejected with 403 Forbidden\\n    78→      - id: ac-4\\n    79→        given: daemon is running\\n    80→        when: any .kspec/*.yaml file changes\\n    81→        then: connected WebSocket clients receive update event via topic subscription\\n    82→      - id: ac-5\\n    83→        given: file watching is active\\n    84→        when: rapid changes occur (< 500ms apart)\\n    85→        then: events are debounced and aggregated into single notification\\n    86→      - id: ac-6\\n    87→        given: watched file has YAML parse error\\n    88→        when: change detected\\n    89→        then: error logged and WebSocket broadcasts error event (daemon does not crash)\\n    90→      - id: ac-7\\n    91→        given: .kspec directory becomes inaccessible\\n    92→        when: watcher encounters error\\n    93→        then: daemon logs error and attempts recovery with exponential backoff\\n    94→      - id: ac-8\\n    95→        given: Bun fs.watch fails or misses events\\n    96→        when: reliability issue detected\\n    97→        then: automatically fall back to Chokidar file watcher\\n    98→      - id: ac-9\\n    99→        given: daemon is running\\n   100→        when: user runs 'kspec serve --daemon'\\n   101→        then: process detaches to background, writes PID to .kspec/.daemon.pid, CLI returns immediately\\n   102→      - id: ac-10\\n   103→        given: daemon is running in background\\n   104→        when: user runs 'kspec serve stop'\\n   105→        then: daemon shuts down gracefully, removes PID file, closes all WebSocket connections\\n   106→      - id: ac-11\\n   107→        given: daemon is running\\n   108→        when: GET /api/health is called\\n   109→        then: returns {status, uptime, connections, version} JSON\\n   110→      - id: ac-12\\n   111→        given: daemon receives SIGTERM or SIGINT\\n   112→        when: shutdown signal received\\n   113→        then: graceful shutdown (flush pending messages, close connections, save state)\\n   114→      - id: ac-13\\n   115→        given: WebSocket connection established\\n   116→        when: 30 seconds pass without activity\\n   117→        then: server sends ping frame\\n   118→      - id: ac-14\\n   119→        given: ping was sent\\n   120→        when: no pong received within 90 seconds\\n   121→        then: connection closed with code 1001\\n   122→      - id: ac-15\\n   123→        given: Elysia server is configured\\n   124→        when: routes are registered\\n   125→        then: use plugin pattern for middleware (CORS, logging, validation)\\n   126→      - id: ac-16\\n   127→        given: daemon code is ready\\n   128→        when: bun build --compile runs\\n   129→        then: produces standalone executable without requiring Bun installation\\n   130→      - id: ac-17\\n   131→        given: daemon is running with web UI built\\n   132→        when: browser opens http://localhost:<port>/\\n   133→        then: serves the built web UI assets (SvelteKit static build) as the root route\\n   134→    status:\\n   135→      maturity: draft\\n   136→      implementation: in_progress\\n   137→    features:\\n   138→      - _ulid: 01KJP2768T96S8870BH36ZE76K\\n   139→        slugs:\\n   140→          - daemon-agent-dispatch\\n   141→        title: Daemon Agent Dispatch Integration\\n   142→        type: feature\\n   143→        tags: []\\n   144→        description: |\\n   145→          Agent dispatch API routes in the daemon, enhanced file watcher with\\n   146→          task state diffing for change detection, CLI event emission endpoint,\\n   147→          and WebSocket broadcasts for agent invocation status.\\n   148→        acceptance_criteria:\\n   149→          - id: ac-1\\n   150→            given: |\\n   151→              The daemon is running with dispatch enabled\\n   152→            when: |\\n   153→              The file watcher detects a change in project.tasks.yaml\\n   154→            then: |\\n   155→              The watcher parses the new task states, diffs against the\\n   156→              previously cached states, and emits state change events to\\n   157→              the dispatch engine for each detected transition\\n   158→          - id: ac-2\\n   159→            given: |\\n   160→              A CLI command changes task state (e.g. kspec task start)\\n   161→            when: |\\n   162→              The daemon is running\\n   163→            then: |\\n   164→              The CLI posts a JSON event to POST /api/agent/events containing\\n   165→              task_id, previous_status, new_status, and timestamp\\n   166→          - id: ac-3\\n   167→            given: |\\n   168→              The daemon receives a state change event matching dispatch rules\\n   169→            when: |\\n   170→              The dispatch engine processes it\\n   171→            then: |\\n   172→              The agent is dispatched and a status event is broadcast on the\\n   173→              agents WebSocket topic\\n   174→          - id: ac-4\\n   175→            given: |\\n   176→              A WebSocket client subscribes to agent status updates\\n   177→            when: |\\n   178→              An agent invocation starts, completes, or fails\\n   179→            then: |\\n   180→              A broadcast event is sent containing session_id, agent_id,\\n   181→              task_id, status, and timestamp\\n   182→          - id: ac-5\\n   183→            given: |\\n   184→              GET /api/agent/status is called\\n   185→            when: |\\n   186→              The dispatch engine is running\\n   187→            then: |\\n   188→              Returns JSON with active invocations array, queue depth number,\\n   189→              dispatch_enabled boolean, and agent_definitions array\\n   190→          - id: ac-6\\n   191→            given: |\\n   192→              POST /api/agent/dispatch is called with action start or stop\\n   193→            when: |\\n   194→              The request is from localhost\\n   195→            then: |\\n   196→              The dispatch engine starts or stops and returns JSON with the\\n   197→              new dispatch_enabled state\\n   198→          - id: ac-7\\n   199→            given: |\\n   200→              The daemon is not running\\n   201→            when: |\\n   202→              A CLI command changes task state\\n   203→            then: |\\n   204→              The event emission POST fails silently with no error to the\\n   205→              user — dispatch requires a running daemon\\n   206→          - id: ac-8\\n   207→            given: The dispatch engine runs an agent invocation\\n   208→            when: The agent produces text output (agent_message_chunk events)\\n   209→            then: The daemon broadcasts each text chunk on the agents WebSocket topic with type\\n   210→              agent_text_chunk, session_id, agent_id, task_id, text, and timestamp\\n   211→        depends_on: []\\n   212→        implements: []\\n   213→        relates_to: []\\n   214→        tests: []\\n   215→        traits:\\n   216→          - \\\"@trait-api-endpoint\\\"\\n   217→          - \\\"@trait-localhost-security\\\"\\n   218→          - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n   219→        notes: []\\n   220→        created: 2026-03-02T01:22:20.058Z\\n   221→        status:\\n   222→          maturity: draft\\n   223→          implementation: implemented\\n   224→    requirements:\\n   225→      - _ulid: 01KJRZWDCC8W2WT0Q3A9CZAAGY\\n   226→        slugs:\\n   227→          - daemon-web-ui-bundle\\n   228→        title: Web UI assets bundled in npm package\\n   229→        type: requirement\\n   230→        tags: []\\n   231→        depends_on: []\\n   232→        implements: []\\n   233→        relates_to: []\\n   234→        tests: []\\n   235→        traits: []\\n   236→        notes: []\\n   237→        created: 2026-03-03T04:39:13.036Z\\n   238→        description: The kspec npm package bundles the pre-built web UI static assets so the daemon can\\n   239→          serve the web UI when installed in any project, without requiring a local web UI build.\\n   240→          The build pipeline copies packages/web-ui/build to dist/web-ui/, and resolveWebUiPath\\n   241→          falls back to that location relative to the daemon module.\\n   242→        acceptance_criteria:\\n   243→          - id: ac-1\\n   244→            given: npm run build is executed\\n   245→            when: build completes\\n   246→            then: packages/web-ui/build output is copied to dist/web-ui/ in the package\\n   247→          - id: ac-2\\n   248→            given: kspec is installed in a project with no local web UI build\\n   249→            when: daemon starts and resolves web UI path\\n   250→            then: resolveWebUiPath returns the bundled dist/web-ui/ path relative to the daemon module location\\n   251→          - id: ac-3\\n   252→            given: kspec is installed as an npm package in a non-monorepo project\\n   253→            when: browser opens http://localhost:3456/\\n   254→            then: daemon serves the bundled web UI and returns HTTP 200 with HTML content\\n   255→          - id: ac-4\\n   256→            given: an explicit webUiDir option or WEB_UI_DIR env var or local packages/web-ui/build is present\\n   257→            when: daemon starts\\n   258→            then: the explicit or local path takes precedence over the bundled dist/web-ui/ fallback\\n   259→        status:\\n   260→          maturity: draft\\n   261→          implementation: implemented\\n   262→      - _ulid: 01KJTVMGPNP3HN9B9SRF6MEER7\\n   263→        slugs:\\n   264→          - ws-disconnect-lifecycle-cleanup\\n   265→        title: WebSocket Disconnect Lifecycle Cleanup\\n   266→        type: requirement\\n   267→        tags:\\n   268→          - daemon\\n   269→          - websocket\\n   270→          - reliability\\n   271→        description: Ensure daemon WebSocket disconnect handling is accurate for abnormal closes. Disconnect\\n   272→          events must reliably identify the same session created on connect, remove that session\\n   273→          from in-memory registries, and prevent stale heartbeat/client counts after client\\n   274→          disconnect or process termination.\\n   275→        depends_on: []\\n   276→        implements: []\\n   277→        relates_to: []\\n   278→        tests: []\\n   279→        traits: []\\n   280→        notes: []\\n   281→        created: 2026-03-03T22:03:28.854Z\\n   282→        acceptance_criteria:\\n   283→          - id: ac-1\\n   284→            given: multiple clients are connected and one disconnects\\n   285→            when: GET /api/health is requested\\n   286→            then: the connections field reflects only currently active sessions\\n   287→          - id: ac-3\\n   288→            given: a disconnected session was previously in heartbeat monitoring\\n   289→            when: the next heartbeat interval executes\\n   290→            then: the daemon does not attempt to ping that session and emits no stale heartbeat ping log for it\\n   291→          - id: ac-2\\n   292→            given: a WebSocket client disconnects unexpectedly with close code 1006\\n   293→            when: the daemon close handler runs\\n   294→            then: the session is removed from pubsub connection tracking and the disconnect log includes that\\n   295→              session id rather than undefined\\n   296→        status:\\n   297→          maturity: draft\\n   298→          implementation: implemented\\n   299→  - _ulid: 01KFMM8F5V7H46QYW9MVFYRTHW\\n   300→    slugs:\\n   301→      - api-contract\\n   302→    title: REST and WebSocket API Contract\\n   303→    type: feature\\n   304→    tags:\\n   305→      - api\\n   306→      - rest\\n   307→      - websocket\\n   308→    description: |\\n   309→      REST API contract for HTTP endpoints and WebSocket protocol for real-time communication.\\n   310→      All REST endpoints return JSON with consistent patterns. WebSocket uses topic-based pub/sub\\n   311→      with request_id correlation for command acknowledgment.\\n   312→    depends_on:\\n   313→      - \\\"@daemon-server\\\"\\n   314→    implements: []\\n   315→    relates_to: []\\n   316→    tests: []\\n   317→    traits:\\n   318→      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n   319→      - \\\"@trait-filterable-list\\\"\\n   320→      - \\\"@trait-error-guidance\\\"\\n   321→      - \\\"@trait-api-endpoint\\\"\\n   322→      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n   323→    notes: []\\n   324→    created: 2026-01-22T07:00:00.000Z\\n   325→    acceptance_criteria:\\n   326→      - id: ac-1\\n   327→        given: daemon is running\\n   328→        when: request from allowed CORS origin received\\n   329→        then: CORS headers allow the request (origins configured for dev and production)\\n   330→      - id: ac-2\\n   331→        given: daemon is running\\n   332→        when: GET /api/tasks is called\\n   333→        then: returns JSON array of all tasks with status, priority, spec_ref, notes count\\n   334→      - id: ac-3\\n   335→        given: daemon is running\\n   336→        when: GET /api/tasks with status filter (e.g., ?status=pending&status=in_progress)\\n   337→        then: returns only tasks matching filter (supports multi-value)\\n   338→      - id: ac-4\\n   339→        given: daemon is running\\n   340→        when: GET /api/tasks with pagination (?limit=10&offset=20)\\n   341→        then: returns paginated results with {items, total, offset, limit} wrapper\\n   342→      - id: ac-5\\n   343→        given: daemon is running\\n   344→        when: GET /api/tasks/:ref is called\\n   345→        then: resolves ref via ReferenceIndex, returns full task with notes, todos, dependencies\\n   346→      - id: ac-6\\n   347→        given: daemon is running\\n   348→        when: POST /api/tasks/:ref/start is called\\n   349→        then: task transitions to in_progress, WebSocket broadcasts update, returns updated task\\n   350→      - id: ac-7\\n   351→        given: daemon is running\\n   352→        when: POST /api/tasks/:ref/note with {content} body\\n   353→        then: note appended to task, shadow commit occurs, WebSocket broadcasts update\\n   354→      - id: ac-8\\n   355→        given: daemon is running\\n   356→        when: GET /api/items is called\\n   357→        then: returns JSON array of all spec items (modules, features, requirements)\\n   358→      - id: ac-9\\n   359→        given: daemon is running\\n   360→        when: GET /api/items with type filter (?type=feature&type=requirement)\\n   361→        then: returns only items matching type filter\\n   362→      - id: ac-10\\n   363→        given: daemon is running\\n   364→        when: GET /api/items/:ref is called\\n   365→        then: resolves ref, returns full item with acceptance_criteria, traits, relationships\\n   366→      - id: ac-11\\n   367→        given: daemon is running\\n   368→        when: GET /api/items/:ref/tasks is called\\n   369→        then: returns tasks linked to this spec via AlignmentIndex\\n   370→      - id: ac-12\\n   371→        given: daemon is running\\n   372→        when: GET /api/inbox is called\\n   373→        then: returns all inbox items ordered by created_at desc\\n   374→      - id: ac-13\\n   375→        given: daemon is running\\n   376→        when: POST /api/inbox with {text} body\\n   377→        then: creates inbox item, returns with generated ULID\\n   378→      - id: ac-14\\n   379→        given: daemon is running\\n   380→        when: DELETE /api/inbox/:ref is called\\n   381→        then: removes inbox item, returns success confirmation\\n   382→      - id: ac-15\\n   383→        given: daemon is running\\n   384→        when: GET /api/meta/session is called\\n   385→        then: returns current session context (focus, threads, questions)\\n   386→      - id: ac-16\\n   387→        given: daemon is running\\n   388→        when: GET /api/meta/agents is called\\n   389→        then: returns all defined agents\\n   390→      - id: ac-17\\n   391→        given: daemon is running\\n   392→        when: GET /api/meta/workflows is called\\n   393→        then: returns all defined workflows\\n   394→      - id: ac-18\\n   395→        given: daemon is running\\n   396→        when: GET /api/meta/observations with filter (?resolved=false)\\n   397→        then: returns observations matching filter\\n   398→      - id: ac-19\\n   399→        given: daemon is running\\n   400→        when: GET /api/search?q=login is called\\n   401→        then: searches across all items using grep/title matching\\n   402→      - id: ac-20\\n   403→        given: daemon is running\\n   404→        when: GET /api/validate is called\\n   405→        then: runs full validation, returns ValidationResult\\n   406→      - id: ac-21\\n   407→        given: daemon is running\\n   408→        when: GET /api/alignment is called\\n   409→        then: returns AlignmentIndex stats and warnings\\n   410→      - id: ac-22\\n   411→        given: API request has invalid ref\\n   412→        when: any endpoint with :ref parameter\\n   413→        then: returns {error, message, suggestion} with 404 status, suggests similar refs if available\\n   414→      - id: ac-23\\n   415→        given: API request has validation error\\n   416→        when: POST/PUT with invalid body\\n   417→        then: returns {error, details:[{field, message}]} with 400 status\\n   418→      - id: ac-24\\n   419→        given: API request causes state transition error\\n   420→        when: POST action violates state machine\\n   421→        then: returns {error, current, valid_transitions} with 409 status\\n   422→      - id: ac-25\\n   423→        given: client connects to /ws\\n   424→        when: WebSocket connection established\\n   425→        then: receives connected event with {session_id}\\n   426→      - id: ac-26\\n   427→        given: WebSocket connection active\\n   428→        when: client sends command\\n   429→        then: command format is {action, request_id?, payload}\\n   430→      - id: ac-27\\n   431→        given: command received\\n   432→        when: processed\\n   433→        then: \\\"server sends {ack: true, request_id, success, error?}\\\"\\n   434→      - id: ac-28\\n   435→        given: WebSocket connection\\n   436→        when: \\\"client sends {action: 'subscribe', topics: ['files:updates']}\\\"\\n   437→        then: server tracks subscription and sends events for that topic\\n   438→      - id: ac-29\\n   439→        given: file changes in .kspec/\\n   440→        when: WebSocket client subscribed to files:updates\\n   441→        then: \\\"receives event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data: {ref, action}}\\\"\\n   442→      - id: ac-30\\n   443→        given: malformed command received\\n   444→        when: parsed\\n   445→        then: \\\"return {ack: false, error: 'validation_error', details: ...}\\\"\\n   446→      - id: ac-31\\n   447→        given: connection closing\\n   448→        when: close initiated\\n   449→        then: use code 1000 for clean, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error\\n   450→      - id: ac-32\\n   451→        given: server sends to slow client\\n   452→        when: backpressure limit reached\\n   453→        then: pause non-critical broadcasts until drain event\\n   454→      - id: ac-33\\n   455→        given: daemon is shutting down\\n   456→        when: WebSocket connection active\\n   457→        then: receives shutdown event with {reason}, connection closes gracefully\\n   458→    status:\\n   459→      maturity: draft\\n   460→      implementation: in_progress\\n   461→  - _ulid: 01KFHMFJD571JQEE33AKKMEQSJ\\n   462→    slugs:\\n   463→      - web-dashboard\\n   464→    title: Web Dashboard\\n   465→    type: feature\\n   466→    tags:\\n   467→      - svelte\\n   468→      - ui\\n   469→      - dashboard\\n   470→    description: |\\n   471→      SvelteKit-based web interface for viewing and editing specs, tasks, inbox, and session state.\\n   472→      Uses shadcn-svelte components for accessible UI. Connects to daemon via REST API and WebSocket\\n   473→      for real-time updates. Includes WebSocketManager for connection resilience with exponential\\n   474→      backoff reconnection and sequence deduplication.\\n   475→    depends_on:\\n   476→      - \\\"@api-contract\\\"\\n   477→    implements: []\\n   478→    relates_to: []\\n   479→    tests: []\\n   480→    traits:\\n   481→      - \\\"@trait-filterable-list\\\"\\n   482→      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n   483→    notes: []\\n   484→    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:11.366Z\\n   485→    acceptance_criteria:\\n   486→      - id: ac-1\\n   487→        given: daemon is running on configured port (default 3456)\\n   488→        when: browser opens the daemon URL\\n   489→        then: dashboard shows task overview with ready, in_progress, pending_review, blocked, completed\\n   490→          counts\\n   491→      - id: ac-2\\n   492→        given: dashboard is displayed\\n   493→        when: task counts update on server\\n   494→        then: counts animate to new values without page refresh (WebSocket-driven)\\n   495→      - id: ac-3\\n   496→        given: dashboard is displayed\\n   497→        when: user clicks a task count badge\\n   498→        then: navigates to task list filtered by that status\\n   499→      - id: ac-4\\n   500→        given: user is viewing task list\\n   501→        when: list loads\\n   502→        then: shows task title, status badge, priority indicator, spec_ref link, notes count\\n   503→      - id: ac-5\\n   504→        given: user is viewing task list\\n   505→        when: clicking a task row\\n   506→        then: task detail panel opens showing description, notes (chronological), todos, dependencies\\n   507→      - id: ac-6\\n   508→        given: user is viewing task detail\\n   509→        when: task has spec_ref\\n   510→        then: spec reference is clickable link to spec item detail\\n   511→      - id: ac-7\\n   512→        given: user is viewing task detail\\n   513→        when: user clicks Start Task button\\n   514→        then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/start, task status updates, UI reflects change\\n   515→      - id: ac-8\\n   516→        given: user is viewing task detail\\n   517→        when: user types in note textarea and clicks Add Note\\n   518→        then: POST to /api/tasks/:ref/note, note appears in list\\n   519→      - id: ac-9\\n   520→        given: user is viewing task list\\n   521→        when: filter controls are visible\\n   522→        then: can filter by status, type, tag, assignee, automation status\\n   523→      - id: ac-10\\n   524→        given: user applies filter\\n   525→        when: filter selection changes\\n   526→        then: URL updates with query params, list updates without full reload\\n   527→      - id: ac-11\\n   528→        given: user navigates to /items\\n   529→        when: spec tree displays\\n   530→        then: shows hierarchical tree with modules > features > requirements, expand/collapse\\n   531→      - id: ac-12\\n   532→        given: user clicks spec item in tree\\n   533→        when: item detail panel opens\\n   534→        then: shows title, description, acceptance criteria (GWT format), traits, implementation status\\n   535→      - id: ac-13\\n   536→        given: spec item has linked tasks\\n   537→        when: viewing item detail\\n   538→        then: Implementation section shows linked tasks with their status\\n   539→      - id: ac-14\\n   540→        given: spec item has traits\\n   541→        when: viewing item detail\\n   542→        then: Traits section shows trait titles as chips, clickable to trait detail\\n   543→      - id: ac-15\\n   544→        given: user clicks acceptance criterion\\n   545→        when: AC row expands\\n   546→        then: shows full Given/When/Then text with test coverage indicator if available\\n   547→      - id: ac-16\\n   548→        given: user navigates to /inbox\\n   549→        when: inbox list displays\\n   550→        then: shows items ordered by created_at desc with text preview, tags, added_by\\n   551→      - id: ac-17\\n   552→        given: user clicks Add button\\n   553→        when: input field appears\\n   554→        then: user can type text, press Enter to submit\\n   555→      - id: ac-18\\n   556→        given: new inbox item submitted\\n   557→        when: POST succeeds\\n   558→        then: item appears at top of list with animation\\n   559→      - id: ac-19\\n   560→        given: user clicks delete button on item\\n   561→        when: confirmation appears\\n   562→        then: on confirm, item removed from list\\n   563→      - id: ac-20\\n   564→        given: dashboard header area\\n   565→        when: session has focus set\\n   566→        then: displays current focus text prominently\\n   567→      - id: ac-21\\n   568→        given: dashboard sidebar\\n   569→        when: observations exist\\n   570→        then: shows unresolved observations count badge\\n   571→      - id: ac-22\\n   572→        given: user clicks observations badge\\n   573→        when: observations panel opens\\n   574→        then: lists unresolved observations with type icons (friction/success/question/idea)\\n   575→      - id: ac-23\\n   576→        given: user presses Cmd+K (or Ctrl+K)\\n   577→        when: command palette opens\\n   578→        then: shows search input with placeholder\\n   579→      - id: ac-24\\n   580→        given: user types in search box\\n   581→        when: debounced search fires (300ms)\\n   582→        then: results show tasks, items, inbox matching query grouped by type\\n   583→      - id: ac-25\\n   584→        given: search results display\\n   585→        when: user clicks a result\\n   586→        then: navigates to detail view for that item\\n   587→      - id: ac-26\\n   588→        given: browser width < 768px\\n   589→        when: viewing any page\\n   590→        then: layout adapts to single column, sidebar becomes bottom nav\\n   591→      - id: ac-27\\n   592→        given: browser width >= 1024px\\n   593→        when: viewing detail panels\\n   594→        then: detail panel opens as slide-over without navigating away from list\\n   595→      - id: ac-28\\n   596→        given: WebSocket connection drops\\n   597→        when: reconnect logic triggers\\n   598→        then: automatic reconnect with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s)\\n   599→      - id: ac-29\\n   600→        given: WebSocket disconnected for >10s\\n   601→        when: viewing dashboard\\n   602→        then: Connection lost indicator shown\\n   603→      - id: ac-30\\n   604→        given: events received via WebSocket\\n   605→        when: seq <= lastSeqProcessed\\n   606→        then: skip duplicate events (sequence deduplication)\\n   607→      - id: ac-31\\n   608→        given: WebSocket reconnects\\n   609→        when: connection established\\n   610→        then: client resets lastSeqProcessed = -1 (server generates new sequence)\\n   611→      - id: ac-32\\n   612→        given: WebSocket reconnects\\n   613→        when: connection established\\n   614→        then: client re-subscribes to all previous topics\\n   615→      - id: ac-33\\n   616→        given: another client modifies task\\n   617→        when: WebSocket update received\\n   618→        then: task list/detail updates without refresh, subtle highlight animation on changed item\\n   619→    status:\\n   620→      maturity: draft\\n   621→      implementation: implemented\\n   622→  - _ulid: 01KFHMFMN8PNQ78K7X7GATNQ2P\\n   623→    slugs:\\n   624→      - gh-pages-export\\n   625→    title: GitHub Pages Export\\n   626→    type: feature\\n   627→    tags:\\n   628→      - static\\n   629→      - export\\n   630→      - github\\n   631→    description: >\\n   632→      Static site generation from kspec state for hosting read-only views on GitHub Pages.\\n   633→\\n   634→      CI workflow builds JSON snapshot from shadow branch on push, SPA reads this JSON for\\n   635→      rendering.\\n   636→\\n   637→      Enables deep linking to tasks/specs from PRs and issues with data freshness indicator.\\n   638→    depends_on: []\\n   639→    implements: []\\n   640→    relates_to: []\\n   641→    tests: []\\n   642→    traits:\\n   643→      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n   644→      - \\\"@trait-dry-run\\\"\\n   645→    notes: []\\n   646→    created: 2026-01-22T01:18:13.672Z\\n   647→    acceptance_criteria:\\n   648→      - id: ac-1\\n   649→        given: kspec is installed\\n   650→        when: user runs 'kspec export --format json'\\n   651→        then: writes kspec-snapshot.json containing all tasks, items, inbox, meta to stdout or --output path\\n   652→      - id: ac-2\\n   653→        given: export runs\\n   654→        when: output is generated\\n   655→        then: JSON includes exported_at timestamp, version (kspec version), project metadata\\n   656→      - id: ac-3\\n   657→        given: export runs\\n   658→        when: tasks are included\\n   659→        then: each task includes resolved spec_ref title (not just ref string) for display without\\n   660→          resolution\\n   661→      - id: ac-4\\n   662→        given: export runs\\n   663→        when: items are included\\n   664→        then: hierarchical structure preserved, acceptance_criteria expanded, traits resolved to include\\n   665→          inherited ACs\\n   666→      - id: ac-5\\n   667→        given: export runs with --include-validation\\n   668→        when: validation is run\\n   669→        then: JSON includes validation block with error/warning counts and details\\n   670→      - id: ac-6\\n   671→        given: kspec is installed\\n   672→        when: user runs 'kspec export --format html'\\n   673→        then: generates self-contained HTML file with embedded JSON and SPA code\\n   674→      - id: ac-7\\n   675→        given: kspec is installed\\n   676→        when: user runs 'kspec export --dry-run'\\n   677→        then: shows what would be exported without writing files\\n   678→      - id: ac-8\\n   679→        given: push to kspec-meta branch\\n   680→        when: CI workflow triggers\\n   681→        then: runs kspec export, commits to gh-pages branch\\n   682→      - id: ac-9\\n   683→        given: CI workflow runs\\n   684→        when: SPA assets don't exist\\n   685→        then: copies SPA static assets (HTML, JS, CSS) to docs/ alongside JSON\\n   686→      - id: ac-10\\n   687→        given: rapid commits to kspec-meta\\n   688→        when: multiple pushes within 30 seconds\\n   689→        then: CI debounces and runs once with latest state\\n   690→      - id: ac-11\\n   691→        given: user opens gh-pages URL\\n   692→        when: SPA loads\\n   693→        then: fetches kspec-snapshot.json from same origin, renders dashboard\\n   694→      - id: ac-12\\n   695→        given: user navigates to /tasks/@task-slug\\n   696→        when: deep link resolves\\n   697→        then: SPA parses path (history API), shows task detail for that ref\\n   698→      - id: ac-13\\n   699→        given: user navigates to /items/@spec-slug\\n   700→        when: deep link resolves\\n   701→        then: SPA shows spec item detail for that ref\\n   702→      - id: ac-14\\n   703→        given: SPA renders\\n   704→        when: validation data present in snapshot\\n   705→        then: shows validation summary badge (green check or red X with count)\\n   706→      - id: ac-15\\n   707→        given: static export page\\n   708→        when: displayed to user\\n   709→        then: \\\"shows 'Data as of: [timestamp]' indicator prominently\\\"\\n   710→      - id: ac-16\\n   711→        given: viewing task in SPA mode\\n   712→        when: user sees Start Task button area\\n   713→        then: button is disabled with tooltip explaining read-only mode\\n   714→      - id: ac-17\\n   715→        given: viewing inbox in SPA mode\\n   716→        when: Add button area visible\\n   717→        then: button is disabled/hidden\\n   718→      - id: ac-18\\n   719→        given: SPA mode\\n   720→        when: any write action attempted\\n   721→        then: graceful no-op with informative message\\n   722→      - id: ac-19\\n   723→        given: app is built with VITE_STATIC_MODE=true\\n   724→        when: app initializes on page load\\n   725→        then: mode is set to static without attempting daemon health check\\n   726→      - id: ac-20\\n   727→        given: app is in static mode\\n   728→        when: fetching kspec-snapshot.json\\n   729→        then: URL is prefixed with SvelteKit configured base path from $app/paths\\n   730→    status:\\n   731→      maturity: draft\\n   732→      implementation: implemented\\n   733→  - _ulid: 01KFMM8F5WG89H244FXVSRZ35E\\n   734→    slugs:\\n   735→      - cli-serve-commands\\n   736→    title: CLI Serve Commands\\n   737→    type: feature\\n   738→    tags:\\n   739→      - cli\\n   740→      - serve\\n   741→    description: |\\n   742→      CLI commands for managing the daemon server lifecycle. Provides human and script-friendly\\n   743→      interfaces to start, stop, and monitor the daemon.\\n   744→    depends_on:\\n   745→      - \\\"@daemon-server\\\"\\n   746→    implements: []\\n   747→    relates_to: []\\n   748→    tests: []\\n   749→    traits:\\n   750→      - \\\"@trait-json-output\\\"\\n   751→      - \\\"@trait-semantic-exit-codes\\\"\\n   752→      - \\\"@trait-error-guidance\\\"\\n   753→    notes: []\\n   754→    created: 2026-01-22T07:00:00.000Z\\n   755→    acceptance_criteria:\\n   756→      - id: ac-1\\n   757→        given: daemon not running\\n   758→        when: kspec serve executed\\n   759→        then: starts server in foreground, logs to stdout, Ctrl+C stops\\n   760→      - id: ac-2\\n   761→        given: daemon not running\\n   762→        when: kspec serve --daemon executed\\n   763→        then: starts in background, writes PID file, returns immediately with status message\\n   764→      - id: ac-3\\n   765→        given: daemon not running\\n   766→        when: kspec serve --port 8080 executed\\n   767→        then: starts on specified port\\n   768→      - id: ac-4\\n   769→        given: daemon running\\n   770→        when: kspec serve stop executed\\n   771→        then: sends SIGTERM to daemon PID, waits for clean shutdown, removes PID file\\n   772→      - id: ac-5\\n   773→        given: daemon not running\\n   774→        when: kspec serve stop executed\\n   775→        then: outputs 'Daemon not running' with exit code 0 (idempotent)\\n   776→      - id: ac-6\\n   777→        given: any state\\n   778→        when: kspec serve status executed\\n   779→        then: outputs JSON with {running, pid, port, uptime, connections}\\n   780→      - id: ac-7\\n   781→        given: daemon running\\n   782→        when: kspec serve restart executed\\n   783→        then: stops existing daemon, starts new one, preserves port setting\\n   784→      - id: ac-8\\n   785→        given: any state\\n   786→        when: kspec serve logs executed\\n   787→        then: tails daemon log file (.kspec/.daemon.log)\\n   788→      - id: ac-9\\n   789→        given: daemon running\\n   790→        when: kspec serve logs --follow executed\\n   791→        then: streams log output continuously until Ctrl+C\\n   792→      - id: ac-10\\n   793→        given: port already in use\\n   794→        when: kspec serve attempts to start\\n   795→        then: fails with clear error message suggesting --port flag\\n   796→    status:\\n   797→      maturity: draft\\n   798→      implementation: implemented\\n   799→  - _ulid: 01KFQ84FVYMN3Z0HXWZ5AK7CQD\\n   800→    slugs:\\n   801→      - multi-directory-daemon\\n   802→    title: Multi-Directory Daemon Architecture\\n   803→    type: feature\\n   804→    tags:\\n   805→      - daemon\\n   806→      - architecture\\n   807→      - multi-project\\n   808→    description: |\\n   809→      Extends the daemon server to support multiple kspec projects simultaneously from a single\\n   810→      daemon process. Projects are identified via X-Kspec-Dir HTTP header. Enables E2E testing\\n   811→      with isolated fixtures and multi-project development workflows.\\n   812→\\n   813→      Key architectural changes:\\n   814→      - Global daemon with PID/port files at ~/.config/kspec/\\n   815→      - Project context caching with on-demand registration\\n   816→      - Per-project file watchers\\n   817→      - WebSocket connections bound to specific projects\\n   818→\\n   819→      BREAKING CHANGE: PID/port files move from .kspec/.daemon.pid to ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid\\n   820→    depends_on:\\n   821→      - \\\"@daemon-server\\\"\\n   822→      - \\\"@api-contract\\\"\\n   823→    implements: []\\n   824→    relates_to:\\n   825→      - \\\"@cli-serve-commands\\\"\\n   826→    tests: []\\n   827→    traits:\\n   828→      - \\\"@trait-localhost-security\\\"\\n   829→      - \\\"@trait-websocket-protocol\\\"\\n   830→    notes:\\n   831→      - _ulid: 01KFQ84FVZB2CWH7Y4GPQR8M9N\\n   832→        created_at: 2026-01-24T06:00:00.000Z\\n   833→        author: \\\"@claude\\\"\\n   834→        content: |\\n   835→          Design decisions:\\n   836→          - X-Kspec-Dir header for project selection (clean URLs, easy for clients)\\n   837→          - Single bundled web UI (consistent version across projects)\\n   838→          - On-demand project registration (auto-register on first request)\\n   839→          - No memory limit on cached projects (keep until restart)\\n   840→          - Global PID at ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid\\n   841→          - Per-project file watchers\\n   842→          - Backwards compatible (no header = startup cwd project if valid)\\n   843→    created: 2026-01-24T06:00:00.000Z\\n   844→    acceptance_criteria:\\n   845→      - id: ac-1\\n   846→        given: daemon is running\\n   847→        when: request includes X-Kspec-Dir header with valid absolute path\\n   848→        then: daemon uses that project's context for the request\\n   849→      - id: ac-2\\n   850→        given: daemon started from directory with .kspec/\\n   851→        when: request has no X-Kspec-Dir header\\n   852→        then: daemon uses startup directory's project as default\\n   853→      - id: ac-3\\n   854→        given: daemon started from directory without .kspec/\\n   855→        when: request without X-Kspec-Dir arrives\\n   856→        then: return 400 with error \\\"No default project configured. Specify X-Kspec-Dir header.\\\"\\n   857→      - id: ac-4\\n   858→        given: request specifies unknown project path\\n   859→        when: path is valid kspec project\\n   860→        then: daemon auto-registers and caches project context\\n   861→      - id: ac-5\\n   862→        given: request specifies invalid path (no .kspec/)\\n   863→        when: request processed\\n   864→        then: return 400 with error \\\"Invalid kspec project - .kspec/ not found at <path>\\\"\\n   865→      - id: ac-6\\n   866→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value\\n   867→        when: path is relative\\n   868→        then: reject with 400 and error \\\"Path must be absolute\\\"\\n   869→      - id: ac-7\\n   870→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value\\n   871→        when: path contains \\\"..\\\" segments\\n   872→        then: reject with 400 and error \\\"Path must not contain parent traversal\\\"\\n   873→      - id: ac-8\\n   874→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header value\\n   875→        when: normalized path differs from provided path\\n   876→        then: use normalized path for registration (resolve \\\".\\\" segments, remove trailing slashes, do NOT\\n   877→          resolve symlinks)\\n   878→      - id: ac-8b\\n   879→        given: X-Kspec-Dir points to path with insufficient read permissions\\n   880→        when: request processed\\n   881→        then: return 403 with error \\\"Permission denied - cannot read <path>\\\"\\n   882→      - id: ac-9\\n   883→        given: no daemon running\\n   884→        when: kspec serve start runs from any directory\\n   885→        then: daemon starts and writes PID to ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid and port to\\n   886→          ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port\\n   887→      - id: ac-9b\\n   888→        given: ~/.config/kspec/ does not exist\\n   889→        when: daemon starts\\n   890→        then: create directory with mode 0755 before writing PID/port files\\n   891→      - id: ac-9c\\n   892→        given: ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port exists but contains invalid content\\n   893→        when: CLI reads port\\n   894→        then: return error \\\"Invalid daemon port file\\\" and suggest \\\"kspec serve stop && kspec serve start\\\"\\n   895→      - id: ac-10\\n   896→        given: daemon running on port 3456\\n   897→        when: kspec serve start runs from different directory\\n   898→        then: command exits with success and outputs \\\"Daemon already running on port 3456\\\" (no second\\n   899→          instance started)\\n   900→      - id: ac-10b\\n   901→        given: two kspec serve start commands run concurrently (neither has written PID yet)\\n   902→        when: both check for running daemon\\n   903→        then: only one daemon starts (use file lock on PID file)\\n   904→      - id: ac-11\\n   905→        given: daemon running\\n   906→        when: kspec serve stop runs from any directory\\n   907→        then: daemon stops and removes global PID and port files\\n   908→      - id: ac-12\\n   909→        given: daemon running\\n   910→        when: kspec serve status runs\\n   911→        then: shows daemon status with port, uptime, and list of registered projects with their paths\\n   912→      - id: ac-13\\n   913→        given: CLI needs to connect to daemon\\n   914→        when: daemon is running\\n   915→        then: CLI reads port from ~/.config/kspec/daemon.port\\n   916→      - id: ac-14\\n   917→        given: daemon restarts\\n   918→        when: first request for a project arrives\\n   919→        then: project is re-registered automatically (same as initial registration)\\n   920→      - id: ac-15\\n   921→        given: daemon running with registered projects\\n   922→        when: daemon restarts\\n   923→        then: registered project list is empty (no persistence across restarts)\\n   924→      - id: ac-16\\n   925→        given: two concurrent requests for unregistered project with same path\\n   926→        when: processed\\n   927→        then: both succeed and share the same registered project context (no duplicate watchers)\\n   928→      - id: ac-17\\n   929→        given: project is registered\\n   930→        when: files change in project's .kspec/\\n   931→        then: file watcher triggers events scoped to that project\\n   932→      - id: ac-18\\n   933→        given: multiple projects registered\\n   934→        when: Project A changes\\n   935→        then: only Project A's WebSocket subscribers receive updates\\n   936→      - id: ac-19\\n   937→        given: project watcher creation fails due to OS limits (ulimit)\\n   938→        when: error occurs\\n   939→        then: project registration fails with 503 and error \\\"Unable to watch project - resource limit\\n   940→          reached\\\"\\n   941→      - id: ac-20\\n   942→        given: registered project's .kspec/ directory is deleted\\n   943→        when: next request arrives for that project\\n   944→        then: return 404 and unregister project automatically\\n   945→      - id: ac-21\\n   946→        given: WebSocket client connects with X-Kspec-Dir header during handshake\\n   947→        when: connection established\\n   948→        then: connection is bound to that project for its lifetime and only receives events from that\\n   949→          project\\n   950→      - id: ac-21b\\n   951→        given: WebSocket connection is established and bound to project\\n   952→        when: client attempts to change project\\n   953→        then: project binding is immutable - client must disconnect and reconnect with new header\\n   954→      - id: ac-22\\n   955→        given: WebSocket client connects without X-Kspec-Dir header\\n   956→        when: default project exists\\n   957→        then: connection is bound to default project\\n   958→      - id: ac-23\\n   959→        given: WebSocket client connects without X-Kspec-Dir header\\n   960→        when: no default project\\n   961→        then: connection is rejected with close code 4000 and reason \\\"No project specified\\\"\\n   962→      - id: ac-24\\n   963→        given: multi-project mode\\n   964→        when: any API endpoint is called\\n   965→        then: response data is scoped to the request's project (no cross-project data leakage)\\n   966→      - id: ac-25\\n   967→        given: web UI loads\\n   968→        when: more than one project registered\\n   969→        then: project selector is shown listing all registered projects\\n   970→      - id: ac-26\\n   971→        given: user selects project in UI\\n   972→        when: selection changes\\n   973→        then: all subsequent API requests include that project's path in X-Kspec-Dir header\\n   974→      - id: ac-27\\n   975→        given: UI is showing project data\\n   976→        when: different project selected\\n   977→        then: UI reloads data from newly selected project\\n   978→      - id: ac-28\\n   979→        given: GET /api/projects\\n   980→        when: called\\n   981→        then: returns list of registered projects with paths, registration time, and watcher status\\n   982→      - id: ac-29\\n   983→        given: POST /api/projects\\n   984→        when: called with {path string} body\\n   985→        then: manually registers a project (for explicit registration use cases)\\n   986→      - id: ac-30\\n   987→        given: DELETE /api/projects/:encodedPath\\n   988→        when: called\\n   989→        then: unregisters project and stops its file watcher\\n   990→      - id: ac-8c\\n   991→        given: X-Kspec-Dir header contains symlinked path\\n   992→        when: path resolves to same directory as another registered project via symlink\\n   993→        then: paths are treated as separate projects (symlinks are NOT resolved during normalization)\\n   994→      - id: ac-20b\\n   995→        given: daemon started from directory with .kspec/ which is later deleted\\n   996→        when: request without X-Kspec-Dir arrives after default project .kspec/ deleted\\n   997→        then: return 400 with error 'Default project no longer valid. Specify X-Kspec-Dir header.'\\n   998→      - id: ac-11b\\n   999→        given: daemon is shutting down\\n  1000→        when: shutdown signal received\\n  1001→        then: all project watchers are stopped and all WebSocket connections are closed before process exits\\n  1002→    status:\\n  1003→      maturity: draft\\n  1004→      implementation: implemented\\n  1005→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF2ZKQRVKRZYZVGP10EN\\n  1006→    slugs:\\n  1007→      - ui-design-system\\n  1008→    title: UI Design System\\n  1009→    type: feature\\n  1010→    tags: []\\n  1011→    description: |\\n  1012→      Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n  1013→      Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n  1014→      keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n  1015→      across all views.\\n  1016→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1017→      - id: ac-1\\n  1018→        given: |\\n  1019→          The web UI app.css file\\n  1020→        when: |\\n  1021→          imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n  1022→        then: |\\n  1023→          All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\n  1024→          are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n  1025→      - id: ac-2\\n  1026→        given: |\\n  1027→          A component using design tokens\\n  1028→        when: |\\n  1029→          The dark theme tokens are applied\\n  1030→        then: |\\n  1031→          oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\n  1032→          pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\n  1033→          are visually distinct\\n  1034→      - id: ac-3\\n  1035→        given: |\\n  1036→          A view with loading states\\n  1037→        when: |\\n  1038→          Content is loading\\n  1039→        then: |\\n  1040→          Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n  1041→      - id: ac-4\\n  1042→        given: |\\n  1043→          An active agent task card\\n  1044→        when: |\\n  1045→          The agent is working\\n  1046→        then: |\\n  1047→          Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n  1048→    depends_on: []\\n  1049→    implements: []\\n  1050→    relates_to: []\\n  1051→    tests: []\\n  1052→    traits: []\\n  1053→    notes: []\\n  1054→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.719Z\\n  1055→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF3J5HTWWDRHWM3C42DJ\\n  1056→    slugs:\\n  1057→      - ui-app-shell\\n  1058→    title: App Shell and Navigation\\n  1059→    type: feature\\n  1060→    tags: []\\n  1061→    description: |\\n  1062→      Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar\\n  1063→      with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.\\n  1064→      Preserve existing functionality during migration.\\n  1065→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1066→      - id: ac-1\\n  1067→        given: |\\n  1068→          The web UI loaded in daemon mode\\n  1069→        when: |\\n  1070→          The app shell renders\\n  1071→        then: |\\n  1072→          A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),\\n  1073→          Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),\\n  1074→          Config (Workflows, Settings)\\n  1075→      - id: ac-2\\n  1076→        given: |\\n  1077→          Sidebar navigation items\\n  1078→        when: |\\n  1079→          Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)\\n  1080→        then: |\\n  1081→          Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items\\n  1082→      - id: ac-3\\n  1083→        given: |\\n  1084→          The /items route\\n  1085→        when: |\\n  1086→          A user navigates to /items\\n  1087→        then: |\\n  1088→          They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters\\n  1089→      - id: ac-4\\n  1090→        given: |\\n  1091→          The Observations nav item\\n  1092→        when: |\\n  1093→          There are zero unresolved observations\\n  1094→        then: |\\n  1095→          The nav item is still visible (not hidden)\\n  1096→    depends_on: []\\n  1097→    implements: []\\n  1098→    relates_to: []\\n  1099→    tests: []\\n  1100→    traits: []\\n  1101→    notes: []\\n  1102→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.738Z\\n  1103→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF40T8KCJHMT0JVYMVV7\\n  1104→    slugs:\\n  1105→      - ui-task-board\\n  1106→    title: Task Board (Kanban)\\n  1107→    type: feature\\n  1108→    tags: []\\n  1109→    description: |\\n  1110→      Kanban-style task board with columns mapping to kspec task states.\\n  1111→      Active Fleet row shows currently running agent work with live output.\\n  1112→      Task cards show key metadata, clicking opens detail modal.\\n  1113→      Not drag-and-drop — tasks transition via agents/CLI.\\n  1114→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1115→      - id: ac-1\\n  1116→        given: |\\n  1117→          Tasks in various states\\n  1118→        when: |\\n  1119→          The task board renders\\n  1120→        then: |\\n  1121→          Tasks are distributed into columns: Backlog (pending, manual_only/unassessed),\\n  1122→          Ready (pending, eligible), In Progress (in_progress, needs_work),\\n  1123→          Review (pending_review), Done (completed recent), with blocked and cancelled\\n  1124→          handled as sections/indicators\\n  1125→      - id: ac-2\\n  1126→        given: |\\n  1127→          A task card on the board\\n  1128→        when: |\\n  1129→          The card renders\\n  1130→        then: |\\n  1131→          It shows priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (mono), spec ref link,\\n  1132→          and metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n  1133→      - id: ac-3\\n  1134→        given: |\\n  1135→          A task card\\n  1136→        when: |\\n  1137→          The user clicks it\\n  1138→        then: |\\n  1139→          A detail modal opens showing full task info: title, description, status,\\n  1140→          priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos,\\n  1141→          automation status, VCS info (branch, PR link), plan ref, session link\\n  1142→      - id: ac-4\\n  1143→        given: |\\n  1144→          Agents actively working on tasks (dispatch running)\\n  1145→        when: |\\n  1146→          The task board renders\\n  1147→        then: |\\n  1148→          An Active Fleet row appears at the top showing cards with task title,\\n  1149→          agent name, elapsed time with pulse indicator, and last few lines of output\\n  1150→      - id: ac-5\\n  1151→        given: |\\n  1152→          The task board with WebSocket connected\\n  1153→        when: |\\n  1154→          A task state changes\\n  1155→        then: |\\n  1156→          The board updates in real-time without page refresh\\n  1157→      - id: ac-6\\n  1158→        given: |\\n  1159→          The task detail modal in daemon mode\\n  1160→        when: |\\n  1161→          The user clicks action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note)\\n  1162→        then: |\\n  1163→          The corresponding task transition or mutation is executed via API\\n  1164→    depends_on: []\\n  1165→    implements: []\\n  1166→    relates_to: []\\n  1167→    tests: []\\n  1168→    traits: []\\n  1169→    notes: []\\n  1170→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.752Z\\n  1171→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF4FP4GY593BCW3XZHQM\\n  1172→    slugs:\\n  1173→      - ui-session-stream\\n  1174→    title: Session Stream View\\n  1175→    type: feature\\n  1176→    tags: []\\n  1177→    description: |\\n  1178→      View for watching agent work — both historical and live. Renders structured\\n  1179→      session events (messages, tool calls, thinking blocks) from events.jsonl.\\n  1180→      Live sessions show streaming text with periodic structured refresh.\\n  1181→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1182→      - id: ac-1\\n  1183→        given: |\\n  1184→          A completed session with events.jsonl\\n  1185→        when: |\\n  1186→          The user navigates to /sessions/:id\\n  1187→        then: |\\n  1188→          The session events render as structured blocks: agent messages (markdown),\\n  1189→          tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), and thinking blocks\\n  1190→          (collapsed by default, expandable)\\n  1191→      - id: ac-2\\n  1192→        given: |\\n  1193→          An active session with streaming output\\n  1194→        when: |\\n  1195→          The user views the session\\n  1196→        then: |\\n  1197→          Live text streams in real-time via agent_text_chunk WebSocket events,\\n  1198→          with periodic structured refresh from events.jsonl\\n  1199→      - id: ac-3\\n  1200→        given: |\\n  1201→          The session stream view\\n  1202→        when: |\\n  1203→          New content arrives while auto-scrolling\\n  1204→        then: |\\n  1205→          The view auto-scrolls to follow new content, pauses when user scrolls up\\n  1206→          (>100px from bottom), and resumes when scrolled back. A \\\"jump to bottom\\\"\\n  1207→          button appears when paused.\\n  1208→      - id: ac-4\\n  1209→        given: |\\n  1210→          The session stream view\\n  1211→        when: |\\n  1212→          A session context panel is shown on the left\\n  1213→        then: |\\n  1214→          It displays session metadata, spec context with AC checklist,\\n  1215→          files changed during session, and budget info\\n  1216→    depends_on: []\\n  1217→    implements: []\\n  1218→    relates_to: []\\n  1219→    tests: []\\n  1220→    traits: []\\n  1221→    notes: []\\n  1222→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.767Z\\n  1223→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF4YR57EJQTNSHFQKZHE\\n  1224→    slugs:\\n  1225→      - ui-agent-dispatch\\n  1226→    title: Agent and Dispatch View\\n  1227→    type: feature\\n  1228→    tags: []\\n  1229→    description: |\\n  1230→      View showing agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped),\\n  1231→      and active invocations with links to session streams.\\n  1232→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1233→      - id: ac-1\\n  1234→        given: |\\n  1235→          The /agents route\\n  1236→        when: |\\n  1237→          Agent definitions exist in meta\\n  1238→        then: |\\n  1239→          Each agent shows name, triggers, active invocation count, and completed count\\n  1240→      - id: ac-2\\n  1241→        given: |\\n  1242→          The dispatch engine is running\\n  1243→        when: |\\n  1244→          The agents page renders\\n  1245→        then: |\\n  1246→          Dispatch status shows as running with a stop button, and active invocations\\n  1247→          show task ref, elapsed time, and link to session stream\\n  1248→      - id: ac-3\\n  1249→        given: |\\n  1250→          The dispatch engine is stopped\\n  1251→        when: |\\n  1252→          The agents page renders\\n  1253→        then: |\\n  1254→          Dispatch status shows as stopped with no active invocations\\n  1255→    depends_on: []\\n  1256→    implements: []\\n  1257→    relates_to: []\\n  1258→    tests: []\\n  1259→    traits: []\\n  1260→    notes: []\\n  1261→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.782Z\\n  1262→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF5CPD38NH05CPXG4NFY\\n  1263→    slugs:\\n  1264→      - ui-session-history\\n  1265→    title: Session History\\n  1266→    type: feature\\n  1267→    tags: []\\n  1268→    description: |\\n  1269→      List view of past agent sessions with filtering and navigation to session detail.\\n  1270→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1271→      - id: ac-1\\n  1272→        given: |\\n  1273→          Sessions exist on disk\\n  1274→        when: |\\n  1275→          The user navigates to /sessions\\n  1276→        then: |\\n  1277→          A list of sessions shows ID, agent type, task ref, status,\\n  1278→          duration, and age, sorted by most recent first\\n  1279→      - id: ac-2\\n  1280→        given: |\\n  1281→          The session list\\n  1282→        when: |\\n  1283→          The user clicks a session\\n  1284→        then: |\\n  1285→          They navigate to /sessions/:id showing the session stream view\\n  1286→    depends_on: []\\n  1287→    implements: []\\n  1288→    relates_to: []\\n  1289→    tests: []\\n  1290→    traits: []\\n  1291→    notes: []\\n  1292→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.796Z\\n  1293→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF5VWDHKVSJ51JSZDSPN\\n  1294→    slugs:\\n  1295→      - ui-inbox-enhanced\\n  1296→    title: Enhanced Inbox View\\n  1297→    type: feature\\n  1298→    tags: []\\n  1299→    description: |\\n  1300→      Enhanced inbox with triage status inline, quick actions, filtering, and bulk selection.\\n  1301→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1302→      - id: ac-1\\n  1303→        given: |\\n  1304→          Inbox items with varying triage states\\n  1305→        when: |\\n  1306→          The inbox view renders\\n  1307→        then: |\\n  1308→          Each item shows triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n  1309→          with quick triage action links\\n  1310→      - id: ac-2\\n  1311→        given: |\\n  1312→          The inbox view\\n  1313→        when: |\\n  1314→          The user applies filters (status, tags, age)\\n  1315→        then: |\\n  1316→          The list filters accordingly\\n  1317→    depends_on: []\\n  1318→    implements: []\\n  1319→    relates_to: []\\n  1320→    tests: []\\n  1321→    traits: []\\n  1322→    notes: []\\n  1323→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.811Z\\n  1324→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF6C8W98RNSGH5V0EM4G\\n  1325→    slugs:\\n  1326→      - ui-plans-view\\n  1327→    title: Plans View\\n  1328→    type: feature\\n  1329→    tags: []\\n  1330→    description: |\\n  1331→      View for browsing plan records with progress tracking via linked specs and tasks.\\n  1332→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1333→      - id: ac-1\\n  1334→        given: |\\n  1335→          Plan records exist\\n  1336→        when: |\\n  1337→          The user navigates to /plans\\n  1338→        then: |\\n  1339→          Each plan shows title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts,\\n  1340→          and progress based on task completion status\\n  1341→    depends_on: []\\n  1342→    implements: []\\n  1343→    relates_to: []\\n  1344→    tests: []\\n  1345→    traits: []\\n  1346→    notes: []\\n  1347→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.828Z\\n  1348→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF6TWXS4Z07QE6R2JEG8\\n  1349→    slugs:\\n  1350→      - ui-validation-view\\n  1351→    title: Validation and Alignment View\\n  1352→    type: feature\\n  1353→    tags: []\\n  1354→    description: |\\n  1355→      View showing validation results, alignment statistics, and issues.\\n  1356→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1357→      - id: ac-1\\n  1358→        given: |\\n  1359→          The user navigates to /validate\\n  1360→        when: |\\n  1361→          Validation data loads\\n  1362→        then: |\\n  1363→          Summary shows error count, warning count, valid item count.\\n  1364→          Alignment section shows spec coverage %, AC coverage %,\\n  1365→          orphaned tasks/specs counts. Issues list grouped by severity.\\n  1366→    depends_on: []\\n  1367→    implements: []\\n  1368→    relates_to: []\\n  1369→    tests: []\\n  1370→    traits: []\\n  1371→    notes: []\\n  1372→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.842Z\\n  1373→  - _ulid: 01KJXSVF7944GT0W021545WRPK\\n  1374→    slugs:\\n  1375→      - ui-dashboard-overview\\n  1376→    title: Dashboard Overview\\n  1377→    type: feature\\n  1378→    tags: []\\n  1379→    description: |\\n  1380→      Home view answering \\\"what's happening right now?\\\" with active work,\\n  1381→      status summary, recent activity, and needs-attention aggregation.\\n  1382→    acceptance_criteria:\\n  1383→      - id: ac-1\\n  1384→        given: |\\n  1385→          The user navigates to /\\n  1386→        when: |\\n  1387→          The dashboard renders\\n  1388→        then: |\\n  1389→          Active work section shows currently running agent tasks (if any),\\n  1390→          status summary shows clickable count cards per status,\\n  1391→          needs-attention section aggregates untriaged inbox, unresolved observations,\\n  1392→          validation warnings, and blocked tasks\\n  1393→    depends_on: []\\n  1394→    implements: []\\n  1395→    relates_to: []\\n  1396→    tests: []\\n  1397→    traits: []\\n  1398→    notes: []\\n  1399→    created: 2026-03-05T01:30:02.857Z\\n  1400→\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":{\"path\":\"blobs/000253-content-0-content-text-bce2291e-4bab-424e-b0ca-c80a9259ff47.blob\",\"bytes\":66343,\"sha256\":\"c572b584a3fb5401d73a6c110c55b5c5d4aa635d548773e1a477032e99cfc8a2\",\"truncated\":true,\"preview\":\"```\\n     1→_ulid: 01KFHMF5ZS4RD70JBQNGBQJVFY\\n     2→slugs:\\n     3→  - web-ui\\n     4→title: Web UI System\\n     5→type: module\\n     6→status:\\n     7→  maturity: draft\\n     8→  implementation: implemented\\n     9→description: >\\n    10→  Web-based interface for viewing, editing, and managing kspec state. Includes three deployment\\n    11→  modes:\\n    12→\\n    13→  1. Local daemon mode - Elysia.js server on Bun with WebSocket for real-time updates\\n    14→\\n    15→  2. Web dashboard - Sv...\"}}}]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:264:{\"ts\":1772684346099,\"seq\":263,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01K8UWbuvRnRYJvSXf1agkTG\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call\",\"rawInput\":{\"command\":\"find /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui -type f \\\\( -name \\\"*.md\\\" -o -name \\\"*.txt\\\" \\\\) 2>/dev/null | xargs grep -l \\\"design\\\\|wireframe\\\\|token\\\\|component\\\\|architecture\\\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | grep -v \\\".git\\\" | head -15\"},\"status\":\"pending\",\"title\":\"find /home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui -type f \\\\( -name \\\"*.md\\\" -o -name \\\"*.txt\\\" \\\\) 2>/dev/null | xargs grep -l \\\"design\\\\|wireframe\\\\|token\\\\|component\\\\|architecture\\\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | grep -v \\\".git\\\" | head -15\",\"kind\":\"execute\",\"content\":[]}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:313:{\"ts\":1772684401237,\"seq\":312,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolResponse\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"prompt\":\"Read the file .kspec/artifacts/ui-revamp-plan.md completely. I need the full architectural context and wireframes for the UI revamp plan, especially any details about the design system, token architecture, and component structure.\",\"agentId\":\"a7bcb35\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Excellent! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report of the UI revamp plan.\\n\\n## UI Revamp Plan - Complete Architectural Context\\n\\nI've thoroughly reviewed the UI/UX revamp plan for the kynetic-spec project. Here's the complete architectural context:\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nThe UI revamp plan (plan ID: `01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2`) defines a comprehensive redesign of the web UI across 10 major feature areas, with supporting design system and component architecture.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Design System Architecture\\n\\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n\\n**Token Structure:**\\n- **Color System**: OKLCH color space for perceptual uniformity\\n- **16 Design Tokens** (oklch format with lightness/chroma/hue):\\n  - Background, Foreground, Card, Card-foreground\\n  - Popover, Popover-foreground\\n  - Primary, Primary-foreground\\n  - Secondary, Secondary-foreground\\n  - Muted, Muted-foreground\\n  - Accent, Accent-foreground\\n  - Destructive\\n  - Border, Input, Ring\\n\\n- **5 Chart Colors** (for data visualization)\\n- **8 Sidebar-specific Tokens** (theme variants for navigation)\\n\\n**Dark Theme Support:**\\nThe tokens automatically swap when the `.dark` class is applied, providing full dark mode support with oklch values optimized for contrast and readability.\\n\\n**Current Status:**\\n- Tailwind @theme inline extensions already mapped (lines 76-112 in app.css)\\n- Variables system uses CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- Base layer styling established (border-border, outline-ring/50, bg-background, text-foreground)\\n\\n**Spacing:** CSS variables calculated as `--radius: 0.625rem` with 4 radius tokens:\\n- `--radius-sm` (0.625rem - 4px)\\n- `--radius-md` (0.625rem - 2px)\\n- `--radius-lg` (0.625rem)\\n- `--radius-xl` (0.625rem + 4px)\\n\\n**Status Color Mappings** (from spec):\\n- `pending` = amber\\n- `in_progress` = orange\\n- `pending_review` = blue\\n- `needs_work` = yellow\\n- `completed` = emerald\\n- `blocked` = red\\n- `cancelled` = gray\\n\\n**Animations:**\\n- Shimmer animation for skeleton loaders (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n- Breathing/pulse animation for active agent task cards (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Component Architecture\\n\\n**Current Component Structure** (`/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`):\\n\\n**Layout Components:**\\n- `Sidebar.svelte` - Collapsible navigation sidebar with grouped sections\\n- `MobileNav.svelte` - Bottom navigation for mobile (< 768px)\\n- `CommandPalette.svelte` - Global command/search palette (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K)\\n- `ConnectionStatus.svelte` - WebSocket connection indicator\\n\\n**Feature Components:**\\n- `ItemDetail.svelte` - Spec item detail viewer\\n- `ItemTree.svelte` - Hierarchical spec item tree\\n- `TaskList.svelte` - Task list with filtering\\n- `TaskDetail.svelte` - Task detail view (legacy)\\n- `TaskDetailPanel.svelte` - Task detail slide-over panel\\n- `TaskFilters.svelte` - Filter controls for task list\\n- `ProjectSelector.svelte` - Multi-project selector (for multi-directory daemon mode)\\n\\n**UI Primitives** (`/lib/components/ui/`):\\n- Shadcn-svelte components: Accordion, Badge, Button, Card, Dialog, Dropdown-menu, Input, Label, Popover, Select, Sheet, Sidebar, Table, Tabs, Toast, Tooltip, etc.\\n\\n**Banner Components:**\\n- `ReadOnlyBanner.svelte` - Static mode indicator with \\\"data freshness\\\" timestamp\\n\\n---\\n\\n### App Shell and Navigation\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n- Main layout file: `+layout.svelte` (SvelteKit root layout)\\n- Uses `SidebarProvider` and `SidebarInset` from shadcn-svelte\\n- Desktop sidebar hidden on mobile (`hidden md:block`)\\n- Responsive inset with main content area (`flex-1 overflow-auto`)\\n\\n**Sidebar Grouping** (planned):\\n```\\nWork\\n  - Dashboard\\n  - Tasks\\n  - Agents\\n  - Sessions\\n\\nSpecs\\n  - Specs\\n  - Plans\\n  - Validate\\n\\nCapture\\n  - Inbox\\n  - Observations\\n  - Triage\\n\\nConfig\\n  - Workflows\\n  - Settings\\n```\\n\\n**Badge Counts:**\\n- Inbox items count\\n- Unresolved observations count\\n- Pending review task count\\n\\n**Current Routes:**\\n- `/` - Dashboard\\n- `/items` - Specs (should redirect `/items` → `/specs`)\\n- `/tasks` - Task list\\n- `/inbox` - Inbox\\n- `/observations` - Observations\\n- `/triage` - Triage view\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Feature Specifications (10 Areas)\\n\\n#### 1. **UI Design System** (`@ui-design-system`)\\n- Port imgen's design token architecture into Tailwind\\n- Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, animation keyframes\\n- **AC Focus**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, 3 font families as Tailwind utilities\\n- Dark theme with status colors\\n- Loading shimmer animations\\n- Agent task card breathing/pulse animations\\n\\n#### 2. **App Shell and Navigation** (`@ui-app-shell`)\\n- Restructure +layout.svelte with grouped sidebar navigation\\n- Migrate Sidebar.svelte to grouped sections\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate 3 existing task detail implementations\\n\\n#### 3. **Task Board (Kanban)** (`@ui-task-board`)\\n- Kanban-style columns mapping to task states:\\n  - **Backlog**: pending (manual_only/unassessed)\\n  - **Ready**: pending (eligible)\\n  - **In Progress**: in_progress, needs_work\\n  - **Review**: pending_review\\n  - **Done**: completed (recent)\\n  - **Blocked/Cancelled**: sections/indicators\\n\\n- **Task Card Elements**: Priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (monospace), spec ref link, metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n- **Detail Modal**: Full task info with title, description, status, priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos, automation status, VCS info, plan ref, session link\\n- **Active Fleet Row**: Shows currently running agent tasks with title, agent name, elapsed time (with pulse indicator), last few lines of output\\n- **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven board updates via `tasks:updates` topic\\n- **Mutations**: Task action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note) execute via API\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisite**: \\n- Daemon must return `type` and `automation` fields in task list API response\\n- Build components: KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal, ActiveFleetRow\\n\\n#### 4. **Session Stream View** (`@ui-session-stream`)\\n- View for watching agent work (historical and live)\\n- Renders structured session events from `events.jsonl`\\n- **Two-tier rendering**:\\n  - Structured events from `events.jsonl` (history)\\n  - `agent_text_chunk` WebSocket events (live text)\\n  \\n- **Event Types**: Agent messages (markdown), tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), thinking blocks (collapsed by default)\\n- **Live Streaming**: Real-time text via WebSocket with periodic structured refresh\\n- **Auto-scroll**: Follow new content, pause when user scrolls up (>100px from bottom), resume when scrolled back, \\\"jump to bottom\\\" button when paused\\n- **Session Context Panel**: Session metadata, spec context with AC checklist, files changed, budget info\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisites**:\\n- Build GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events` endpoints\\n- Build components: SessionStream, ChatMessage, ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock\\n\\n#### 5. **Agent and Dispatch View** (`@ui-agent-dispatch`)\\n- Shows agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped)\\n- Active invocations with links to session streams\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/agent/dispatch/status` and GET `/api/agent/status` endpoints\\n- Subscribe to `agents` WebSocket topic for real-time updates\\n- Components: AgentList, DispatchStatus, InvocationCard\\n\\n#### 6. **Session History** (`@ui-session-history`)\\n- List view of past agent sessions\\n- Display: ID, agent type, task ref, status, duration, age (sorted by most recent first)\\n- Filtering support\\n- Navigate to session detail (session stream view)\\n- Depends on GET `/api/sessions` endpoint from ui-session-stream work\\n\\n#### 7. **Enhanced Inbox View** (`@ui-inbox-enhanced`)\\n- Triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n- Quick triage action links\\n- Filter controls (status, tags, age)\\n- Keep existing add/delete functionality\\n\\n#### 8. **Plans View** (`@ui-plans-view`)\\n- Browse plan records with progress tracking\\n- Display: Title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts, progress (based on task completion)\\n- **Daemon Prerequisite**: Build GET `/api/plans` endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans)\\n\\n#### 9. **Validation and Alignment View** (`@ui-validation-view`)\\n- Validation results, alignment statistics, issues\\n- Summary: Error count, warning count, valid item count\\n- Alignment section: Spec coverage %, AC coverage %, orphaned tasks/specs counts\\n- Issues list grouped by severity\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/validate` and GET `/api/alignment` endpoints\\n\\n#### 10. **Dashboard Overview** (`@ui-dashboard-overview`)\\n- Home view: \\\"What's happening right now?\\\"\\n- **Active work section**: Currently running agent tasks\\n- **Status summary**: Clickable count cards per status\\n- **Needs-attention section**: Aggregates:\\n  - Untriaged inbox items\\n  - Unresolved observations\\n  - Validation warnings\\n  - Blocked tasks\\n- Build last (reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board)\\n- No aggregated activity API needed; merge recent data client-side\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n**Design System:**\\n- Set up isolated clone first\\n- Port imgen's full `token-contract.css` into Tailwind @theme inline in app.css\\n- Start with token bridge pilot on dashboard page to validate approach\\n- Create modular CSS files: `tokens.css`, `animations.css`, `typography.css` in `lib/ds/`\\n- Establish loading skeleton and error boundary patterns\\n\\n**App Shell:**\\n- Restructure `+layout.svelte` with new sidebar component\\n- Migrate existing Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate three existing task detail implementations\\n- Ensure all existing routes continue working\\n\\n**Daemon API Changes Required:**\\n- Task list API: Add `type` and `automation` fields to response\\n- Task mutations: Build POST endpoints for `/api/tasks/:ref/start`, `/api/tasks/:ref/submit`, `/api/tasks/:ref/complete`, `/api/tasks/:ref/block`\\n- Sessions: Add GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events`\\n- Plans: Add GET `/api/plans` endpoint\\n\\n**WebSocket Topics:**\\n- `tasks:updates` - Task state changes\\n- `agents` - Agent dispatch status and text chunks\\n- `files:updates` - File change notifications\\n\\n**Dependencies Between Features:**\\n```\\nui-design-system (foundation)\\n├── ui-app-shell\\n├── ui-task-board\\n├── ui-dashboard-overview\\n└── ui-session-stream\\n    ├── ui-session-history\\n    └── ui-agent-dispatch\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Technology Stack\\n\\n- **Framework**: SvelteKit (Svelte 5 with runes)\\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 with @theme inline\\n- **UI Components**: shadcn-svelte\\n- **Color Space**: OKLCH (perceptual)\\n- **Real-time**: WebSocket (topic-based pub/sub)\\n- **State Management**: Svelte runes (reactive)\\n- **Animation**: CSS keyframes with `prefers-reduced-motion` gates\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Acceptance Criteria Highlights\\n\\n1. **Design System**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing values, 7 z-index, 3 font families available as Tailwind utilities\\n2. **Dark Theme**: Status colors visually distinct (amber, orange, blue, yellow, emerald, red, gray)\\n3. **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven without page refresh\\n4. **Mobile Responsive**: Sidebar → bottom nav on small screens, detail panels on large screens (≥1024px)\\n5. **Command Palette**: Global search (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K) with results grouped by type\\n6. **WebSocket Resilience**: Exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s), sequence deduplication\\n7. **Agent Work Visibility**: Active Fleet row with elapsed time, pulse indicator, live output streaming\\n\\n---\\n\\n### File Locations\\n\\n- **Plan Record**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml` (lines 7613-8133)\\n- **App CSS (Design Tokens)**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n- **Layout**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/routes/+layout.svelte`\\n- **Tailwind Config**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/tailwind.config.js`\\n- **Components**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`\\n- **UI Primitives**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ui/`\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a complete redesign roadmap with clear feature boundaries, specific acceptance criteria, daemon API requirements, and implementation guidance for modernizing the kspec web UI with a cohesive design system and improved user experience.\"}],\"totalDurationMs\":74652,\"totalTokens\":59766,\"totalToolUseCount\":21,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1251,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":54929,\"output_tokens\":3586,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1251,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"}},\"toolName\":\"Task\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01ThiD6dTsa1F73oouG6F7np\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\"}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59/events.jsonl:314:{\"ts\":1772684401239,\"seq\":313,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJY3FGB4W881DYXQ42PQHA59\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Task\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01ThiD6dTsa1F73oouG6F7np\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"rawOutput\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Excellent! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report of the UI revamp plan.\\n\\n## UI Revamp Plan - Complete Architectural Context\\n\\nI've thoroughly reviewed the UI/UX revamp plan for the kynetic-spec project. Here's the complete architectural context:\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nThe UI revamp plan (plan ID: `01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2`) defines a comprehensive redesign of the web UI across 10 major feature areas, with supporting design system and component architecture.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Design System Architecture\\n\\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n\\n**Token Structure:**\\n- **Color System**: OKLCH color space for perceptual uniformity\\n- **16 Design Tokens** (oklch format with lightness/chroma/hue):\\n  - Background, Foreground, Card, Card-foreground\\n  - Popover, Popover-foreground\\n  - Primary, Primary-foreground\\n  - Secondary, Secondary-foreground\\n  - Muted, Muted-foreground\\n  - Accent, Accent-foreground\\n  - Destructive\\n  - Border, Input, Ring\\n\\n- **5 Chart Colors** (for data visualization)\\n- **8 Sidebar-specific Tokens** (theme variants for navigation)\\n\\n**Dark Theme Support:**\\nThe tokens automatically swap when the `.dark` class is applied, providing full dark mode support with oklch values optimized for contrast and readability.\\n\\n**Current Status:**\\n- Tailwind @theme inline extensions already mapped (lines 76-112 in app.css)\\n- Variables system uses CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- Base layer styling established (border-border, outline-ring/50, bg-background, text-foreground)\\n\\n**Spacing:** CSS variables calculated as `--radius: 0.625rem` with 4 radius tokens:\\n- `--radius-sm` (0.625rem - 4px)\\n- `--radius-md` (0.625rem - 2px)\\n- `--radius-lg` (0.625rem)\\n- `--radius-xl` (0.625rem + 4px)\\n\\n**Status Color Mappings** (from spec):\\n- `pending` = amber\\n- `in_progress` = orange\\n- `pending_review` = blue\\n- `needs_work` = yellow\\n- `completed` = emerald\\n- `blocked` = red\\n- `cancelled` = gray\\n\\n**Animations:**\\n- Shimmer animation for skeleton loaders (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n- Breathing/pulse animation for active agent task cards (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Component Architecture\\n\\n**Current Component Structure** (`/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`):\\n\\n**Layout Components:**\\n- `Sidebar.svelte` - Collapsible navigation sidebar with grouped sections\\n- `MobileNav.svelte` - Bottom navigation for mobile (< 768px)\\n- `CommandPalette.svelte` - Global command/search palette (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K)\\n- `ConnectionStatus.svelte` - WebSocket connection indicator\\n\\n**Feature Components:**\\n- `ItemDetail.svelte` - Spec item detail viewer\\n- `ItemTree.svelte` - Hierarchical spec item tree\\n- `TaskList.svelte` - Task list with filtering\\n- `TaskDetail.svelte` - Task detail view (legacy)\\n- `TaskDetailPanel.svelte` - Task detail slide-over panel\\n- `TaskFilters.svelte` - Filter controls for task list\\n- `ProjectSelector.svelte` - Multi-project selector (for multi-directory daemon mode)\\n\\n**UI Primitives** (`/lib/components/ui/`):\\n- Shadcn-svelte components: Accordion, Badge, Button, Card, Dialog, Dropdown-menu, Input, Label, Popover, Select, Sheet, Sidebar, Table, Tabs, Toast, Tooltip, etc.\\n\\n**Banner Components:**\\n- `ReadOnlyBanner.svelte` - Static mode indicator with \\\"data freshness\\\" timestamp\\n\\n---\\n\\n### App Shell and Navigation\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n- Main layout file: `+layout.svelte` (SvelteKit root layout)\\n- Uses `SidebarProvider` and `SidebarInset` from shadcn-svelte\\n- Desktop sidebar hidden on mobile (`hidden md:block`)\\n- Responsive inset with main content area (`flex-1 overflow-auto`)\\n\\n**Sidebar Grouping** (planned):\\n```\\nWork\\n  - Dashboard\\n  - Tasks\\n  - Agents\\n  - Sessions\\n\\nSpecs\\n  - Specs\\n  - Plans\\n  - Validate\\n\\nCapture\\n  - Inbox\\n  - Observations\\n  - Triage\\n\\nConfig\\n  - Workflows\\n  - Settings\\n```\\n\\n**Badge Counts:**\\n- Inbox items count\\n- Unresolved observations count\\n- Pending review task count\\n\\n**Current Routes:**\\n- `/` - Dashboard\\n- `/items` - Specs (should redirect `/items` → `/specs`)\\n- `/tasks` - Task list\\n- `/inbox` - Inbox\\n- `/observations` - Observations\\n- `/triage` - Triage view\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Feature Specifications (10 Areas)\\n\\n#### 1. **UI Design System** (`@ui-design-system`)\\n- Port imgen's design token architecture into Tailwind\\n- Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, animation keyframes\\n- **AC Focus**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, 3 font families as Tailwind utilities\\n- Dark theme with status colors\\n- Loading shimmer animations\\n- Agent task card breathing/pulse animations\\n\\n#### 2. **App Shell and Navigation** (`@ui-app-shell`)\\n- Restructure +layout.svelte with grouped sidebar navigation\\n- Migrate Sidebar.svelte to grouped sections\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate 3 existing task detail implementations\\n\\n#### 3. **Task Board (Kanban)** (`@ui-task-board`)\\n- Kanban-style columns mapping to task states:\\n  - **Backlog**: pending (manual_only/unassessed)\\n  - **Ready**: pending (eligible)\\n  - **In Progress**: in_progress, needs_work\\n  - **Review**: pending_review\\n  - **Done**: completed (recent)\\n  - **Blocked/Cancelled**: sections/indicators\\n\\n- **Task Card Elements**: Priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (monospace), spec ref link, metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n- **Detail Modal**: Full task info with title, description, status, priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos, automation status, VCS info, plan ref, session link\\n- **Active Fleet Row**: Shows currently running agent tasks with title, agent name, elapsed time (with pulse indicator), last few lines of output\\n- **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven board updates via `tasks:updates` topic\\n- **Mutations**: Task action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note) execute via API\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisite**: \\n- Daemon must return `type` and `automation` fields in task list API response\\n- Build components: KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal, ActiveFleetRow\\n\\n#### 4. **Session Stream View** (`@ui-session-stream`)\\n- View for watching agent work (historical and live)\\n- Renders structured session events from `events.jsonl`\\n- **Two-tier rendering**:\\n  - Structured events from `events.jsonl` (history)\\n  - `agent_text_chunk` WebSocket events (live text)\\n  \\n- **Event Types**: Agent messages (markdown), tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), thinking blocks (collapsed by default)\\n- **Live Streaming**: Real-time text via WebSocket with periodic structured refresh\\n- **Auto-scroll**: Follow new content, pause when user scrolls up (>100px from bottom), resume when scrolled back, \\\"jump to bottom\\\" button when paused\\n- **Session Context Panel**: Session metadata, spec context with AC checklist, files changed, budget info\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisites**:\\n- Build GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events` endpoints\\n- Build components: SessionStream, ChatMessage, ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock\\n\\n#### 5. **Agent and Dispatch View** (`@ui-agent-dispatch`)\\n- Shows agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped)\\n- Active invocations with links to session streams\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/agent/dispatch/status` and GET `/api/agent/status` endpoints\\n- Subscribe to `agents` WebSocket topic for real-time updates\\n- Components: AgentList, DispatchStatus, InvocationCard\\n\\n#### 6. **Session History** (`@ui-session-history`)\\n- List view of past agent sessions\\n- Display: ID, agent type, task ref, status, duration, age (sorted by most recent first)\\n- Filtering support\\n- Navigate to session detail (session stream view)\\n- Depends on GET `/api/sessions` endpoint from ui-session-stream work\\n\\n#### 7. **Enhanced Inbox View** (`@ui-inbox-enhanced`)\\n- Triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n- Quick triage action links\\n- Filter controls (status, tags, age)\\n- Keep existing add/delete functionality\\n\\n#### 8. **Plans View** (`@ui-plans-view`)\\n- Browse plan records with progress tracking\\n- Display: Title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts, progress (based on task completion)\\n- **Daemon Prerequisite**: Build GET `/api/plans` endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans)\\n\\n#### 9. **Validation and Alignment View** (`@ui-validation-view`)\\n- Validation results, alignment statistics, issues\\n- Summary: Error count, warning count, valid item count\\n- Alignment section: Spec coverage %, AC coverage %, orphaned tasks/specs counts\\n- Issues list grouped by severity\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/validate` and GET `/api/alignment` endpoints\\n\\n#### 10. **Dashboard Overview** (`@ui-dashboard-overview`)\\n- Home view: \\\"What's happening right now?\\\"\\n- **Active work section**: Currently running agent tasks\\n- **Status summary**: Clickable count cards per status\\n- **Needs-attention section**: Aggregates:\\n  - Untriaged inbox items\\n  - Unresolved observations\\n  - Validation warnings\\n  - Blocked tasks\\n- Build last (reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board)\\n- No aggregated activity API needed; merge recent data client-side\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n**Design System:**\\n- Set up isolated clone first\\n- Port imgen's full `token-contract.css` into Tailwind @theme inline in app.css\\n- Start with token bridge pilot on dashboard page to validate approach\\n- Create modular CSS files: `tokens.css`, `animations.css`, `typography.css` in `lib/ds/`\\n- Establish loading skeleton and error boundary patterns\\n\\n**App Shell:**\\n- Restructure `+layout.svelte` with new sidebar component\\n- Migrate existing Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate three existing task detail implementations\\n- Ensure all existing routes continue working\\n\\n**Daemon API Changes Required:**\\n- Task list API: Add `type` and `automation` fields to response\\n- Task mutations: Build POST endpoints for `/api/tasks/:ref/start`, `/api/tasks/:ref/submit`, `/api/tasks/:ref/complete`, `/api/tasks/:ref/block`\\n- Sessions: Add GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events`\\n- Plans: Add GET `/api/plans` endpoint\\n\\n**WebSocket Topics:**\\n- `tasks:updates` - Task state changes\\n- `agents` - Agent dispatch status and text chunks\\n- `files:updates` - File change notifications\\n\\n**Dependencies Between Features:**\\n```\\nui-design-system (foundation)\\n├── ui-app-shell\\n├── ui-task-board\\n├── ui-dashboard-overview\\n└── ui-session-stream\\n    ├── ui-session-history\\n    └── ui-agent-dispatch\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Technology Stack\\n\\n- **Framework**: SvelteKit (Svelte 5 with runes)\\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 with @theme inline\\n- **UI Components**: shadcn-svelte\\n- **Color Space**: OKLCH (perceptual)\\n- **Real-time**: WebSocket (topic-based pub/sub)\\n- **State Management**: Svelte runes (reactive)\\n- **Animation**: CSS keyframes with `prefers-reduced-motion` gates\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Acceptance Criteria Highlights\\n\\n1. **Design System**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing values, 7 z-index, 3 font families available as Tailwind utilities\\n2. **Dark Theme**: Status colors visually distinct (amber, orange, blue, yellow, emerald, red, gray)\\n3. **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven without page refresh\\n4. **Mobile Responsive**: Sidebar → bottom nav on small screens, detail panels on large screens (≥1024px)\\n5. **Command Palette**: Global search (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K) with results grouped by type\\n6. **WebSocket Resilience**: Exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s), sequence deduplication\\n7. **Agent Work Visibility**: Active Fleet row with elapsed time, pulse indicator, live output streaming\\n\\n---\\n\\n### File Locations\\n\\n- **Plan Record**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml` (lines 7613-8133)\\n- **App CSS (Design Tokens)**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n- **Layout**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/routes/+layout.svelte`\\n- **Tailwind Config**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/tailwind.config.js`\\n- **Components**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`\\n- **UI Primitives**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ui/`\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a complete redesign roadmap with clear feature boundaries, specific acceptance criteria, daemon API requirements, and implementation guidance for modernizing the kspec web UI with a cohesive design system and improved user experience.\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"agentId: a7bcb35 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\\n<usage>total_tokens: 59766\\ntool_uses: 21\\nduration_ms: 74652</usage>\"}],\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Excellent! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report of the UI revamp plan.\\n\\n## UI Revamp Plan - Complete Architectural Context\\n\\nI've thoroughly reviewed the UI/UX revamp plan for the kynetic-spec project. Here's the complete architectural context:\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nThe UI revamp plan (plan ID: `01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2`) defines a comprehensive redesign of the web UI across 10 major feature areas, with supporting design system and component architecture.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Design System Architecture\\n\\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n\\n**Token Structure:**\\n- **Color System**: OKLCH color space for perceptual uniformity\\n- **16 Design Tokens** (oklch format with lightness/chroma/hue):\\n  - Background, Foreground, Card, Card-foreground\\n  - Popover, Popover-foreground\\n  - Primary, Primary-foreground\\n  - Secondary, Secondary-foreground\\n  - Muted, Muted-foreground\\n  - Accent, Accent-foreground\\n  - Destructive\\n  - Border, Input, Ring\\n\\n- **5 Chart Colors** (for data visualization)\\n- **8 Sidebar-specific Tokens** (theme variants for navigation)\\n\\n**Dark Theme Support:**\\nThe tokens automatically swap when the `.dark` class is applied, providing full dark mode support with oklch values optimized for contrast and readability.\\n\\n**Current Status:**\\n- Tailwind @theme inline extensions already mapped (lines 76-112 in app.css)\\n- Variables system uses CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- Base layer styling established (border-border, outline-ring/50, bg-background, text-foreground)\\n\\n**Spacing:** CSS variables calculated as `--radius: 0.625rem` with 4 radius tokens:\\n- `--radius-sm` (0.625rem - 4px)\\n- `--radius-md` (0.625rem - 2px)\\n- `--radius-lg` (0.625rem)\\n- `--radius-xl` (0.625rem + 4px)\\n\\n**Status Color Mappings** (from spec):\\n- `pending` = amber\\n- `in_progress` = orange\\n- `pending_review` = blue\\n- `needs_work` = yellow\\n- `completed` = emerald\\n- `blocked` = red\\n- `cancelled` = gray\\n\\n**Animations:**\\n- Shimmer animation for skeleton loaders (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n- Breathing/pulse animation for active agent task cards (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Component Architecture\\n\\n**Current Component Structure** (`/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`):\\n\\n**Layout Components:**\\n- `Sidebar.svelte` - Collapsible navigation sidebar with grouped sections\\n- `MobileNav.svelte` - Bottom navigation for mobile (< 768px)\\n- `CommandPalette.svelte` - Global command/search palette (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K)\\n- `ConnectionStatus.svelte` - WebSocket connection indicator\\n\\n**Feature Components:**\\n- `ItemDetail.svelte` - Spec item detail viewer\\n- `ItemTree.svelte` - Hierarchical spec item tree\\n- `TaskList.svelte` - Task list with filtering\\n- `TaskDetail.svelte` - Task detail view (legacy)\\n- `TaskDetailPanel.svelte` - Task detail slide-over panel\\n- `TaskFilters.svelte` - Filter controls for task list\\n- `ProjectSelector.svelte` - Multi-project selector (for multi-directory daemon mode)\\n\\n**UI Primitives** (`/lib/components/ui/`):\\n- Shadcn-svelte components: Accordion, Badge, Button, Card, Dialog, Dropdown-menu, Input, Label, Popover, Select, Sheet, Sidebar, Table, Tabs, Toast, Tooltip, etc.\\n\\n**Banner Components:**\\n- `ReadOnlyBanner.svelte` - Static mode indicator with \\\"data freshness\\\" timestamp\\n\\n---\\n\\n### App Shell and Navigation\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n- Main layout file: `+layout.svelte` (SvelteKit root layout)\\n- Uses `SidebarProvider` and `SidebarInset` from shadcn-svelte\\n- Desktop sidebar hidden on mobile (`hidden md:block`)\\n- Responsive inset with main content area (`flex-1 overflow-auto`)\\n\\n**Sidebar Grouping** (planned):\\n```\\nWork\\n  - Dashboard\\n  - Tasks\\n  - Agents\\n  - Sessions\\n\\nSpecs\\n  - Specs\\n  - Plans\\n  - Validate\\n\\nCapture\\n  - Inbox\\n  - Observations\\n  - Triage\\n\\nConfig\\n  - Workflows\\n  - Settings\\n```\\n\\n**Badge Counts:**\\n- Inbox items count\\n- Unresolved observations count\\n- Pending review task count\\n\\n**Current Routes:**\\n- `/` - Dashboard\\n- `/items` - Specs (should redirect `/items` → `/specs`)\\n- `/tasks` - Task list\\n- `/inbox` - Inbox\\n- `/observations` - Observations\\n- `/triage` - Triage view\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Feature Specifications (10 Areas)\\n\\n#### 1. **UI Design System** (`@ui-design-system`)\\n- Port imgen's design token architecture into Tailwind\\n- Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, animation keyframes\\n- **AC Focus**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, 3 font families as Tailwind utilities\\n- Dark theme with status colors\\n- Loading shimmer animations\\n- Agent task card breathing/pulse animations\\n\\n#### 2. **App Shell and Navigation** (`@ui-app-shell`)\\n- Restructure +layout.svelte with grouped sidebar navigation\\n- Migrate Sidebar.svelte to grouped sections\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate 3 existing task detail implementations\\n\\n#### 3. **Task Board (Kanban)** (`@ui-task-board`)\\n- Kanban-style columns mapping to task states:\\n  - **Backlog**: pending (manual_only/unassessed)\\n  - **Ready**: pending (eligible)\\n  - **In Progress**: in_progress, needs_work\\n  - **Review**: pending_review\\n  - **Done**: completed (recent)\\n  - **Blocked/Cancelled**: sections/indicators\\n\\n- **Task Card Elements**: Priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (monospace), spec ref link, metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n- **Detail Modal**: Full task info with title, description, status, priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos, automation status, VCS info, plan ref, session link\\n- **Active Fleet Row**: Shows currently running agent tasks with title, agent name, elapsed time (with pulse indicator), last few lines of output\\n- **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven board updates via `tasks:updates` topic\\n- **Mutations**: Task action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note) execute via API\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisite**: \\n- Daemon must return `type` and `automation` fields in task list API response\\n- Build components: KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal, ActiveFleetRow\\n\\n#### 4. **Session Stream View** (`@ui-session-stream`)\\n- View for watching agent work (historical and live)\\n- Renders structured session events from `events.jsonl`\\n- **Two-tier rendering**:\\n  - Structured events from `events.jsonl` (history)\\n  - `agent_text_chunk` WebSocket events (live text)\\n  \\n- **Event Types**: Agent messages (markdown), tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), thinking blocks (collapsed by default)\\n- **Live Streaming**: Real-time text via WebSocket with periodic structured refresh\\n- **Auto-scroll**: Follow new content, pause when user scrolls up (>100px from bottom), resume when scrolled back, \\\"jump to bottom\\\" button when paused\\n- **Session Context Panel**: Session metadata, spec context with AC checklist, files changed, budget info\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisites**:\\n- Build GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events` endpoints\\n- Build components: SessionStream, ChatMessage, ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock\\n\\n#### 5. **Agent and Dispatch View** (`@ui-agent-dispatch`)\\n- Shows agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped)\\n- Active invocations with links to session streams\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/agent/dispatch/status` and GET `/api/agent/status` endpoints\\n- Subscribe to `agents` WebSocket topic for real-time updates\\n- Components: AgentList, DispatchStatus, InvocationCard\\n\\n#### 6. **Session History** (`@ui-session-history`)\\n- List view of past agent sessions\\n- Display: ID, agent type, task ref, status, duration, age (sorted by most recent first)\\n- Filtering support\\n- Navigate to session detail (session stream view)\\n- Depends on GET `/api/sessions` endpoint from ui-session-stream work\\n\\n#### 7. **Enhanced Inbox View** (`@ui-inbox-enhanced`)\\n- Triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n- Quick triage action links\\n- Filter controls (status, tags, age)\\n- Keep existing add/delete functionality\\n\\n#### 8. **Plans View** (`@ui-plans-view`)\\n- Browse plan records with progress tracking\\n- Display: Title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts, progress (based on task completion)\\n- **Daemon Prerequisite**: Build GET `/api/plans` endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans)\\n\\n#### 9. **Validation and Alignment View** (`@ui-validation-view`)\\n- Validation results, alignment statistics, issues\\n- Summary: Error count, warning count, valid item count\\n- Alignment section: Spec coverage %, AC coverage %, orphaned tasks/specs counts\\n- Issues list grouped by severity\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/validate` and GET `/api/alignment` endpoints\\n\\n#### 10. **Dashboard Overview** (`@ui-dashboard-overview`)\\n- Home view: \\\"What's happening right now?\\\"\\n- **Active work section**: Currently running agent tasks\\n- **Status summary**: Clickable count cards per status\\n- **Needs-attention section**: Aggregates:\\n  - Untriaged inbox items\\n  - Unresolved observations\\n  - Validation warnings\\n  - Blocked tasks\\n- Build last (reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board)\\n- No aggregated activity API needed; merge recent data client-side\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n**Design System:**\\n- Set up isolated clone first\\n- Port imgen's full `token-contract.css` into Tailwind @theme inline in app.css\\n- Start with token bridge pilot on dashboard page to validate approach\\n- Create modular CSS files: `tokens.css`, `animations.css`, `typography.css` in `lib/ds/`\\n- Establish loading skeleton and error boundary patterns\\n\\n**App Shell:**\\n- Restructure `+layout.svelte` with new sidebar component\\n- Migrate existing Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate three existing task detail implementations\\n- Ensure all existing routes continue working\\n\\n**Daemon API Changes Required:**\\n- Task list API: Add `type` and `automation` fields to response\\n- Task mutations: Build POST endpoints for `/api/tasks/:ref/start`, `/api/tasks/:ref/submit`, `/api/tasks/:ref/complete`, `/api/tasks/:ref/block`\\n- Sessions: Add GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events`\\n- Plans: Add GET `/api/plans` endpoint\\n\\n**WebSocket Topics:**\\n- `tasks:updates` - Task state changes\\n- `agents` - Agent dispatch status and text chunks\\n- `files:updates` - File change notifications\\n\\n**Dependencies Between Features:**\\n```\\nui-design-system (foundation)\\n├── ui-app-shell\\n├── ui-task-board\\n├── ui-dashboard-overview\\n└── ui-session-stream\\n    ├── ui-session-history\\n    └── ui-agent-dispatch\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Technology Stack\\n\\n- **Framework**: SvelteKit (Svelte 5 with runes)\\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 with @theme inline\\n- **UI Components**: shadcn-svelte\\n- **Color Space**: OKLCH (perceptual)\\n- **Real-time**: WebSocket (topic-based pub/sub)\\n- **State Management**: Svelte runes (reactive)\\n- **Animation**: CSS keyframes with `prefers-reduced-motion` gates\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Acceptance Criteria Highlights\\n\\n1. **Design System**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing values, 7 z-index, 3 font families available as Tailwind utilities\\n2. **Dark Theme**: Status colors visually distinct (amber, orange, blue, yellow, emerald, red, gray)\\n3. **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven without page refresh\\n4. **Mobile Responsive**: Sidebar → bottom nav on small screens, detail panels on large screens (≥1024px)\\n5. **Command Palette**: Global search (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K) with results grouped by type\\n6. **WebSocket Resilience**: Exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s), sequence deduplication\\n7. **Agent Work Visibility**: Active Fleet row with elapsed time, pulse indicator, live output streaming\\n\\n---\\n\\n### File Locations\\n\\n- **Plan Record**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml` (lines 7613-8133)\\n- **App CSS (Design Tokens)**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n- **Layout**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/routes/+layout.svelte`\\n- **Tailwind Config**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/tailwind.config.js`\\n- **Components**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`\\n- **UI Primitives**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ui/`\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a complete redesign roadmap with clear feature boundaries, specific acceptance criteria, daemon API requirements, and implementation guidance for modernizing the kspec web UI with a cohesive design system and improved user experience.\"}},{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"agentId: a7bcb35 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\\n<usage>total_tokens: 59766\\ntool_uses: 21\\nduration_ms: 74652</usage>\"}}]}}\n","exit_code":2,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":401985117},"formatted_output":"Total output lines: 135\n\n.kspec/sessions/01KJYBAYDE4HQR64FHAVSG19NV/events.jsonl:21:{\"ts\":1772692545698,\"seq\":20,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJYBAYDE4HQR64FHAVSG19NV\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolResponse\":{\"stdout\":\"Implement UI Design System\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nULID:      01KJXSVFHZ2FHQND06AEGFC3FF\\nSlugs:     implement-ui-design-system\\nType:      task\\nStatus:    completed\\nPriority:  1\\nAutomation: eligible\\nSession:   01KJY9JDA1723TJVFBPEDS4VV0\\nSpec ref:  @ui-design-system\\nPlan ref:  @plan-ui-ux-revamp\\nDepends:\\n  @01KJXSWR → UI Revamp Prerequisites (Quick Wins) [pending]\\nCreated:   2026-03-05T01:30:03.199Z\\nStarted:   2026-03-05T06:12:08.948Z\\nCompleted: 2026-03-05T06:23:49.642Z\\n\\n─── Spec Context ───\\nUI Design System\\nType: feature\\nImplementation: implemented\\nDescription:\\n  Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n  Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n  keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n  across all views.\\nAcceptance Criteria:\\n  [ac-1]\\n    Given: The web UI app.css file\\n\\n    When: imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n\\n    Then: All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\nare available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n\\n  [ac-2]\\n    Given: A component using design tokens\\n\\n    When: The dark theme tokens are applied\\n\\n    Then: oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\npending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\nare visually distinct\\n\\n  [ac-3]\\n    Given: A view with loading states\\n\\n    When: Content is loading\\n\\n    Then: Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n  [ac-4]\\n    Given: An active agent task card\\n\\n    When: The agent is working\\n\\n    Then: Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n\\n─── Notes ───\\n[2026-03-05T01:30:03.199Z] @claude:\\nSee plan @plan-ui-ux-revamp for implementation notes\\n[2026-03-05T04:20:57.692Z] @claude:\\nExecution context:\\n- Background: Foundation design token layer that all other UI revamp tasks build on\\n- Scope: Create lib/ds/ directory with tokens.css and animations.css; extend app.css @theme inline block with design-* tokens, status colors, spacing, z-index, typography; add shimmer and breathing animations gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/ds/tokens.css, packages/web-ui/src/lib/ds/animations.css, packages/web-ui/src/app.css, tests for AC coverage\\n- Verification: npm test in project root, vitest tests validating token presence and animation definitions\\n[2026-03-05T04:31:57.761Z] @claude:\\nImplementation complete. Created:\\n- lib/ds/tokens.css: 16 oklch color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, 3 fonts, 7 status colors (light+dark)\\n- lib/ds/animations.css: ds-shimmer (2s) and ds-breathe (3s) keyframes with prefers-reduced-motion gates\\n- Updated app.css: imports tokens/animations, extends @theme inline with all design-* token mappings\\n- tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts: 18 tests covering all 4 ACs (reads built CSS output)\\n- Build succeeds, all 18 new tests pass, full suite passes (2 pre-existing codex failures unrelated)\\n[2026-03-05T04:41:04.671Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX 1) Required test command fails in web-ui package: 'cd packages/web-ui && npm test' exits 1 because package script 'test' is missing (packages/web-ui/package.json). 2) kspec validate reports a warning for this spec that is a blocker per checklist: UI Design System status mismatch (spec implementation='in_progress' but validator expects 'not_started' based on task progress). AC annotation coverage exists for ac-1..ac-4 in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts.\\n[2026-03-05T04:41:09.606Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Review issues: required web-ui test command fails (missing npm test script) and kspec validate reports spec-specific status mismatch warning for @ui-design-system.\\n[2026-03-05T04:55:43.148Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 1: Addressed both review findings. (1) Added 'test' script to packages/web-ui/package.json that delegates to root vitest for web-ui-design-system.test.ts — 'cd packages/web-ui && npm test' now passes all 18 tests. (2) Fixed spec status mismatch by resetting @ui-design-system implementation to not_started, and restored 19 unrelated specs that were incorrectly cascaded to not_started by the item set command.\\n[2026-03-05T05:01:45.150Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX - kspec validate reports a warning for this spec: UI Design System status mismatch (spec implementation='in_progress' but expected 'not_started' based on task progress). Required test sequence passed: root npm test (176 files, 3703 tests) and packages/web-ui npm test (18 tests). AC annotations for @ui-design-system ac-1..ac-4 are present in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts; no inherited trait ACs for this spec.\\n[2026-03-05T05:01:48.158Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Review findings: Review issues: MUST-FIX spec-specific kspec validate warning remains for @ui-design-system (status mismatch: implementation in_progress vs expected not_started).\\n[2026-03-05T05:06:41.467Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 2: Resolved spec status mismatch by setting @ui-design-system implementation to not_started (declined cascading to children). The previous fix cycle set it correctly but it appears to have been re-set to in_progress. Verified kspec validate no longer reports the status mismatch warning. All tests pass: root (3701/3701), web-ui (18/18). The 2 pre-existing enhanced-setup.test.ts failures are unrelated.\\n[2026-03-05T05:12:36.945Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX — kspec validate reports a spec-specific warning for @ui-design-system: status mismatch (implementation=\\\"in_progress\\\" but expected \\\"not_started\\\" based on task progress). Required review checks completed: git diff feat/ui-revamp...HEAD reviewed; AC annotations present for ac-1..ac-4 in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts; no inherited trait ACs shown by kspec item get @ui-design-system; required test sequence passed (root npm test and packages/web-ui npm test).\\n[2026-03-05T05:12:39.790Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 3] Review findings: Review issues: MUST-FIX spec warning remains in kspec validate for @ui-design-system (status mismatch implementation in_progress vs expected not_started).\\n[2026-03-05T05:22:56.150Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 3: The status mismatch warning was caused by the task being in needs_work state (which maps to expected spec status not_started in alignment.ts calculateExpectedStatus), while the spec remained at in_progress. Running kspec task start transitions the task back to in_progress, which aligns with the spec's in_progress status. Previous fix cycles were setting spec to not_started but that got overridden when task start re-ran. The fix is simply that the task is now properly in in_progress state. kspec validate confirms no status mismatch warning for @ui-design-system. All 18 design system tests pass. 4 pre-existing failures unrelated (codex platform detection + session-start timeout).\\n[2026-03-05T05:32:59.987Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX — kspec validate reports a warning for this spec: UI Design System status mismatch (implementation=\\\"in_progress\\\" but expected \\\"not_started\\\" based on task progress). Review checks: diff against feat/ui-revamp reviewed; AC annotations present for @ui-design-system ac-1..ac-4 in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts; no inherited trait ACs shown by kspec item get @ui-design-system; required test commands pass (npm test and cd packages/web-ui && npm test).\\n[2026-03-05T05:33:05.469Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 4] Review findings: Review issues: MUST-FIX spec-specific kspec validate warning remains for @ui-design-system (status mismatch: implementation in_progress vs expected not_started).\\n[2026-03-05T05:49:49.518Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 4: Root-caused the persistent status mismatch. calculateExpectedStatus() in alignment.ts only checked for in_progress tasks — needs_work and pending_review fell through to not_started. Fixed by treating needs_work, pending_review, and in_progress as active work states that map to spec in_progress. Added 3 new alignment tests. All 3706 tests pass (3 pre-existing codex failures unrelated). kspec validate confirms 294/294 aligned (was 293/294).\\n[2026-03-05T05:55:44.682Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX 1) Incorrect AC annotation mapping in tests/validate-alignment-no-task-policy.test.ts:128 — '// AC: @ui-design-system ac-1' is attached to alignment status behavior, not UI design token behavior from @ui-design-system ac-1. AC annotations must map to the referenced AC text. 2) Out-of-scope core behavior change in src/parser/alignment.ts:154-167 modifies global expected status rules (treats pending_review/needs_work as active work) and was added on this UI design-system task branch; move to a dedicated alignment/spec task or remove from this task branch. Required test sequence passed: npm test (3706 passed) and packages/web-ui npm test (18 passed). kspec validate run completed; no spec-specific warning shown for @ui-design-system, but global repo validation errors/warnings remain unrelated to this task.\\n[2026-03-05T05:55:50.042Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 5] Review findings: Review issues: MUST-FIX incorrect AC annotation mapping (tests/validate-alignment-no-task-policy.test.ts:128) and out-of-scope global alignment behavior change in src/parser/alignment.ts:154-167 on this UI design-system task branch.\\n[2026-03-05T06:04:22.569Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 5: Reverted out-of-scope alignment.ts changes (needs_work/pending_review active-work logic) and removed incorrect AC annotation (@ui-design-system ac-1 on alignment tests). These changes belong on a dedicated alignment task — captured as inbox item 01KJY9H2. All tests pass: root (3701/3701 + 2 pre-existing codex failures), web-ui (18/18), alignment tests (5/5). kspec validate clean for @ui-design-system.\\n[2026-03-05T06:09:46.280Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX — kspec validate reports a warning for this spec: UI Design System status mismatch (implementation=\\\"in_progress\\\" but expected \\\"not_started\\\" based on task progress). Review checks completed: diff against feat/ui-revamp reviewed; AC annotations present for @ui-design-system ac-1..ac-4 in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts; no inherited trait ACs shown by kspec item get @ui-design-system; required test commands passed (root npm test and cd packages/web-ui && npm test).\\n[2026-03-05T06:09:47.998Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 6] Review findings: Review issues: MUST-FIX spec-specific kspec validate warning remains for @ui-design-system (status mismatch implementation in_progress vs expected not_started).\\n[2026-03-05T06:16:33.924Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 6: Set spec @ui-design-system implementation to not_started and used --no-sync on task start to prevent auto-sync back to in_progress. The root cause is a known alignment bug (tracked in inbox 01KJY9H2) where calculateExpectedStatus() doesn't treat pending_review/needs_work as active work states. Workaround: keep spec at not_started so it matches what the validator expects when task is in pending_review state. All tests pass: root (3701/3701 + 2 pre-existing codex failures), web-ui (18/18).\\n[2026-03-05T06:34:49.691Z] @claude:\\nTask already completed in a previous invocation. All fix cycle issues resolved, merged to feat/ui-revamp in ea25b70a8. No remaining kspec validate warnings for @ui-design-system. No further work needed.\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01NPkcdrYmKEaP17YbVwg1aN\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\"}}\n.kspec/sessions/01KJYBAYDE4HQR64FHAVSG19NV/events.jsonl:22:{\"ts\":1772692545710,\"seq\":21,\"type\":\"session.update\",\"session_id\":\"01KJYBAYDE4HQR64FHAVSG19NV\",\"data\":{\"_meta\":{\"claudeCode\":{\"toolName\":\"Bash\"}},\"toolCallId\":\"toolu_01NPkcdrYmKEaP17YbVwg1aN\",\"sessionUpdate\":\"tool_call_update\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"rawOutput\":\"Implement UI Design System\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\nULID:      01KJXSVFHZ2FHQND06AEGFC3FF\\nSlugs:     implement-ui-design-system\\nType:      task\\nStatus:    completed\\nPriority:  1\\nAutomation: eligible\\nSession:   01KJY9JDA1723TJVFBPEDS4VV0\\nSpec ref:  @ui-design-system\\nPlan ref:  @plan-ui-ux-revamp\\nDepends:\\n  @01KJXSWR → UI Revamp Prerequisites (Quick Wins) [pending]\\nCreated:   2026-03-05T01:30:03.199Z\\nStarted:   2026-03-05T06:12:08.948Z\\nCompleted: 2026-03-05T06:23:49.642Z\\n\\n─── Spec Context ───\\nUI Design System\\nType: feature\\nImplementation: implemented\\nDescription:\\n  Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.\\n  Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation\\n  keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language\\n  across all views.\\nAcceptance Criteria:\\n  [ac-1]\\n    Given: The web UI app.css file\\n\\n    When: imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions\\n\\n    Then: All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families\\nare available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)\\n\\n  [ac-2]\\n    Given: A component using design tokens\\n\\n    When: The dark theme tokens are applied\\n\\n    Then: oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,\\npending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)\\nare visually distinct\\n\\n  [ac-3]\\n    Given: A view with loading states\\n\\n    When: Content is loading\\n\\n    Then: Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n  [ac-4]\\n    Given: An active agent task card\\n\\n    When: The agent is working\\n\\n    Then: Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n\\n\\n─── Notes ───\\n[2026-03-05T01:30:03.199Z] @claude:\\nSee plan @plan-ui-ux-revamp for implementation notes\\n[2026-03-05T04:20:57.692Z] @claude:\\nExecution context:\\n- Background: Foundation design token layer that all other UI revamp tasks build on\\n- Scope: Create lib/ds/ directory with tokens.css and animations.css; extend app.css @theme inline block with design-* tokens, status colors, spacing, z-index, typography; add shimmer and breathing animations gated behind prefers-reduced-motion\\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/ds/tokens.css, packages/web-ui/src/lib/ds/animations.css, packages/web-ui/src/app.css, tests for AC coverage\\n- Verification: npm test in project root, vitest tests validating token presence and animation definitions\\n[2026-03-05T04:31:57.761Z] @claude:\\nImplementation complete. Created:\\n- lib/ds/tokens.css: 16 oklch color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, 3 fonts, 7 status colors (light+dark)\\n- lib/ds/animations.css: ds-shimmer (2s) and ds-breathe (3s) keyframes with prefers-reduced-motion gates\\n- Updated app.css: imports tokens/animations, extends @theme inline with all design-* token mappings\\n- tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts: 18 tests covering all 4 ACs (reads built CSS output)\\n- Build succeeds, all 18 new tests pass, full suite passes (2 pre-existing codex failures unrelated)\\n[2026-03-05T04:41:04.671Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX 1) Required test command fails in web-ui package: 'cd packages/web-ui && npm test' exits 1 because package script 'test' is missing (packages/web-ui/package.json). 2) kspec validate reports a warning for this spec that is a blocker per checklist: UI Design System status mismatch (spec implementation='in_progress' but validator expects 'not_started' based on task progress). AC annotation coverage exists for ac-1..ac-4 in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts.\\n[2026-03-05T04:41:09.606Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Review issues: required web-ui test command fails (missing npm test script) and kspec validate reports spec-specific status mismatch warning for @ui-design-system.\\n[2026-03-05T04:55:43.148Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 1: Addressed both review findings. (1) Added 'test' script to packages/web-ui/package.json that delegates to root vitest for web-ui-design-system.test.ts — 'cd packages/web-ui && npm test' now passes all 18 tests. (2) Fixed spec status mismatch by resetting @ui-design-system implementation to not_started, and restored 19 unrelated specs that were incorrectly cascaded to not_started by the item set command.\\n[2026-03-05T05:01:45.150Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX - kspec validate reports a warning for this spec: UI Design System status mismatch (spec implementation='in_progress' but expected 'not_started' based on task progress). Required test sequence passed: root npm test (176 files, 3703 tests) and packages/web-ui npm test (18 tests). AC annotations for @ui-design-system ac-1..ac-4 are present in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts; no inherited trait ACs for this spec.\\n[2026-03-05T05:01:48.158Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 2] Review findings: Review issues: MUST-FIX spec-specific kspec validate warning remains for @ui-design-system (status mismatch: implementation in_progress vs expected not_started).\\n[2026-03-05T05:06:41.467Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 2: Resolved spec status mismatch by setting @ui-design-system implementation to not_started (declined cascading to children). The previous fix cycle set it correctly but it appears to have been re-set to in_progress. Verified kspec validate no longer reports the status mismatch warning. All tests pass: root (3701/3701), web-ui (18/18). The 2 pre-existing enhanced-setup.test.ts failures are unrelated.\\n[2026-03-05T05:12:36.945Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX — kspec validate reports a spec-specific warning for @ui-design-system: status mismatch (implementation=\\\"in_progress\\\" but expected \\\"not_started\\\" based on task progress). Required review checks completed: git diff feat/ui-revamp...HEAD reviewed; AC annotations present for ac-1..ac-4 in tests/web-ui-design-system.test.ts; no inherited trait ACs shown by kspec item get @ui-design-system; required test sequence passed (root npm test and packages/web-ui npm test).\\n[2026-03-05T05:12:39.790Z] Jacob Chapel:\\n[FIX_CYCLE: 3] Review findings: Review issues: MUST-FIX spec warning remains in kspec validate for @ui-design-system (status mismatch implementation in_progress vs expected not_started).\\n[2026-03-05T05:22:56.150Z] @claude:\\nFix cycle 3: The status mismatch warning was caused by the task being in needs_work state (which maps to expected spec status not_started in alignment.ts calculateExpectedStatus), while the spec remained at in_progress. Running kspec task start transitions the task back to in_progress, which aligns with the spec's in_progress status. Previous fix cycles were setting spec to not_started but that got overridden when task start re-ran. The fix is simply that the task is now properly in in_progress state. kspec validate confirms no status mismatch warning for @ui-design-system. All 18 design system tests pass. 4 pre-existing failures unrelated (codex platform detection + session-start timeout).\\n[2026-03-05T05:32:59.987Z] Jacob Chapel:\\nReview findings: MUST-FIX — kspec validate reports a warning for this spec: UI Design System status mismatch (implementation=\\\"in_progress\\\" but expected \\\"not_started\\\" based on task progress). Review checks: diff against feat/ui-revamp reviewed; AC annotations present for @ui-design-system ac-1..ac-4 in tests/w…246926 tokens truncated…etailModal, ActiveFleetRow\\n\\n#### 4. **Session Stream View** (`@ui-session-stream`)\\n- View for watching agent work (historical and live)\\n- Renders structured session events from `events.jsonl`\\n- **Two-tier rendering**:\\n  - Structured events from `events.jsonl` (history)\\n  - `agent_text_chunk` WebSocket events (live text)\\n  \\n- **Event Types**: Agent messages (markdown), tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), thinking blocks (collapsed by default)\\n- **Live Streaming**: Real-time text via WebSocket with periodic structured refresh\\n- **Auto-scroll**: Follow new content, pause when user scrolls up (>100px from bottom), resume when scrolled back, \\\"jump to bottom\\\" button when paused\\n- **Session Context Panel**: Session metadata, spec context with AC checklist, files changed, budget info\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisites**:\\n- Build GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events` endpoints\\n- Build components: SessionStream, ChatMessage, ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock\\n\\n#### 5. **Agent and Dispatch View** (`@ui-agent-dispatch`)\\n- Shows agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped)\\n- Active invocations with links to session streams\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/agent/dispatch/status` and GET `/api/agent/status` endpoints\\n- Subscribe to `agents` WebSocket topic for real-time updates\\n- Components: AgentList, DispatchStatus, InvocationCard\\n\\n#### 6. **Session History** (`@ui-session-history`)\\n- List view of past agent sessions\\n- Display: ID, agent type, task ref, status, duration, age (sorted by most recent first)\\n- Filtering support\\n- Navigate to session detail (session stream view)\\n- Depends on GET `/api/sessions` endpoint from ui-session-stream work\\n\\n#### 7. **Enhanced Inbox View** (`@ui-inbox-enhanced`)\\n- Triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n- Quick triage action links\\n- Filter controls (status, tags, age)\\n- Keep existing add/delete functionality\\n\\n#### 8. **Plans View** (`@ui-plans-view`)\\n- Browse plan records with progress tracking\\n- Display: Title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts, progress (based on task completion)\\n- **Daemon Prerequisite**: Build GET `/api/plans` endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans)\\n\\n#### 9. **Validation and Alignment View** (`@ui-validation-view`)\\n- Validation results, alignment statistics, issues\\n- Summary: Error count, warning count, valid item count\\n- Alignment section: Spec coverage %, AC coverage %, orphaned tasks/specs counts\\n- Issues list grouped by severity\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/validate` and GET `/api/alignment` endpoints\\n\\n#### 10. **Dashboard Overview** (`@ui-dashboard-overview`)\\n- Home view: \\\"What's happening right now?\\\"\\n- **Active work section**: Currently running agent tasks\\n- **Status summary**: Clickable count cards per status\\n- **Needs-attention section**: Aggregates:\\n  - Untriaged inbox items\\n  - Unresolved observations\\n  - Validation warnings\\n  - Blocked tasks\\n- Build last (reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board)\\n- No aggregated activity API needed; merge recent data client-side\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n**Design System:**\\n- Set up isolated clone first\\n- Port imgen's full `token-contract.css` into Tailwind @theme inline in app.css\\n- Start with token bridge pilot on dashboard page to validate approach\\n- Create modular CSS files: `tokens.css`, `animations.css`, `typography.css` in `lib/ds/`\\n- Establish loading skeleton and error boundary patterns\\n\\n**App Shell:**\\n- Restructure `+layout.svelte` with new sidebar component\\n- Migrate existing Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate three existing task detail implementations\\n- Ensure all existing routes continue working\\n\\n**Daemon API Changes Required:**\\n- Task list API: Add `type` and `automation` fields to response\\n- Task mutations: Build POST endpoints for `/api/tasks/:ref/start`, `/api/tasks/:ref/submit`, `/api/tasks/:ref/complete`, `/api/tasks/:ref/block`\\n- Sessions: Add GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events`\\n- Plans: Add GET `/api/plans` endpoint\\n\\n**WebSocket Topics:**\\n- `tasks:updates` - Task state changes\\n- `agents` - Agent dispatch status and text chunks\\n- `files:updates` - File change notifications\\n\\n**Dependencies Between Features:**\\n```\\nui-design-system (foundation)\\n├── ui-app-shell\\n├── ui-task-board\\n├── ui-dashboard-overview\\n└── ui-session-stream\\n    ├── ui-session-history\\n    └── ui-agent-dispatch\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Technology Stack\\n\\n- **Framework**: SvelteKit (Svelte 5 with runes)\\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 with @theme inline\\n- **UI Components**: shadcn-svelte\\n- **Color Space**: OKLCH (perceptual)\\n- **Real-time**: WebSocket (topic-based pub/sub)\\n- **State Management**: Svelte runes (reactive)\\n- **Animation**: CSS keyframes with `prefers-reduced-motion` gates\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Acceptance Criteria Highlights\\n\\n1. **Design System**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing values, 7 z-index, 3 font families available as Tailwind utilities\\n2. **Dark Theme**: Status colors visually distinct (amber, orange, blue, yellow, emerald, red, gray)\\n3. **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven without page refresh\\n4. **Mobile Responsive**: Sidebar → bottom nav on small screens, detail panels on large screens (≥1024px)\\n5. **Command Palette**: Global search (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K) with results grouped by type\\n6. **WebSocket Resilience**: Exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s), sequence deduplication\\n7. **Agent Work Visibility**: Active Fleet row with elapsed time, pulse indicator, live output streaming\\n\\n---\\n\\n### File Locations\\n\\n- **Plan Record**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml` (lines 7613-8133)\\n- **App CSS (Design Tokens)**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n- **Layout**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/routes/+layout.svelte`\\n- **Tailwind Config**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/tailwind.config.js`\\n- **Components**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`\\n- **UI Primitives**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ui/`\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a complete redesign roadmap with clear feature boundaries, specific acceptance criteria, daemon API requirements, and implementation guidance for modernizing the kspec web UI with a cohesive design system and improved user experience.\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"agentId: a7bcb35 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\\n<usage>total_tokens: 59766\\ntool_uses: 21\\nduration_ms: 74652</usage>\"}],\"content\":[{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Excellent! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report of the UI revamp plan.\\n\\n## UI Revamp Plan - Complete Architectural Context\\n\\nI've thoroughly reviewed the UI/UX revamp plan for the kynetic-spec project. Here's the complete architectural context:\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nThe UI revamp plan (plan ID: `01KJXSVF2YKCXMJGC55G1CPBV2`) defines a comprehensive redesign of the web UI across 10 major feature areas, with supporting design system and component architecture.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Design System Architecture\\n\\n**File:** `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n\\n**Token Structure:**\\n- **Color System**: OKLCH color space for perceptual uniformity\\n- **16 Design Tokens** (oklch format with lightness/chroma/hue):\\n  - Background, Foreground, Card, Card-foreground\\n  - Popover, Popover-foreground\\n  - Primary, Primary-foreground\\n  - Secondary, Secondary-foreground\\n  - Muted, Muted-foreground\\n  - Accent, Accent-foreground\\n  - Destructive\\n  - Border, Input, Ring\\n\\n- **5 Chart Colors** (for data visualization)\\n- **8 Sidebar-specific Tokens** (theme variants for navigation)\\n\\n**Dark Theme Support:**\\nThe tokens automatically swap when the `.dark` class is applied, providing full dark mode support with oklch values optimized for contrast and readability.\\n\\n**Current Status:**\\n- Tailwind @theme inline extensions already mapped (lines 76-112 in app.css)\\n- Variables system uses CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- Base layer styling established (border-border, outline-ring/50, bg-background, text-foreground)\\n\\n**Spacing:** CSS variables calculated as `--radius: 0.625rem` with 4 radius tokens:\\n- `--radius-sm` (0.625rem - 4px)\\n- `--radius-md` (0.625rem - 2px)\\n- `--radius-lg` (0.625rem)\\n- `--radius-xl` (0.625rem + 4px)\\n\\n**Status Color Mappings** (from spec):\\n- `pending` = amber\\n- `in_progress` = orange\\n- `pending_review` = blue\\n- `needs_work` = yellow\\n- `completed` = emerald\\n- `blocked` = red\\n- `cancelled` = gray\\n\\n**Animations:**\\n- Shimmer animation for skeleton loaders (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n- Breathing/pulse animation for active agent task cards (gated behind `prefers-reduced-motion`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Component Architecture\\n\\n**Current Component Structure** (`/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`):\\n\\n**Layout Components:**\\n- `Sidebar.svelte` - Collapsible navigation sidebar with grouped sections\\n- `MobileNav.svelte` - Bottom navigation for mobile (< 768px)\\n- `CommandPalette.svelte` - Global command/search palette (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K)\\n- `ConnectionStatus.svelte` - WebSocket connection indicator\\n\\n**Feature Components:**\\n- `ItemDetail.svelte` - Spec item detail viewer\\n- `ItemTree.svelte` - Hierarchical spec item tree\\n- `TaskList.svelte` - Task list with filtering\\n- `TaskDetail.svelte` - Task detail view (legacy)\\n- `TaskDetailPanel.svelte` - Task detail slide-over panel\\n- `TaskFilters.svelte` - Filter controls for task list\\n- `ProjectSelector.svelte` - Multi-project selector (for multi-directory daemon mode)\\n\\n**UI Primitives** (`/lib/components/ui/`):\\n- Shadcn-svelte components: Accordion, Badge, Button, Card, Dialog, Dropdown-menu, Input, Label, Popover, Select, Sheet, Sidebar, Table, Tabs, Toast, Tooltip, etc.\\n\\n**Banner Components:**\\n- `ReadOnlyBanner.svelte` - Static mode indicator with \\\"data freshness\\\" timestamp\\n\\n---\\n\\n### App Shell and Navigation\\n\\n**Current Implementation:**\\n- Main layout file: `+layout.svelte` (SvelteKit root layout)\\n- Uses `SidebarProvider` and `SidebarInset` from shadcn-svelte\\n- Desktop sidebar hidden on mobile (`hidden md:block`)\\n- Responsive inset with main content area (`flex-1 overflow-auto`)\\n\\n**Sidebar Grouping** (planned):\\n```\\nWork\\n  - Dashboard\\n  - Tasks\\n  - Agents\\n  - Sessions\\n\\nSpecs\\n  - Specs\\n  - Plans\\n  - Validate\\n\\nCapture\\n  - Inbox\\n  - Observations\\n  - Triage\\n\\nConfig\\n  - Workflows\\n  - Settings\\n```\\n\\n**Badge Counts:**\\n- Inbox items count\\n- Unresolved observations count\\n- Pending review task count\\n\\n**Current Routes:**\\n- `/` - Dashboard\\n- `/items` - Specs (should redirect `/items` → `/specs`)\\n- `/tasks` - Task list\\n- `/inbox` - Inbox\\n- `/observations` - Observations\\n- `/triage` - Triage view\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Feature Specifications (10 Areas)\\n\\n#### 1. **UI Design System** (`@ui-design-system`)\\n- Port imgen's design token architecture into Tailwind\\n- Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, animation keyframes\\n- **AC Focus**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, 3 font families as Tailwind utilities\\n- Dark theme with status colors\\n- Loading shimmer animations\\n- Agent task card breathing/pulse animations\\n\\n#### 2. **App Shell and Navigation** (`@ui-app-shell`)\\n- Restructure +layout.svelte with grouped sidebar navigation\\n- Migrate Sidebar.svelte to grouped sections\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate 3 existing task detail implementations\\n\\n#### 3. **Task Board (Kanban)** (`@ui-task-board`)\\n- Kanban-style columns mapping to task states:\\n  - **Backlog**: pending (manual_only/unassessed)\\n  - **Ready**: pending (eligible)\\n  - **In Progress**: in_progress, needs_work\\n  - **Review**: pending_review\\n  - **Done**: completed (recent)\\n  - **Blocked/Cancelled**: sections/indicators\\n\\n- **Task Card Elements**: Priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (monospace), spec ref link, metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)\\n- **Detail Modal**: Full task info with title, description, status, priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos, automation status, VCS info, plan ref, session link\\n- **Active Fleet Row**: Shows currently running agent tasks with title, agent name, elapsed time (with pulse indicator), last few lines of output\\n- **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven board updates via `tasks:updates` topic\\n- **Mutations**: Task action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note) execute via API\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisite**: \\n- Daemon must return `type` and `automation` fields in task list API response\\n- Build components: KanbanBoard, KanbanColumn, TaskCard, TaskDetailModal, ActiveFleetRow\\n\\n#### 4. **Session Stream View** (`@ui-session-stream`)\\n- View for watching agent work (historical and live)\\n- Renders structured session events from `events.jsonl`\\n- **Two-tier rendering**:\\n  - Structured events from `events.jsonl` (history)\\n  - `agent_text_chunk` WebSocket events (live text)\\n  \\n- **Event Types**: Agent messages (markdown), tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), thinking blocks (collapsed by default)\\n- **Live Streaming**: Real-time text via WebSocket with periodic structured refresh\\n- **Auto-scroll**: Follow new content, pause when user scrolls up (>100px from bottom), resume when scrolled back, \\\"jump to bottom\\\" button when paused\\n- **Session Context Panel**: Session metadata, spec context with AC checklist, files changed, budget info\\n\\n**Daemon Prerequisites**:\\n- Build GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events` endpoints\\n- Build components: SessionStream, ChatMessage, ToolCallView, ThinkingBlock\\n\\n#### 5. **Agent and Dispatch View** (`@ui-agent-dispatch`)\\n- Shows agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped)\\n- Active invocations with links to session streams\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/agent/dispatch/status` and GET `/api/agent/status` endpoints\\n- Subscribe to `agents` WebSocket topic for real-time updates\\n- Components: AgentList, DispatchStatus, InvocationCard\\n\\n#### 6. **Session History** (`@ui-session-history`)\\n- List view of past agent sessions\\n- Display: ID, agent type, task ref, status, duration, age (sorted by most recent first)\\n- Filtering support\\n- Navigate to session detail (session stream view)\\n- Depends on GET `/api/sessions` endpoint from ui-session-stream work\\n\\n#### 7. **Enhanced Inbox View** (`@ui-inbox-enhanced`)\\n- Triage status inline (untriaged/triaged/acted_on)\\n- Quick triage action links\\n- Filter controls (status, tags, age)\\n- Keep existing add/delete functionality\\n\\n#### 8. **Plans View** (`@ui-plans-view`)\\n- Browse plan records with progress tracking\\n- Display: Title, status, creation date, linked spec/task counts, progress (based on task completion)\\n- **Daemon Prerequisite**: Build GET `/api/plans` endpoint (wrap existing loadAllPlans)\\n\\n#### 9. **Validation and Alignment View** (`@ui-validation-view`)\\n- Validation results, alignment statistics, issues\\n- Summary: Error count, warning count, valid item count\\n- Alignment section: Spec coverage %, AC coverage %, orphaned tasks/specs counts\\n- Issues list grouped by severity\\n- Uses existing GET `/api/validate` and GET `/api/alignment` endpoints\\n\\n#### 10. **Dashboard Overview** (`@ui-dashboard-overview`)\\n- Home view: \\\"What's happening right now?\\\"\\n- **Active work section**: Currently running agent tasks\\n- **Status summary**: Clickable count cards per status\\n- **Needs-attention section**: Aggregates:\\n  - Untriaged inbox items\\n  - Unresolved observations\\n  - Validation warnings\\n  - Blocked tasks\\n- Build last (reuses ActiveFleetRow from task board)\\n- No aggregated activity API needed; merge recent data client-side\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\n**Design System:**\\n- Set up isolated clone first\\n- Port imgen's full `token-contract.css` into Tailwind @theme inline in app.css\\n- Start with token bridge pilot on dashboard page to validate approach\\n- Create modular CSS files: `tokens.css`, `animations.css`, `typography.css` in `lib/ds/`\\n- Establish loading skeleton and error boundary patterns\\n\\n**App Shell:**\\n- Restructure `+layout.svelte` with new sidebar component\\n- Migrate existing Sidebar.svelte to grouped navigation\\n- Add `/items` → `/specs` redirect\\n- Fix Observations nav visibility bug\\n- Migrate taskDetailStore from Svelte 4 to Svelte 5 runes\\n- Consolidate three existing task detail implementations\\n- Ensure all existing routes continue working\\n\\n**Daemon API Changes Required:**\\n- Task list API: Add `type` and `automation` fields to response\\n- Task mutations: Build POST endpoints for `/api/tasks/:ref/start`, `/api/tasks/:ref/submit`, `/api/tasks/:ref/complete`, `/api/tasks/:ref/block`\\n- Sessions: Add GET `/api/sessions` and GET `/api/sessions/:id/events`\\n- Plans: Add GET `/api/plans` endpoint\\n\\n**WebSocket Topics:**\\n- `tasks:updates` - Task state changes\\n- `agents` - Agent dispatch status and text chunks\\n- `files:updates` - File change notifications\\n\\n**Dependencies Between Features:**\\n```\\nui-design-system (foundation)\\n├── ui-app-shell\\n├── ui-task-board\\n├── ui-dashboard-overview\\n└── ui-session-stream\\n    ├── ui-session-history\\n    └── ui-agent-dispatch\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Technology Stack\\n\\n- **Framework**: SvelteKit (Svelte 5 with runes)\\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 with @theme inline\\n- **UI Components**: shadcn-svelte\\n- **Color Space**: OKLCH (perceptual)\\n- **Real-time**: WebSocket (topic-based pub/sub)\\n- **State Management**: Svelte runes (reactive)\\n- **Animation**: CSS keyframes with `prefers-reduced-motion` gates\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Acceptance Criteria Highlights\\n\\n1. **Design System**: 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing values, 7 z-index, 3 font families available as Tailwind utilities\\n2. **Dark Theme**: Status colors visually distinct (amber, orange, blue, yellow, emerald, red, gray)\\n3. **Real-time Updates**: WebSocket-driven without page refresh\\n4. **Mobile Responsive**: Sidebar → bottom nav on small screens, detail panels on large screens (≥1024px)\\n5. **Command Palette**: Global search (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K) with results grouped by type\\n6. **WebSocket Resilience**: Exponential backoff reconnection (1s, 2s, 4s... max 30s), sequence deduplication\\n7. **Agent Work Visibility**: Active Fleet row with elapsed time, pulse indicator, live output streaming\\n\\n---\\n\\n### File Locations\\n\\n- **Plan Record**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.plans.yaml` (lines 7613-8133)\\n- **App CSS (Design Tokens)**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/app.css`\\n- **Layout**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/routes/+layout.svelte`\\n- **Tailwind Config**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/tailwind.config.js`\\n- **Components**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/`\\n- **UI Primitives**: `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/ui/`\\n\\n---\\n\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a complete redesign roadmap with clear feature boundaries, specific acceptance criteria, daemon API requirements, and implementation guidance for modernizing the kspec web UI with a cohesive design system and improved user experience.\"}},{\"type\":\"content\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"agentId: a7bcb35 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\\n<usage>total_tokens: 59766\\ntool_uses: 21\\nduration_ms: 74652</usage>\"}}]}}\n","status":"failed"}}